   "slug": "commands",
   "title": "Command reference",
   "summary": "Useful player commands and where to learn more.",
-  "body": "<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Level-scaled AA — live testing:</strong> Earn two AA per level while leveling. From level 1, use the AA +/− buttons to choose 0–100%; 100% pauses leveling so you can grind AA where you prefer. Close EverQuest and update through launcher Play for game 2026102301. Existing points, purchases and partial progress stay intact. <a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">AA progression and examples</a>.</p>\n<table><caption>Player commands</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Command</th><th scope=\"col\">What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\"><code>#classes</code></th><td>Show Primary, Second and Third classes. <a href=\"multiclass.html\">Class guide</a>.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\"><code>#aaexp</code></th><td>Check your AA percentage. The native AA +/− buttons work from level 1.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\"><code>#aaexp off</code></th><td>Set 0% AA: full leveling experience plus two AA per level from eligible rewards.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\"><code>#aaexp on</code></th><td>Set 100% AA: pause leveling and earn 20 AA per current-level equivalent of eligible experience.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\"><code>#aaexp 0–100</code></th><td>Set an AA percentage directly, for example <code>#aaexp 50</code>. Partial allocations split progression; <code>on</code>/<code>off</code> are aliases for 100/0.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\"><code>/advloot</code></th><td>Open the <a href=\"advanced-loot.html\">custom loot window</a>.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\"><code>/pet</code> orders</th><td>Command the selected pet or All pets. Check the Commands line in <a href=\"pets.html\">Pet Info</a>.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\"><code>#instances</code></th><td>Show open private dungeon runs and timers. <a href=\"travel.html#instances\">Instance guide</a>.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\"><code>#zoneforge</code></th><td>Upgrade matching zone rewards: three Base copies, or four Polished/Exalted copies. <a href=\"zone-hunt.html#forging\">Forging guide</a>.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\"><code>#sellall</code></th><td>Immediately sell eligible carried items. <strong>Bank valuables first.</strong> <a href=\"equipment.html#selling\">Selling rules</a>.</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id=\"recall\">Recall is an ability</h2><p>Make a hotkey for Ancient Attunement in the General abilities tab. It returns you to the tunnel with a five-second cast and ten-minute reuse while preserving your bind point.</p>\n<h2 id=\"highkeep-dialogue\">High Keep rescue dialogue</h2><p>Hail the Gate Sergeant to begin the entrance confrontation. After defeating the four bosses, hail Osargen and choose Lead the way. An enrolled player may take over the escort by hailing him and choosing Lead the way. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#highkeep-rescue\">Full instructions</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"player-bazaar\">Player bazaar — live testing</h2><p>In public East Commonlands, use <code>#bazaar post &lt;price-pp&gt;</code>, <code>#bazaar confirm &lt;nonce&gt;</code>, <code>#bazaar listings</code>, <code>#bazaar cancel &lt;id&gt;</code> and <code>#bazaar collect</code>. Native <code>/bazaar</code> searches the Commonlands market. Native search and buying still need player verification; see <a href=\"tunnel.html#player-bazaar\">posting, buying and item restrictions</a>.</p>\n<p>The Bazaar window’s <a href=\"tunnel.html#bazaar-seller-panel\">Sell / My Listings panel</a> provides buttons for posting, cancellation and collection after updating through the launcher. The commands above remain available. Both are in live testing.</p>\n<h2 id=\"faction-standings\">Faction standings — live testing</h2><p>The <code>#factions</code> command opens your faction standings in a scrollable window with white text, standing names, numerical totals and bars. Use <code>#factions qeynos</code> to search names, <code>#factions 2 qeynos</code> for the next page, or <code>#factions target</code> for your standing with the targeted NPC's faction. Six factions appear per page; reopen the window to refresh.</p><p>Totals include earned faction, base standing, starting class, current faction race, deity, spell and item modifiers. Bars cover that faction's attainable minimum-to-maximum range, not progress toward the next standing tier. Factions with no earned changes still show their base standing. NPC reactions can differ because of invisibility, feign death, combat, merchant rules or special scripts. This view does not change faction and does not grant GM reset controls.</p>\n<h2 id=\"power-source-training\">Power Source training — Not released</h2><p><code>#itemxp</code> is a candidate command for the current training item’s quality and progress. It is not a released player command yet. <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#power-source-training\">Power Source training preview</a>.</p>",
