   "slug": "dungeon-modes",
   "title": "Raid & Grind dungeons",
   "summary": "Choose Raid or Grind, track boss credit and claim rewards.",
-  "body": "<p>Choose <strong>Raid or Grind in 21 Classic dungeons</strong>, plus curated level-50 Chapterhouse and Kael expeditions. Hail an entrance Keeper, enroll in a run and earn your own boss-checklist rewards. Runs last up to twelve hours.</p><h2 id=\"modes\">Choose a mode</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th>Grind</th><th>Raid</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Enemies</td><td>Normal stats and respawns</td><td>35% more HP, 15% more damage; defeated enemies do not return</td></tr><tr><td>Bosses</td><td>Required bosses available initially</td><td>Final boss unlocks after all required minibosses</td></tr><tr><td>Personal reward</td><td>One Normal item</td><td>One item: 90% Polished, 10% Ascended</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2 id=\"credit\">Earn your own checklist</h2><p>The creator chooses the mode. Hail the entrance Keeper for Raid, Grind, Enter, Join, Status, Claim Rewards and Reset. Open Tasks and select your dungeon and mode for its checklist and deadline. Keeper Status lists every required boss, your personal credit and permanent completion counts. A yellow Task Stage Completed message marks one boss objective. A full dungeon clear requires personal credit for every required boss. New High Keep rescue Raids also require surviving the extraction with Osargen; see <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#highkeep-rescue\">the rescue instructions</a>. During live testing, if the task objectives are blank or Completed history is missing, use Keeper Status; these display problems do not erase earned credit or rewards. Stay enrolled, connected and within 200 units of your party’s encounter, including vertical distance. Owned-pet kills count for the owner’s party. Missed kills never receive retroactive credit. Grind respawns offer another opportunity; Raid deaths are permanent for that run.</p>\n<details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"required-bosses\"><summary>Required bosses</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Each name below is required for personal completion in either mode. The final boss is marked; Raid unlocks it after the required minibosses. A group’s unlock does not give missed personal credit.</p><h3>Befallen</h3><ul><li>skeleton Lrodd</li><li>Priest Amiaz</li><li>the thaumaturgist</li><li>Boondin Babbinsbort</li><li>Gynok Moltor — final boss</li></ul><h3>Unrest</h3><ul><li>lesser blade fiend</li><li>a reanimated hand</li><li>reclusive ghoul magus</li><li>an undead barkeep</li><li>an undead knight of Unrest</li><li>a priest of najena</li><li>Garanel Rucksif — final boss</li></ul><h3>High Keep</h3><ul><li>Captain Bosec</li><li>Captain Boshinko</li><li>Dyrna Nlith</li><li>Carson McCabe — final boss</li></ul><h3>Najena</h3><ul><li>Moosh</li><li>Ekeros</li><li>BoneCracker</li><li>Rathyl</li><li>Trazdon</li><li>Drelzna</li><li>the guard captain</li><li>The Widowmistress</li><li>Najena — final boss</li></ul><h3>Cazic-Thule</h3><ul><li>Radiant</li><li>Tae Ew Diviner</li><li>Tae Ew Templar</li><li>Tae Ew Archon</li><li>Cazic Cenobite</li><li>Avatar of Fear — final boss</li></ul><h3>Permafrost</h3><ul><li>a goblin jailmaster</li><li>a goblin preacher</li><li>a goblin scryer</li><li>the goblin sage</li><li>an elite honor guard</li><li>High Priest Zaharn</li><li>King Thex`Ka IV</li><li>Lady Vox — final boss</li></ul><h3>Nagafen’s Lair</h3><ul><li>guano harvester</li><li>kobold noble</li><li>kobold champion</li><li>kobold priest</li><li>Solusek kobold king</li><li>death beetle</li><li>noxious spider</li><li>stone spider</li><li>Efreeti Lord Djarn</li><li>Magus Rokyl</li><li>King Tranix</li><li>Warlord Skarlon</li><li>Lord Nagafen — final boss</li></ul>\n</div></details><details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"added-keepers\"><summary>Additional entrance Keepers</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Use <code>/target Instance_Keeper</code> and hail if its eye model is difficult to select. Locations use in-game <code>/loc</code> order. Hate’s public Keeper is in East Commonlands; its private instances retain the entrance Keeper. Each Keeper has Raid, Grind, Enter, Join, Status, Claim Rewards and Reset.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Dungeon</th><th>Keeper /loc</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blackburrow</td><td><code>-159,23,2.0</code></td></tr><tr><td>Crushbone</td><td><code>-644,174,2.0</code></td></tr><tr><td>Runnyeye</td><td><code>106,201,3.0</code></td></tr><tr><td>Solusek&#x27;s Eye</td><td><code>-487.312,-474.688,71.969</code></td></tr><tr><td>Upper Guk</td><td><code>-36,23,2.0</code></td></tr><tr><td>Lower Guk</td><td><code>1197,-201,-81.969</code></td></tr><tr><td>Mistmoore</td><td><code>-314,120,-179.938</code></td></tr><tr><td>Kedge Keep</td><td><code>100,30,301.875</code></td></tr><tr><td>Splitpaw</td><td><code>-106,63,2.0</code></td></tr><tr><td>The Hole</td><td><code>624,-1050,-78.969</code></td></tr><tr><td>Qeynos Catacombs</td><td><code>860,96,-39.969</code></td></tr><tr><td>Plane of Fear</td><td><code>-1139,1298,-0.371</code></td></tr><tr><td>Plane of Hate (East Commonlands)</td><td><code>-1570,-346,3</code>; new-layout Keeper: <code>656,-409,2</code>; original-run Keeper: <code>-374.8,-337.08,2</code></td></tr><tr><td>Plane of Sky</td><td><code>1415,630,-666.709</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"added-objectives\"><summary>Required bosses in the added dungeons</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Every listed boss requires personal credit. Raid unlocks the final boss after all required minibosses; Keeper Status is the live checklist.</p><h3>Blackburrow</h3><ul><li>a gnoll commander</li><li>Splitpaw Commander</li><li>the gnoll high shaman</li><li>Lord Elgnub — final boss</li></ul><h3>Crushbone</h3><ul><li>orc taskmaster</li><li>orc warlord</li><li>Lord Darish</li><li>The Prophet</li><li>Ambassador DVinn</li><li>Emperor Crush — final boss</li></ul><h3>Runnyeye</h3><ul><li>The Sporali Moldmaster</li><li>Sludge Dankmire</li><li>Battlelord Paluk</li><li>Battlewizard Unak</li><li>Lord Pickclaw — final boss</li></ul><h3>Solusek&#x27;s Eye</h3><ul><li>flame goblin foreman</li><li>reckless efreeti</li><li>Singe</li><li>Kindle</li><li>inferno goblin captain</li><li>goblin high shaman</li><li>Lord Gimblox</li><li>Solusek goblin king — final boss</li></ul><h3>Upper Guk</h3><ul><li>a froglok gaz squire</li><li>a giant heart spider</li><li>a froglok scryer</li><li>a froglok realist</li><li>the froglok warden</li><li>a froglok summoner</li><li>the froglok shin lord — final boss</li></ul><h3>Lower Guk</h3><ul><li>a minotaur elder</li><li>a minotaur patriarch</li><li>a ghoul supplier</li><li>a ghoul executioner</li><li>a ghoul assassin</li><li>a ghoul sage</li><li>a ghoul cavalier</li><li>a frenzied ghoul</li><li>the ghoul arch magus</li><li>the froglok king</li><li>the ghoul lord — final boss</li></ul><h3>Mistmoore</h3><ul><li>a glyphed ghoul</li><li>an avenging caitiff</li><li>a cloaked dhampyre</li><li>Butler Syncall</li><li>Maid Issis</li><li>Mynthi Davissi</li><li>Lasna Cheroon</li><li>Garton Viswin</li><li>Xicotl — final boss</li></ul><h3>Kedge Keep</h3><ul><li>a frenzied cauldron shark</li><li>a fierce impaler</li><li>Coralyn Kelpmaiden</li><li>Shellara Ebbhunter</li><li>a seahorse matriarch</li><li>a seahorse patriarch</li><li>Cauldronboil</li><li>Undertow</li><li>Priestess Auraia</li><li>Phinigel Autropos — final boss</li></ul><h3>Splitpaw</h3><ul><li>Verishe Mal Judge</li><li>Verishe Mal Executioner</li><li>Tesch Val Kadvem</li><li>Nisch Val Torash Mashk</li><li>Rosch Val L`Vlor</li><li>Tesch Val Deval`Nmak</li><li>The Ishva Mal — final boss</li></ul><h3>The Hole</h3><ul><li>Stonesoul the Unmoving</li><li>Ikurenm the Sly</li><li>Tzitzi the Crazed</li><li>Commander Yarik</li><li>Irslak the Wretched — final boss</li></ul><h3>Qeynos Catacombs</h3><ul><li>a gelatinous cube</li><li>a thug leader</li><li>a ring leader</li><li>a shark</li><li>Omorb — final boss</li></ul><h3>Plane of Fear</h3><ul><li>Dread</li><li>Terror</li><li>Fright</li><li>a dracoliche</li><li>Cazic Thule — final boss</li></ul><h3>Plane of Hate</h3><ul><li>Magi P`Tasa</li><li>Hand of the Maestro</li><li>Maestro of Rancor</li><li>Innoruuk — final boss</li></ul><h3>Plane of Sky</h3><ul><li>a thunder spirit princess</li><li>Protector of Sky</li><li>Gorgalosk</li><li>Keeper of Souls</li><li>The Spiroc Guardian</li><li>The Spiroc Lord</li><li>Bazzt Zzzt</li><li>Sister of the Spire</li><li>Eye of Veeshan — final boss</li></ul></div></details><details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"unique-rewards\"><summary>Exclusive Raid rewards</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Every Classic dungeon has three exclusive Raid designs. The 14 added dungeons contribute 42 designs in two qualities; all 414 Classic dungeon reward definitions are MAGIC. Fear, Hate and Sky include planar relics and equipped utility clicks.</p><p>New recommended levels follow each dungeon’s equipment band. Planar items require level 46. All remain permanent, tradeable, non-LORE, zero-resale and outside existing forging recipes. The original seven exclusive families remain, with MAGIC added where needed. Already earned rewards and generated loot keep their identities.</p><p>New numeric power stays within the existing band, slot and quality budgets. Their lore is original Nightcap fiction inspired by each dungeon. Each family has Polished and Ascended versions.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Dungeon / band</th><th>Exclusive designs</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>blackburrow / 20</td><td>Elgnub&#x27;s Burrowfang<br>Blackburrow Packwarden Mantle<br>Brewer&#x27;s Amber Seal</td></tr><tr><td>crushbone / 20</td><td>Crush&#x27;s Broken Scepter<br>Ambassador&#x27;s Ashen Veil<br>Liberator of the Pens</td></tr><tr><td>runnyeye / 30</td><td>Pickclaw Tunnelbreaker<br>Evil Eye Witness<br>Crown of the Pickclaw Court</td></tr><tr><td>soldunga / 40</td><td>Goblin King&#x27;s Cinderstaff<br>Firebloom Forgegrips<br>Embervault Reliquary</td></tr><tr><td>guktop / 30</td><td>Shinlord&#x27;s Oathblade<br>Heart of the Living Guk<br>Reedwoven Watcher Boots</td></tr><tr><td>gukbottom / 50</td><td>Ghoul Lord&#x27;s Last Decree<br>Pall of the Silent Court<br>Seal of Released Souls</td></tr><tr><td>mistmoore / 40</td><td>Xicotl&#x27;s Midnight Talon<br>Mistmoore Bloodless Gorget<br>Echo of the Unfinished Waltz</td></tr><tr><td>kedge / 50</td><td>Phinigel&#x27;s Tidebound Trident<br>Pearl of the Drowned Chorus<br>Kedge Deepcurrent Robe</td></tr><tr><td>paw / 40</td><td>Ishva&#x27;s Splitpaw Knuckles<br>Splitpaw Spiritcord<br>Denfather Stoneguard</td></tr><tr><td>hole / 50</td><td>Wretched Stonecleaver<br>Pael Sealed Memory<br>Earthbound Oathplate</td></tr><tr><td>qcat / 20</td><td>Omorb&#x27;s Sluicefang<br>Catacomb Vigil Lantern<br>Qeynos Underway Satchel</td></tr><tr><td>fearplane / 50</td><td>Spine of the Faceless<br>Visage of Unbroken Will<br>Dreadhusk of the Last Stand</td></tr><tr><td>Plane of Hate (both layouts) / 50</td><td>Innoruuk&#x27;s Severed Covenant<br>Maestro&#x27;s Unfinished Requiem<br>Seal of the First Betrayal</td></tr><tr><td>airplane / 50</td><td>Veeshan&#x27;s Unwritten Horizon<br>Mantle of the First Brood<br>Astrolabe of the Eighth Island</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Planar relics</h3><p><strong>Fear:</strong> Visage of Unbroken Will reveals the unseen with See Invisible, beside Spine of the Faceless and Dreadhusk of the Last Stand. Its reuse is five minutes.</p><p><strong>Hate:</strong> Maestro’s Unfinished Requiem grants Invisibility; Innoruuk’s Severed Covenant and Seal of the First Betrayal recall hatred and broken elven royalty. Its reuse is ten minutes.</p><p><strong>Sky:</strong> Astrolabe of the Eighth Island grants ordinary Levitate, beside Veeshan’s Unwritten Horizon and Mantle of the First Brood. Its reuse is fifteen minutes. Levitate requires one Bat Wing and respects no-levitation zones, including Sky itself; island keys are still required.</p><p>Each click requires equipping the item at level 46 and a ten-second cast. Both qualities and duplicate copies share the same family cooldown; Ascended does not improve the utility. Cast/reuse figures are base values subject to native focus reductions. Native targeting, reagent conservation and spell restrictions remain.</p></div></details><h2 id=\"rewards\">Shared rewards and exclusive drops</h2><p>Twenty-four shared designs include eight armor pieces, eight weapon families, six accessories and two weight-reduction bags. Every dungeon uses these designs at its equipment band. Original dungeons: Befallen 20; Unrest/Najena 30; High Keep/Cazic-Thule 40; Permafrost/Nagafen’s Lair 50. Selection does not filter by class. Rewards are permanent, tradeable, non-lore and have zero merchant resale. Dungeon rewards cannot be converted by existing forging recipes.</p><p>Raid final bosses also drop one, two or three distinct exclusive designs with 80%, 18% and 2% chances. Each independently rolls Polished or Ascended at 90%/10%. Examples include Moltor’s Graveblade, Rucksif’s Mourning Mantle, McCabe’s Hidden Treasury, Vox’s Hoarfrost Satchel and Nagafen’s Emberfang. These shared corpse drops use normal loot controls and are additional to native loot and personal completion rewards.</p><p>Weapon delay stays fixed between qualities. Bags have six, eight or ten slots and up to 100% weight reduction. Rewards are selected durably; reconnecting cannot change them. There is one personal completion reward per character per run. A full inventory leaves an earned claim at the Keeper.</p>\n<h2 id=\"recovery\">Keep progress through interruptions</h2><p>Progress and the original deadline survive reconnects and restarts. Abandoning the task removes its display, not earned credit. Only the creator can confirm a reset, and no player, pending entry or recoverable player corpse may remain inside. Earned claims survive reset and expiry. Classic Cazic-Thule encounters are restored in both the public zone and managed private instances. Public encounters use ordinary random spawn choices; Raid objectives, final-boss unlocking and completion rewards belong only to private runs. Public High Keep, Grind and older Raid runs keep their prior faction behavior; newly enrolled rescue Raids use a temporary run alarm without permanent faction loss.</p>\n<h2 id=\"testing\">Testing still required</h2><p>All 21 Classic dungeons and both curated expeditions need in-game checks in both modes. Cazic-Thule paths and doors, inventory/loot recovery and demanding solo/small-group balance remain open. Lady Vox and Lord Nagafen explicitly require level-50 gameplay acceptance. The equipment index covers the separate zone-hunt catalog; dungeon rewards use the designs and bands described here. Existing forging recipes do not upgrade these rewards.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"chapterhouse-candidate\">The Vigil of the Dawn — live testing</h2><p>Chapterhouse adds a level-50 Raid/Grind expedition with four named enemies and a separate personal Paladin story journal. Chapterhouse contributes six exclusive final Raid variants alongside the shared dungeon completion rewards. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> and <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a>.</p>\n<details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"classic-candidate\"><summary>Classic dungeon coverage and planar rules</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>The 21 combat dungeons include Fear, Hate and Sky, with current native populations. Managed Sky has durable key exchangers that still require the normal tokens; its four previously scripted Grind bosses have eight-hour timers and the princess keeps four hours. Public and legacy Sky retain their original behavior. Plane runs isolate quest state from public zones and other runs.</p><p>Hate’s public Keeper is in East Commonlands at <code>/loc -1570,-346,3</code>, between Mirielle and Khalure; its private instances keep an entrance Keeper. Hate entry requires level 46.</p><p>For the keyless Paineel passage, see <a href=\"travel.html#hole-entrance\">Entering The Hole</a>.</p><details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"original-keepers\"><summary>Original dungeon Keeper locations</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Locations use in-game /loc order. Use <code>/target Instance_Keeper</code> and hail if needed.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Dungeon</th><th>Keeper /loc</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Befallen</td><td><code>-67,35,3.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Unrest</td><td><code>-38,67,3.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Najena</td><td><code>-61,858,4.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Permafrost</td><td><code>-121,46,2.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Nagafen’s Lair</td><td><code>-424,-248,-108</code></td></tr><tr><td>High Keep (unchanged)</td><td><code>-16,88,4</code></td></tr><tr><td>Cazic-Thule (unchanged)</td><td><code>71,-74,4</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div></details></div></details><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"hole-entrance\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#dungeon-modes--hole-entrance\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"hate-commonlands-candidate\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#dungeon-modes--hate-commonlands-candidate\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><h2 id=\"ashen-compact\">The Ashen Compact — live testing</h2><p><a href=\"ashen-compact.html\">The Ashen Compact</a> is an installed level-50 Shadow Knight helmet campaign in a curated Kael expedition. Its paired server and client release is available for testing; full encounter, rendering and balance acceptance remain open.</p><p>Four bosses, personal credit and Raid/Grind journals follow the existing expedition system. The separate story has fourteen objectives and durable progress. Temporary war souls give no loot or XP.</p>\n<h2 id=\"highkeep-rescue\">High Keep: rescue Osargen</h2>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing.</strong> The prison break is installed; escort pathing and full encounter acceptance remain open. It applies only to new Raid runs after this release. Existing runs, Grind and public High Keep keep their current rules.</p>\n<ol><li><strong>Bluff your way in.</strong> Hail the Gate Sergeant just inside the entrance. Claim to be the relief detail, then insist on seeing Osargen. His suspicion turns into an alarm, and the keep's guards become hostile to everyone in your run. Attacking a guard also raises the alarm.</li><li><strong>Break the prison's command.</strong> Fight Boshinko on the entrance approach, Bosec at the prison stairs, Dyrna in the prison and McCabe by the cell-block approach. Follow the zone shouts and journal guidance; the route no longer sends you upstairs. Existing boss loot stays.</li><li><strong>Bring Osargen out alive.</strong> Hail him in his cell and choose Lead the way. He follows your character. Defeat three pairs of pursuers as you return to the entrance; the first pair comes when you release him. He stops while a wave is alive. Intercept or taunt guards and target Osargen directly for heals.</li><li><strong>Finish together.</strong> Reach the entrance and clear nearby guard combat. Living nearby participants who personally earned all four boss credits receive completion and the existing one-time dungeon reward.</li></ol>\n<p>Stay close. If the guide disconnects or falls behind, Osargen waits; another enrolled player can hail him and choose Lead the way. If the current guide dies, another player can take over before the 90-second separation limit. Osargen’s death or 90 seconds without a nearby living guide resets the escort, with another attempt available after 20 seconds. Defeated bosses remain defeated. A zone restart returns an unfinished escort to his cell but preserves the alarm and boss progress. Keeper Claim Rewards remains available for earned rewards when inventory was full. There is no permanent faction penalty or extra reward from repeatedly killing pursuers.</p>\n<p>There are now 23 dungeon choices: 21 Classic dungeons, Chapterhouse and curated Kael. Kael adds six exclusive final Raid variants, bringing the combined dungeon item catalog to 426 definitions, including shared completion rewards. Its fourteen total new items include the story helmet, Cinder augment qualities and three named relics.</p>\n<h2 id=\"hate-layout-preview\">Plane of Hate layout — live testing</h2>\n<p>New Raid and Grind runs from the East Commonlands Keeper use a ground-level Plane of Hate layout. The Keeper is still at <code>/loc -1570,-346,3</code>. You must be level 46 to enter. Fully exit EverQuest and press Play in the launcher to install the paired terrain and creature models before entering.</p>\n<p>Existing unexpired runs remain in the original layout, with their enemies, corpses, timers and earned progress intact. Return to your current run through the Keeper; joining an existing group run follows its layout. Ordinary spell travel keeps its original destination. To start a new-layout run, use the Commonlands Keeper after your original run has ended.</p>\n<p>The same four bosses, NPC strength, ordinary and epic loot, Book of Souls, experience, Hunt rewards and Raid/Grind completion rewards remain. The Hunt catalog still labels that reward family <code>hateplane</code>. Enemy placement and patrol routes have changed, so pull spacing and difficulty still need player testing.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><caption>New-layout landmarks, in /loc order Y,X,Z</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Landmark</th><th scope=\"col\">/loc</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Arrival</td><td><code>656,-393,2</code></td></tr><tr><td>Instance Keeper</td><td><code>656,-409,2</code></td></tr><tr><td>Magi P’Tasa</td><td><code>365.2,-361.9,3</code></td></tr><tr><td>Hand of the Maestro</td><td><code>-43,-93,3</code></td></tr><tr><td>Maestro of Rancor</td><td><code>-386,-173,3</code></td></tr><tr><td>Innoruuk</td><td><code>-765,-451,3</code></td></tr><tr><td>Book of Souls</td><td><code>313,-673,3</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>All four bosses and the book have ground-level routes from the arrival point. RoF2 rendering, doors, actual pulls, complete runs and reconnect recovery remain open player checks.</p>\n",
+  "body": "<p>Choose <strong>Raid or Grind in 21 Classic dungeons</strong>, plus curated level-50 Chapterhouse and Kael expeditions. Hail an entrance Keeper, enroll in a run and earn your own boss-checklist rewards. Runs last up to twelve hours.</p><h2 id=\"modes\">Choose a mode</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th>Grind</th><th>Raid</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Enemies</td><td>Normal stats and respawns</td><td>35% more HP, 15% more damage; defeated enemies do not return</td></tr><tr><td>Bosses</td><td>Required bosses available initially</td><td>Final boss unlocks after all required minibosses</td></tr><tr><td>Personal reward</td><td>One Normal item</td><td>One item: 90% Polished, 10% Ascended</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2 id=\"credit\">Earn your own checklist</h2><p>The creator chooses the mode. Hail the entrance Keeper for Raid, Grind, Enter, Join, Status, Claim Rewards and Reset. Open Tasks and select your dungeon and mode for its checklist and deadline. Keeper Status lists every required boss, your personal credit and permanent completion counts. A yellow Task Stage Completed message marks one boss objective. A full dungeon clear requires personal credit for every required boss. New High Keep rescue Raids also require surviving the extraction with Osargen; see <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#highkeep-rescue\">the rescue instructions</a>. During live testing, if the task objectives are blank or Completed history is missing, use Keeper Status; these display problems do not erase earned credit or rewards. Stay enrolled, connected and within 200 units of your party’s encounter, including vertical distance. Owned-pet kills count for the owner’s party. Missed kills never receive retroactive credit. Grind respawns offer another opportunity; Raid deaths are permanent for that run.</p>\n<details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"required-bosses\"><summary>Required bosses</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Each name below is required for personal completion in either mode. The final boss is marked; Raid unlocks it after the required minibosses. A group’s unlock does not give missed personal credit.</p><h3>Befallen</h3><ul><li>skeleton Lrodd</li><li>Priest Amiaz</li><li>the thaumaturgist</li><li>Boondin Babbinsbort</li><li>Gynok Moltor — final boss</li></ul><h3>Unrest</h3><ul><li>lesser blade fiend</li><li>a reanimated hand</li><li>reclusive ghoul magus</li><li>an undead barkeep</li><li>an undead knight of Unrest</li><li>a priest of najena</li><li>Garanel Rucksif — final boss</li></ul><h3>High Keep</h3><ul><li>Captain Bosec</li><li>Captain Boshinko</li><li>Dyrna Nlith</li><li>Carson McCabe — final boss</li></ul><h3>Najena</h3><ul><li>Moosh</li><li>Ekeros</li><li>BoneCracker</li><li>Rathyl</li><li>Trazdon</li><li>Drelzna</li><li>the guard captain</li><li>The Widowmistress</li><li>Najena — final boss</li></ul><h3>Cazic-Thule</h3><ul><li>Radiant</li><li>Tae Ew Diviner</li><li>Tae Ew Templar</li><li>Tae Ew Archon</li><li>Cazic Cenobite</li><li>Avatar of Fear — final boss</li></ul><h3>Permafrost</h3><ul><li>a goblin jailmaster</li><li>a goblin preacher</li><li>a goblin scryer</li><li>the goblin sage</li><li>an elite honor guard</li><li>High Priest Zaharn</li><li>King Thex`Ka IV</li><li>Lady Vox — final boss</li></ul><h3>Nagafen’s Lair</h3><ul><li>guano harvester</li><li>kobold noble</li><li>kobold champion</li><li>kobold priest</li><li>Solusek kobold king</li><li>death beetle</li><li>noxious spider</li><li>stone spider</li><li>Efreeti Lord Djarn</li><li>Magus Rokyl</li><li>King Tranix</li><li>Warlord Skarlon</li><li>Lord Nagafen — final boss</li></ul>\n</div></details><details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"added-keepers\"><summary>Additional entrance Keepers</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Use <code>/target Instance_Keeper</code> and hail if its eye model is difficult to select. Locations use in-game <code>/loc</code> order. Hate’s public Keeper is in East Commonlands; its private instances retain the entrance Keeper. Each Keeper has Raid, Grind, Enter, Join, Status, Claim Rewards and Reset.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Dungeon</th><th>Keeper /loc</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blackburrow</td><td><code>-159,23,2.0</code></td></tr><tr><td>Crushbone</td><td><code>-644,174,2.0</code></td></tr><tr><td>Runnyeye</td><td><code>106,201,3.0</code></td></tr><tr><td>Solusek&#x27;s Eye</td><td><code>-487.312,-474.688,71.969</code></td></tr><tr><td>Upper Guk</td><td><code>-36,23,2.0</code></td></tr><tr><td>Lower Guk</td><td><code>1197,-201,-81.969</code></td></tr><tr><td>Mistmoore</td><td><code>-314,120,-179.938</code></td></tr><tr><td>Kedge Keep</td><td><code>100,30,301.875</code></td></tr><tr><td>Splitpaw</td><td><code>-106,63,2.0</code></td></tr><tr><td>The Hole</td><td><code>624,-1050,-78.969</code></td></tr><tr><td>Qeynos Catacombs</td><td><code>860,96,-39.969</code></td></tr><tr><td>Plane of Fear</td><td><code>-1139,1298,-0.371</code></td></tr><tr><td>Plane of Hate (East Commonlands)</td><td><code>-1570,-346,3</code>; new-layout Keeper: <code>656,-409,2</code>; original-run Keeper: <code>-374.8,-337.08,2</code></td></tr><tr><td>Plane of Sky</td><td><code>1415,630,-666.709</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"added-objectives\"><summary>Required bosses in the added dungeons</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Every listed boss requires personal credit. Raid unlocks the final boss after all required minibosses; Keeper Status is the live checklist.</p><h3>Blackburrow</h3><ul><li>a gnoll commander</li><li>Splitpaw Commander</li><li>the gnoll high shaman</li><li>Lord Elgnub — final boss</li></ul><h3>Crushbone</h3><ul><li>orc taskmaster</li><li>orc warlord</li><li>Lord Darish</li><li>The Prophet</li><li>Ambassador DVinn</li><li>Emperor Crush — final boss</li></ul><h3>Runnyeye</h3><ul><li>The Sporali Moldmaster</li><li>Sludge Dankmire</li><li>Battlelord Paluk</li><li>Battlewizard Unak</li><li>Lord Pickclaw — final boss</li></ul><h3>Solusek&#x27;s Eye</h3><ul><li>flame goblin foreman</li><li>reckless efreeti</li><li>Singe</li><li>Kindle</li><li>inferno goblin captain</li><li>goblin high shaman</li><li>Lord Gimblox</li><li>Solusek goblin king — final boss</li></ul><h3>Upper Guk</h3><ul><li>a froglok gaz squire</li><li>a giant heart spider</li><li>a froglok scryer</li><li>a froglok realist</li><li>the froglok warden</li><li>a froglok summoner</li><li>the froglok shin lord — final boss</li></ul><h3>Lower Guk</h3><ul><li>a minotaur elder</li><li>a minotaur patriarch</li><li>a ghoul supplier</li><li>a ghoul executioner</li><li>a ghoul assassin</li><li>a ghoul sage</li><li>a ghoul cavalier</li><li>a frenzied ghoul</li><li>the ghoul arch magus</li><li>the froglok king</li><li>the ghoul lord — final boss</li></ul><h3>Mistmoore</h3><ul><li>a glyphed ghoul</li><li>an avenging caitiff</li><li>a cloaked dhampyre</li><li>Butler Syncall</li><li>Maid Issis</li><li>Mynthi Davissi</li><li>Lasna Cheroon</li><li>Garton Viswin</li><li>Xicotl — final boss</li></ul><h3>Kedge Keep</h3><ul><li>a frenzied cauldron shark</li><li>a fierce impaler</li><li>Coralyn Kelpmaiden</li><li>Shellara Ebbhunter</li><li>a seahorse matriarch</li><li>a seahorse patriarch</li><li>Cauldronboil</li><li>Undertow</li><li>Priestess Auraia</li><li>Phinigel Autropos — final boss</li></ul><h3>Splitpaw</h3><ul><li>Verishe Mal Judge</li><li>Verishe Mal Executioner</li><li>Tesch Val Kadvem</li><li>Nisch Val Torash Mashk</li><li>Rosch Val L`Vlor</li><li>Tesch Val Deval`Nmak</li><li>The Ishva Mal — final boss</li></ul><h3>The Hole</h3><ul><li>Stonesoul the Unmoving</li><li>Ikurenm the Sly</li><li>Tzitzi the Crazed</li><li>Commander Yarik</li><li>Irslak the Wretched — final boss</li></ul><h3>Qeynos Catacombs</h3><ul><li>a gelatinous cube</li><li>a thug leader</li><li>a ring leader</li><li>a shark</li><li>Omorb — final boss</li></ul><h3>Plane of Fear</h3><ul><li>Dread</li><li>Terror</li><li>Fright</li><li>a dracoliche</li><li>Cazic Thule — final boss</li></ul><h3>Plane of Hate</h3><ul><li>Magi P`Tasa</li><li>Hand of the Maestro</li><li>Maestro of Rancor</li><li>Innoruuk — final boss</li></ul><h3>Plane of Sky</h3><ul><li>a thunder spirit princess</li><li>Protector of Sky</li><li>Gorgalosk</li><li>Keeper of Souls</li><li>The Spiroc Guardian</li><li>The Spiroc Lord</li><li>Bazzt Zzzt</li><li>Sister of the Spire</li><li>Eye of Veeshan — final boss</li></ul></div></details><details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"unique-rewards\"><summary>Exclusive Raid rewards</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Every Classic dungeon has three exclusive Raid designs. The 14 added dungeons contribute 42 designs in two qualities; all 414 Classic dungeon reward definitions are MAGIC. Fear, Hate and Sky include planar relics and equipped utility clicks.</p><p>New recommended levels follow each dungeon’s equipment band. Planar items require level 46. All remain permanent, tradeable, non-LORE, zero-resale and outside existing forging recipes. The original seven exclusive families remain, with MAGIC added where needed. Already earned rewards and generated loot keep their identities.</p><p>New numeric power stays within the existing band, slot and quality budgets. Their lore is original Nightcap fiction inspired by each dungeon. Each family has Polished and Ascended versions.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Dungeon / band</th><th>Exclusive designs</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>blackburrow / 20</td><td>Elgnub&#x27;s Burrowfang<br>Blackburrow Packwarden Mantle<br>Brewer&#x27;s Amber Seal</td></tr><tr><td>crushbone / 20</td><td>Crush&#x27;s Broken Scepter<br>Ambassador&#x27;s Ashen Veil<br>Liberator of the Pens</td></tr><tr><td>runnyeye / 30</td><td>Pickclaw Tunnelbreaker<br>Evil Eye Witness<br>Crown of the Pickclaw Court</td></tr><tr><td>soldunga / 40</td><td>Goblin King&#x27;s Cinderstaff<br>Firebloom Forgegrips<br>Embervault Reliquary</td></tr><tr><td>guktop / 30</td><td>Shinlord&#x27;s Oathblade<br>Heart of the Living Guk<br>Reedwoven Watcher Boots</td></tr><tr><td>gukbottom / 50</td><td>Ghoul Lord&#x27;s Last Decree<br>Pall of the Silent Court<br>Seal of Released Souls</td></tr><tr><td>mistmoore / 40</td><td>Xicotl&#x27;s Midnight Talon<br>Mistmoore Bloodless Gorget<br>Echo of the Unfinished Waltz</td></tr><tr><td>kedge / 50</td><td>Phinigel&#x27;s Tidebound Trident<br>Pearl of the Drowned Chorus<br>Kedge Deepcurrent Robe</td></tr><tr><td>paw / 40</td><td>Ishva&#x27;s Splitpaw Knuckles<br>Splitpaw Spiritcord<br>Denfather Stoneguard</td></tr><tr><td>hole / 50</td><td>Wretched Stonecleaver<br>Pael Sealed Memory<br>Earthbound Oathplate</td></tr><tr><td>qcat / 20</td><td>Omorb&#x27;s Sluicefang<br>Catacomb Vigil Lantern<br>Qeynos Underway Satchel</td></tr><tr><td>fearplane / 50</td><td>Spine of the Faceless<br>Visage of Unbroken Will<br>Dreadhusk of the Last Stand</td></tr><tr><td>Plane of Hate (both layouts) / 50</td><td>Innoruuk&#x27;s Severed Covenant<br>Maestro&#x27;s Unfinished Requiem<br>Seal of the First Betrayal</td></tr><tr><td>airplane / 50</td><td>Veeshan&#x27;s Unwritten Horizon<br>Mantle of the First Brood<br>Astrolabe of the Eighth Island</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Planar relics</h3><p><strong>Fear:</strong> Visage of Unbroken Will reveals the unseen with See Invisible, beside Spine of the Faceless and Dreadhusk of the Last Stand. Its reuse is five minutes.</p><p><strong>Hate:</strong> Maestro’s Unfinished Requiem grants Invisibility; Innoruuk’s Severed Covenant and Seal of the First Betrayal recall hatred and broken elven royalty. Its reuse is ten minutes.</p><p><strong>Sky:</strong> Astrolabe of the Eighth Island grants ordinary Levitate, beside Veeshan’s Unwritten Horizon and Mantle of the First Brood. Its reuse is fifteen minutes. Levitate requires one Bat Wing and respects no-levitation zones, including Sky itself; island keys are still required.</p><p>Each click requires equipping the item at level 46 and a ten-second cast. Both qualities and duplicate copies share the same family cooldown; Ascended does not improve the utility. Cast/reuse figures are base values subject to native focus reductions. Native targeting, reagent conservation and spell restrictions remain.</p></div></details><h2 id=\"rewards\">Shared rewards and exclusive drops</h2><p>Twenty-four shared designs include eight armor pieces, eight weapon families, six accessories and two weight-reduction bags. Every dungeon uses these designs at its equipment band. Original dungeons: Befallen 20; Unrest/Najena 30; High Keep/Cazic-Thule 40; Permafrost/Nagafen’s Lair 50. Selection does not filter by class. Rewards are permanent, tradeable, non-lore and have zero merchant resale. Dungeon rewards cannot be converted by existing forging recipes.</p><p>Raid final bosses also drop one, two or three distinct exclusive designs with 80%, 18% and 2% chances. Each independently rolls Polished or Ascended at 90%/10%. Examples include Moltor’s Graveblade, Rucksif’s Mourning Mantle, McCabe’s Hidden Treasury, Vox’s Hoarfrost Satchel and Nagafen’s Emberfang. These shared corpse drops use normal loot controls and are additional to native loot and personal completion rewards.</p><p>Weapon delay stays fixed between qualities. Bags have six, eight or ten slots and up to 100% weight reduction. Rewards are selected durably; reconnecting cannot change them. There is one personal completion reward per character per run. A full inventory leaves an earned claim at the Keeper.</p>\n<h2 id=\"recovery\">Keep progress through interruptions</h2><p>Progress and the original deadline survive reconnects and restarts. Abandoning the task removes its display, not earned credit. Only the creator can confirm a reset, and no player, pending entry or recoverable player corpse may remain inside. Earned claims survive reset and expiry. Classic Cazic-Thule encounters are restored in both the public zone and managed private instances. Public encounters use ordinary random spawn choices; Raid objectives, final-boss unlocking and completion rewards belong only to private runs. Public High Keep, Grind and older Raid runs keep their prior faction behavior; newly enrolled rescue Raids use a temporary run alarm without permanent faction loss.</p>\n<h2 id=\"testing\">Testing still required</h2><p>All 21 Classic dungeons and both curated expeditions need in-game checks in both modes. Cazic-Thule paths and doors, inventory/loot recovery and demanding solo/small-group balance remain open. Lady Vox and Lord Nagafen explicitly require level-50 gameplay acceptance. The equipment index covers the separate zone-hunt catalog; dungeon rewards use the designs and bands described here. Existing forging recipes do not upgrade these rewards.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"chapterhouse-candidate\">The Vigil of the Dawn — live testing</h2><p>Chapterhouse adds a level-50 Raid/Grind expedition with four named enemies and a separate personal Paladin story journal. Chapterhouse contributes six exclusive final Raid variants alongside the shared dungeon completion rewards. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> and <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a>.</p>\n<details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"classic-candidate\"><summary>Classic dungeon coverage and planar rules</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>The 21 combat dungeons include Fear, Hate and Sky, with current native populations. Managed Sky has durable key exchangers that still require the normal tokens; its four previously scripted Grind bosses have eight-hour timers and the princess keeps four hours. Public and legacy Sky retain their original behavior. Plane runs isolate quest state from public zones and other runs.</p><p>Hate’s public Keeper is in East Commonlands at <code>/loc -1570,-346,3</code>, between Mirielle and Khalure; its private instances keep an entrance Keeper. Hate entry requires level 46.</p><p>For the keyless Paineel passage, see <a href=\"travel.html#hole-entrance\">Entering The Hole</a>.</p><details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"original-keepers\"><summary>Original dungeon Keeper locations</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Locations use in-game /loc order. Use <code>/target Instance_Keeper</code> and hail if needed.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Dungeon</th><th>Keeper /loc</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Befallen</td><td><code>-67,35,3.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Unrest</td><td><code>-38,67,3.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Najena</td><td><code>-61,858,4.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Permafrost</td><td><code>-121,46,2.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Nagafen’s Lair</td><td><code>-424,-248,-108</code></td></tr><tr><td>High Keep (unchanged)</td><td><code>-16,88,4</code></td></tr><tr><td>Cazic-Thule (unchanged)</td><td><code>71,-74,4</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div></details></div></details><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"hole-entrance\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#dungeon-modes--hole-entrance\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"hate-commonlands-candidate\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#dungeon-modes--hate-commonlands-candidate\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><h2 id=\"ashen-compact\">The Ashen Compact — live testing</h2><p><a href=\"ashen-compact.html\">The Ashen Compact</a> is an installed level-50 Shadow Knight helmet campaign in a curated Kael expedition. Its paired server and client release is available for testing; full encounter, rendering and balance acceptance remain open.</p><p>Four bosses, personal credit and Raid/Grind journals follow the existing expedition system. The separate story has fourteen objectives and durable progress. Temporary war souls give no loot or XP.</p>\n<h2 id=\"highkeep-rescue\">High Keep: rescue Osargen</h2>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing.</strong> The prison break is installed; escort pathing and full encounter acceptance remain open. It applies only to new Raid runs after this release. Existing runs, Grind and public High Keep keep their current rules.</p>\n<ol><li><strong>Bluff your way in.</strong> Hail the Gate Sergeant just inside the entrance. Claim to be the relief detail, then insist on seeing Osargen. His suspicion turns into an alarm, and the keep's guards become hostile to everyone in your run. Attacking a guard also raises the alarm.</li><li><strong>Break the prison's command.</strong> Fight Boshinko on the entrance approach, Bosec at the prison stairs, Dyrna in the prison and McCabe by the cell-block approach. Follow the zone shouts and journal guidance; the route no longer sends you upstairs. Existing boss loot stays.</li><li><strong>Bring Osargen out alive.</strong> Hail him in his cell and choose Lead the way. He follows your character. Defeat three pairs of pursuers as you return to the entrance; the first pair comes when you release him. He stops while a wave is alive. Intercept or taunt guards and target Osargen directly for heals.</li><li><strong>Finish together.</strong> Reach the entrance and clear nearby guard combat. Living nearby participants who personally earned all four boss credits receive completion and the existing one-time dungeon reward.</li></ol>\n<p>Stay close. If the guide disconnects or falls behind, Osargen waits; another enrolled player can hail him and choose Lead the way. If the current guide dies, another player can take over before the 90-second separation limit. Osargen’s death or 90 seconds without a nearby living guide resets the escort, with another attempt available after 20 seconds. Defeated bosses remain defeated. A zone restart returns an unfinished escort to his cell but preserves the alarm and boss progress. Keeper Claim Rewards remains available for earned rewards when inventory was full. There is no permanent faction penalty or extra reward from repeatedly killing pursuers.</p>\n<p>There are now 23 dungeon choices: 21 Classic dungeons, Chapterhouse and curated Kael. Kael adds six exclusive final Raid variants, bringing the combined dungeon item catalog to 426 definitions, including shared completion rewards. Its fourteen total new items include the story helmet, Cinder augment qualities and three named relics.</p>\n<h2 id=\"hate-layout-preview\">Plane of Hate layout — live testing</h2>\n<p>New Raid and Grind runs from the East Commonlands Keeper use a newer Plane of Hate layout. The Keeper is still at <code>/loc -1570,-346,3</code>. You must be level 46 to enter. Fully exit EverQuest and press Play in the launcher to install the paired terrain and creature models before entering.</p>\n<p>Existing unexpired runs remain in the original layout, with their enemies, corpses, timers and earned progress intact. Return to your current run through the Keeper; joining an existing group run follows its layout. Ordinary spell travel keeps its original destination. To start a new-layout run, use the Commonlands Keeper after your original run has ended.</p>\n<p>The same four bosses, NPC strength, ordinary and epic loot, Book of Souls, experience, Hunt rewards and Raid/Grind completion rewards remain. The Hunt catalog still labels that reward family <code>hateplane</code>. The density update adds 47 ordinary enemies to reduce empty stretches, bringing managed Hate to 222 encounter points plus its Keeper. Existing bosses, named encounters and 47 patrols are preserved. Both modes use the same boss checklist; Grind has normal respawns and all four bosses available without the Raid unlock gate. Existing kills, timers, corpses and run progress remain. The update is installed; pull difficulty, rendering and full-run player acceptance remain open.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><caption>New-layout landmarks, in /loc order Y,X,Z</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Landmark</th><th scope=\"col\">/loc</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Arrival</td><td><code>656,-393,2</code></td></tr><tr><td>Instance Keeper</td><td><code>656,-409,2</code></td></tr><tr><td>Magi P’Tasa</td><td><code>365.2,-361.9,3</code></td></tr><tr><td>Hand of the Maestro</td><td><code>-120,-185,29.75</code></td></tr><tr><td>Maestro of Rancor</td><td><code>-479,-135,32</code></td></tr><tr><td>Innoruuk</td><td><code>-1611.2688,-459.4862,69.5276</code></td></tr><tr><td>Book of Souls</td><td><code>313,-673,3</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Maestro occupies the organ room, the Hand its stock platform, and Innoruuk the southern throne area. These raised landmarks have ordinary walking routes from arrival. The placement correction preserves boss health and loot, existing kills, respawn timers, corpses and run progress; no client update or run reset is needed. RoF2 rendering, doors, actual pulls, complete runs and reconnect recovery remain open player checks.</p>\n",
