   "slug": "equipment",
   "title": "Equipment & trading",
   "summary": "Item qualities, trading, equipment access and reward systems.",
-  "body": "<p>Find ordinary equipment with the <a href=\"loot-finder.html\">Loot finder</a>, browse <a href=\"items.html\">Hunt rewards</a>, or compare an upgrade in the experimental <a href=\"build-lab.html\">Build Lab</a>.</p><h2 id=\"free-trade\">Player trading and duplicate items</h2><p>Trade formerly NO DROP and NO TRANSFER items, already-attuned gear, bags, their contents and augments. <strong>LORE restrictions are disabled</strong>, so duplicate ownership is allowed. Inventory capacity, temporary-item expiration and Pet Armor restrictions remain. Equipment eligibility still depends on your held classes and the remaining item requirements.</p>\n<h2 id=\"item-tiers\">Polished, Exalted, and Ascended loot</h2><p>Eligible dropped equipment and bags can appear in three stronger custom tiers. Their health, mana, defenses, and offensive stats scale by item family.</p>\n<p>Ordinary eligible equipment and bags now roll <strong>20% Polished, 5% Exalted and 1% Ascended</strong>, leaving 74% Normal when all variants exist. These chances apply per eligible item drop, not per kill. Already generated loot is not rerolled. Zone-hunt and dungeon rewards retain their separate rates.</p><h2 id=\"zone-hunt\">Augments in50 Classic zones; gear in the original48</h2><p>Any unowned, killable NPC in an enabled augment zone can roll its augment, including guards, named and quest NPCs, killable merchants and scripted combat adds. Player-owned/charmed pets, mercenaries, swarm pets, protected noncombat actors and restored corpses do not reroll. Native corpse ownership and encounter access still apply. Augments roll at 1.5%; approved native equipment sources keep their separate 0.5% chance and level/night restrictions. Qualities remain Base60%, Polished30%, Exalted8%, Ascension2%; no guaranteed drop or pity counter. <a href=\"zones.html\">Zone rewards</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"hunt-sockets\">Six armor locations for heroic augments</h2><p>Eligible Base and tiered head, arms, hands, chest, legs and feet armor gains one type-22 socket, preserving existing sockets. Zone augments add stats and heroic attributes; item level requirements still apply. At level 50, every two effective heroic INT from these socketed augments allows one more point of item Spell Damage, up to +30; heroic WIS does the same for Healing Amount. With the current 750 cap, either can reach 780. Extra cap room only helps when you have enough of the actual bonus.</p>\n<h2 id=\"zone-forge\">Upgrade matching rewards</h2><p><code>#zoneforge</code> uses <strong>three Base copies</strong> for one Polished reward, then <strong>four Polished</strong> for one Exalted or <strong>four Exalted</strong> for one Ascension. Artisan Veyra’s reusable Reforging Box also upgrades four identical Polished or Exalted copies, including eligible ordinary tiered gear. The box also accepts <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#normal-items\">three identical eligible Normal/Base copies for Polished</a>; higher recipes stay at four. Read <a href=\"item-upgrades.html\">Item upgrades</a> for inputs, restrictions and the two distinct top-tier names.</p>\n<details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"heroic-gear\"><summary>Heroic stats on Ascended equipment</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Ascended gear and Ascended epics add heroic stats on top of their improved base stats. This describes the existing equipment tiers; the new zone rewards have their own heroic stats at each quality.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"caster-gear\"><summary>Gear bonuses for casters and healers</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Eligible direct damage spells and procs add effective Spell Damage once. Each ordinary DoT tick adds half the effective bonus, rounded down, independent of duration. Healing Amount retains percentage healing and its existing HoT distribution. Each item-bonus total has a 750 base cap; eligible Hunt augments can raise it to 780 at level 50 when enough actual bonus is equipped. Clients also gain 0.1% per heroic INT on direct damage and per heroic WIS on direct healing; DoTs and HoTs do not gain this heroic multiplier. The separate Bard area-DoT route retains its native behavior.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"stat-cap\"><summary>More room for core stats</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>The normal core-stat cap is raised to 425, with heroic stat effects handled separately.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"summoned-gear\"><summary>Ascended summoned equipment</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Eligible summoned gear becomes Ascended when a matching version exists. The supported Paladin and Cleric summoned-hammer families have zero merchant resale value at every quality, including items you already own. Summoning does not bypass spell or item-level requirements.</p>\n</div></details><h2 id=\"bags\">More room in your bags</h2><p>Buy bags up to 40 slots, with base prices from 10 to 7,500 platinum. Merchant price adjustments and each bag’s capacity and contents restrictions still apply. Free trading does not reduce expensive bag purchase prices.</p>\n<details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"merchant-payouts\"><summary>Better payouts for ordinary loot</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Boosted merchant payouts remain in place for ordinary loot. Formerly NO DROP items use the fixed one-platinum payout below instead of those price modifiers.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"fixed-resale\"><summary>One platinum for formerly NO DROP items</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Ordinary merchants and <code>#sellall</code> pay exactly 1 platinum per physical item from the eligible formerly NO DROP pool. Five stack units pay 5 platinum; a charged object pays 1 platinum total. Purchase prices have a one-platinum floor. Merchant previews can differ from actual payment. Zone-hunt rewards, dungeon rewards and the supported divine summoned-hammer families have no merchant resale value.</p>\n</div></details><h2 id=\"selling\">Bulk selling from the command or merchant window</h2><p>Use <code>#sellall</code> to sell eligible carried items without targeting a merchant, or use the merchant window’s <strong>Sell All</strong> button. Containers, food, drink, spell reagents and casting focus items are kept. Zero-value items, including zone rewards and the supported divine summoned hammers, are skipped. <strong class=\"inline\">Sales are immediate and can include valuable gear. Bank anything you want to keep first.</strong></p>\n<h2 id=\"winged-helmet\">Winged Helm of the Dawn</h2><p>A custom Paladin helmet with an installed appearance for visual testing. <strong class=\"inline\">Earn this helmet through Camil’s Vigil of the Dawn, now in live testing.</strong></p>\n\n<h2 id=\"eligibility\">Wear gear for your whole build</h2><p>Ordinary equipment recognizes all held classes. Class-matching wearable items and augments allow all playable races; deity, level, slot, weapon and augment restrictions remain. See <a href=\"multiclass.html#equipment-access\">equipment eligibility</a>.</p><h2 id=\"dungeon-rewards\">Dungeon completion rewards</h2><p><a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Raid and Grind dungeons</a> have 24 shared reward designs and three exclusive Raid designs for each of the 21 released dungeons. Grind grants Normal; Raid grants Polished or Ascended. These permanent, tradeable, non-lore items have zero merchant resale and no existing forging recipe. Their bags have up to ten slots and 100% weight reduction.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"click-cooldowns\">Item click reuse</h2><p>Items without an explicit shared reuse group keep their own cooldowns without locking unrelated abilities. Copies of the same item share reuse; explicitly grouped items still share their group. Existing saved waits retain their expiry. See <a href=\"combat.html#ability-cooldowns\">the cooldown update</a>.</p>\n<details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"reviewed-ascended\"><summary>Reviewed Ascended values</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Supported numeric fields on 131 Ascended items now follow inspected THJ Legendary references. These families use per-item values rather than one universal multiplier. Some values are lower than before; original effects and existing sockets remain.</p><table><caption>Selected Ascended reference values</caption><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Values</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Heavy Yttrium Chestplate</td><td>150 AC; 250 HP and mana; 40 Spell Damage and Healing Amount</td></tr><tr><td>Blood Cord</td><td>70 AC; 200 HP and mana; 40 STA and 10 heroic STA; 40 Spell Damage and Healing Amount</td></tr><tr><td>Talisman of Vah Kerrath</td><td>250 HP and mana; 8 to each heroic attribute; 30 Spell Damage and Healing Amount</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"starter-bands\"><summary>Starter upgrades and dungeon progression</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Approved starter families use smaller steps: Bronze chest armor has 6, 7, 8 and 9 AC across Normal, Polished, Exalted and Ascended. Bronze Long Sword has 4, 5, 6 and 7 damage at fixed delay 32. Cultural armor is excluded from this retuning. Comparable Normal dungeon rewards remain stronger.</p></div></details><details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"earned-procs\"><summary>Earned melee and pet equipment</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Selected items gain sympathetic healing, combat procs or received-healing support. Healing, Runic and Hastened Fragments of Truth and Bloodfrenzy Core have earned boss routes; later-era bosses still require their normal access. Bloodfrenzy Core is a power-source item, while the original Bloodfrenzy remains a weapon. New sockets do not bypass augment compatibility.</p>\n</div></details><h2 id=\"class-armor-candidate\">Ascended class-armor quest rewards</h2><p>Crafted, Lambent, Darkforge, Ivy Etched and Totemic quests now grant existing Ascended versions of their 37 reviewed armor rewards. Substantial class-armor quests qualify even when repeatable; cheap/basic hand-ins stay excluded. Materials and quest requirements remain. Already-owned armor is not automatically converted. <a href=\"unreleased.html#quest-quality\">Scope and live testing</a>.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"chapterhouse-candidate\">The Vigil of the Dawn — live testing</h2><p>The Winged Helm of the Dawn is earned through Camil’s Vigil of the Dawn. Its existing stats and sockets remain unchanged. Chapterhouse also awards three miniboss items, six final Raid variants and a four-quality augment. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> and <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"quest-ingredients\">Quest ingredients and item quality</h2><p>Normal-item quest requirements accept Polished, Exalted and Ascended versions of the same item. Shakrn Meadowgreen in South Karana accepts an Aviak Charm of any ordinary quality plus two Star Rubies for Ascended Crafted Gauntlets, following the current class-armor reward policy. Ingredients are consumed; their quality does not upgrade the configured reward. Exact Normal inputs are used first when both are offered. Explicit quality requirements, reforging recipes and separate epic, hunt and dungeon catalogs retain their own rules. Quest hand-ins and task delivery support the change; in-game acceptance testing remains open.</p>\n<details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"thj-behavior-candidate\"><summary>How ordinary item stats scale</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>The update uses unmodified stock ProjectEQ as an approximation of standard EverQuest, then preserves the exact researched values where available. It changes 143,332 existing tier definitions across 47,809 eligible ordinary families. Normal items, the 209 starter families, custom Hunt/dungeon rewards, augment families and quest-only epics keep their existing treatment. Families that exceed native stat limits are excluded for review.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Ascended field</th><th>Candidate target from stock</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Positive AC, HP, mana, primary stats, resists, weapon damage and HP/mana regeneration</td><td>2×</td></tr><tr><td>Haste</td><td>1.5×, rounded</td></tr><tr><td>Spell Damage when stock has none</td><td>Higher of 2× INT or WIS</td></tr><tr><td>Healing Amount when stock has none</td><td>2× WIS</td></tr><tr><td>Accuracy when stock has none</td><td>Half DEX, rounded upward</td></tr><tr><td>New heroics</td><td>Quarter of the final matching stat, rounded; Ascended only</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Polished and Exalted receive one-third and two-thirds of the increase from Normal to Ascended. These intermediate formulas and extrapolation beyond the screenshots are Nightcap tuning choices. Attack and sparse utility fields use stock values unless an exact observed override applies. Existing effects, sockets, delays, equip rules, loot routes and owned items are preserved.</p>\n\n</div></details><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"loot-finder-preview\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#equipment--loot-finder-preview\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"classic-robes\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#equipment--classic-robes\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><h2 id=\"ashen-compact\">The Ashen Compact — live testing</h2><p><a href=\"ashen-compact.html\">The Ashen Compact</a> is an installed level-50 Shadow Knight helmet campaign in a curated Kael expedition. Its paired server and client release is available for testing; full encounter, rendering and balance acceptance remain open.</p><p>The Warhelm of the Ashen Compact uses the Paladin helm budget with INT replacing WIS. It requires a held Shadow Knight class. Its new enclosed Classic appearance requires the paired client update.</p>\n<h2 id=\"player-bazaar\">Persistent player listings — live testing</h2><p>The Commonlands player market is installed for live testing; native search and buying still need player verification. Its supported permanent items and stacks remain listed while the seller is offline. It has stricter posting requirements than direct player trading, including empty bags and exactly recoverable saved item data. <a href=\"tunnel.html#player-bazaar\">Market instructions and restrictions</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"paladin-weapon-grip\">Paladin weapon grips — live testing</h2><p><strong>Paired October28 update:</strong> fully exit EQ and use launcher Play to install release2026102801. It repairs the stale client definition that could leave SoulFire two-handed after a 1HS message. Shield use and rendered swing checks remain open for player testing.</p><p>The assessed stats are installed for live testing. Ascended SoulFire uses 26/30 in 1HS or 46/45 in 2HS with Accuracy 10; Ascended Avenger uses 30/30 or 66/44 with Accuracy 15; Ascended Defender uses 36/30 or 72/40 with Accuracy 25. Avenger adds 1 point and Defender adds 3 points of shield block with an eligible shield in 1HS. Defender also gains improved healing and heroic wisdom, with its proc available at level 45. Grip changes preserve augments and saved charges. The one-handed grip stays primary-only. Shield abilities and augments can affect which grip deals more damage.</p><p>The SoulFire, Fiery Avenger and Fiery Defender quests award their Ascended versions directly. No extra essence or platinum is required for Defender. Owners of an original Defender can use the free <a href=\"ascension.html\">Epic Forgemaster exchange</a>, preserving its grip and customizations. There is no automatic inventory conversion. Meet each quest's faction and ingredient requirements.</p><p>Change grip out of combat and casting. Remove the shield before returning an equipped weapon to 2HS; augments must support the destination type. SoulFire's heal click is replaced by the grip toggle. Return to 2HS before reforging eligible copies. The grip is saved per item, including Bazaar transfers; generic links and type filters describe the base 2HS definition. Full native gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p><p><a href=\"augment-audit.html\">All top-quality augments, drop zones and secondary specialties</a> — live testing; gameplay acceptance remains open.</p>\n<h2 id=\"power-source-training\">Power Source training — Not released</h2><p>A separate combat-XP path for supported item families is in development. A training item occupies the Power Source slot and grants no equipment benefits there. Existing loot qualities, stats, drops and Reforging Box recipes remain. <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#power-source-training\">Power Source training preview</a>.</p>\n",
+  "body": "<p>Find ordinary equipment with the <a href=\"loot-finder.html\">Loot finder</a>, browse <a href=\"items.html\">Hunt rewards</a>, or compare an upgrade in the experimental <a href=\"build-lab.html\">Build Lab</a>.</p><h2 id=\"free-trade\">Player trading and duplicate items</h2><p>Trade formerly NO DROP and NO TRANSFER items, already-attuned gear, bags, their contents and augments. <strong>LORE restrictions are disabled</strong>, so duplicate ownership is allowed. Inventory capacity, temporary-item expiration and Pet Armor restrictions remain. Equipment eligibility still depends on your held classes and the remaining item requirements.</p>\n<h2 id=\"item-tiers\">Polished, Exalted, and Ascended loot</h2><p>Eligible dropped equipment and bags can appear in three stronger custom tiers. Their health, mana, defenses, and offensive stats scale by item family.</p>\n<p>Ordinary eligible equipment and bags now roll <strong>20% Polished, 5% Exalted and 1% Ascended</strong>, leaving 74% Normal when all variants exist. These chances apply per eligible item drop, not per kill. Already generated loot is not rerolled. Zone-hunt and dungeon rewards retain their separate rates.</p><h2 id=\"zone-hunt\">Augments in50 Classic zones; gear in the original48</h2><p>Any unowned, killable NPC in an enabled augment zone can roll its augment, including guards, named and quest NPCs, killable merchants and scripted combat adds. Player-owned/charmed pets, mercenaries, swarm pets, protected noncombat actors and restored corpses do not reroll. Native corpse ownership and encounter access still apply. Augments roll at 1.5%; approved native equipment sources keep their separate 0.5% chance and level/night restrictions. Qualities remain Base60%, Polished30%, Exalted8%, Ascension2%; no guaranteed drop or pity counter. <a href=\"zones.html\">Zone rewards</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"hunt-sockets\">Six armor locations for heroic augments</h2><p>Eligible Base and tiered head, arms, hands, chest, legs and feet armor gains one type-22 socket, preserving existing sockets. Zone augments add stats and heroic attributes; item level requirements still apply. At level 50, every two effective heroic INT from these socketed augments allows one more point of item Spell Damage, up to +30; heroic WIS does the same for Healing Amount. With the current 750 cap, either can reach 780. Extra cap room only helps when you have enough of the actual bonus.</p>\n<h2 id=\"zone-forge\">Upgrade matching rewards</h2><p><code>#zoneforge</code> uses <strong>three Base copies</strong> for one Polished reward, then <strong>four Polished</strong> for one Exalted or <strong>four Exalted</strong> for one Ascension. Artisan Veyra’s reusable Reforging Box also upgrades four identical Polished or Exalted copies, including eligible ordinary tiered gear. The box also accepts <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#normal-items\">three identical eligible Normal/Base copies for Polished</a>; higher recipes stay at four. Read <a href=\"item-upgrades.html\">Item upgrades</a> for inputs, restrictions and the two distinct top-tier names.</p>\n<details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"heroic-gear\"><summary>Heroic stats on Ascended equipment</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Ascended gear and Ascended epics add heroic stats on top of their improved base stats. This describes the existing equipment tiers; the new zone rewards have their own heroic stats at each quality.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"caster-gear\"><summary>Gear bonuses for casters and healers</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Eligible direct damage spells and procs add effective Spell Damage once. Each ordinary DoT tick adds half the effective bonus, rounded down, independent of duration. Healing Amount retains percentage healing and its existing HoT distribution. Each item-bonus total has a 750 base cap; eligible Hunt augments can raise it to 780 at level 50 when enough actual bonus is equipped. Clients also gain 0.1% per heroic INT on direct damage and per heroic WIS on direct healing; DoTs and HoTs do not gain this heroic multiplier. The separate Bard area-DoT route retains its native behavior.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"stat-cap\"><summary>More room for core stats</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>The normal core-stat cap is raised to 425, with heroic stat effects handled separately.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"summoned-gear\"><summary>Ascended summoned equipment</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Eligible summoned gear becomes Ascended when a matching version exists. The supported Paladin and Cleric summoned-hammer families have zero merchant resale value at every quality, including items you already own. Summoning does not bypass spell or item-level requirements.</p>\n</div></details><h2 id=\"bags\">More room in your bags</h2><p>Buy bags up to 40 slots, with base prices from 10 to 7,500 platinum. Merchant price adjustments and each bag’s capacity and contents restrictions still apply. Free trading does not reduce expensive bag purchase prices.</p>\n<details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"merchant-payouts\"><summary>Better payouts for ordinary loot</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Boosted merchant payouts remain in place for ordinary loot. Formerly NO DROP items use the fixed one-platinum payout below instead of those price modifiers.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"fixed-resale\"><summary>One platinum for formerly NO DROP items</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Ordinary merchants and <code>#sellall</code> pay exactly 1 platinum per physical item from the eligible formerly NO DROP pool. Five stack units pay 5 platinum; a charged object pays 1 platinum total. Purchase prices have a one-platinum floor. Merchant previews can differ from actual payment. Zone-hunt rewards, dungeon rewards and the supported divine summoned-hammer families have no merchant resale value.</p>\n</div></details><h2 id=\"selling\">Bulk selling from the command or merchant window</h2><p>Use <code>#sellall</code> to sell eligible carried items without targeting a merchant, or use the merchant window’s <strong>Sell All</strong> button. Containers, food, drink, spell reagents and casting focus items are kept. Zero-value items, including zone rewards and the supported divine summoned hammers, are skipped. <strong class=\"inline\">Sales are immediate and can include valuable gear. Bank anything you want to keep first.</strong></p>\n<h2 id=\"winged-helmet\">Winged Helm of the Dawn</h2><p>A custom Paladin helmet with an installed appearance for visual testing. <strong class=\"inline\">Earn this helmet through Camil’s Vigil of the Dawn, now in live testing.</strong></p>\n\n<h2 id=\"eligibility\">Wear gear for your whole build</h2><p>Ordinary equipment recognizes all held classes. Class-matching wearable items and augments allow all playable races; deity, level, slot, weapon and augment restrictions remain. See <a href=\"multiclass.html#equipment-access\">equipment eligibility</a>.</p><h2 id=\"dungeon-rewards\">Dungeon completion rewards</h2><p><a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Raid and Grind dungeons</a> have 24 shared reward designs and three exclusive Raid designs for each of the 21 released dungeons. Grind grants Normal; Raid grants Polished or Ascended. These permanent, tradeable, non-lore items have zero merchant resale and no existing forging recipe. Their bags have up to ten slots and 100% weight reduction.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"click-cooldowns\">Item click reuse</h2><p>Items without an explicit shared reuse group keep their own cooldowns without locking unrelated abilities. Copies of the same item share reuse; explicitly grouped items still share their group. Existing saved waits retain their expiry. See <a href=\"combat.html#ability-cooldowns\">the cooldown update</a>.</p>\n<details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"reviewed-ascended\"><summary>Reviewed Ascended values</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Supported numeric fields on 131 Ascended items now follow inspected THJ Legendary references. These families use per-item values rather than one universal multiplier. Some values are lower than before; original effects and existing sockets remain.</p><table><caption>Selected Ascended reference values</caption><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Values</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Heavy Yttrium Chestplate</td><td>150 AC; 250 HP and mana; 40 Spell Damage and Healing Amount</td></tr><tr><td>Blood Cord</td><td>70 AC; 200 HP and mana; 40 STA and 10 heroic STA; 40 Spell Damage and Healing Amount</td></tr><tr><td>Talisman of Vah Kerrath</td><td>250 HP and mana; 8 to each heroic attribute; 30 Spell Damage and Healing Amount</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"starter-bands\"><summary>Starter upgrades and dungeon progression</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Approved starter families use smaller steps: Bronze chest armor has 6, 7, 8 and 9 AC across Normal, Polished, Exalted and Ascended. Bronze Long Sword has 4, 5, 6 and 7 damage at fixed delay 32. Cultural armor is excluded from this retuning. Comparable Normal dungeon rewards remain stronger.</p></div></details><details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"earned-procs\"><summary>Earned melee and pet equipment</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Selected items gain sympathetic healing, combat procs or received-healing support. Healing, Runic and Hastened Fragments of Truth and Bloodfrenzy Core have earned boss routes; later-era bosses still require their normal access. Bloodfrenzy Core is a power-source item, while the original Bloodfrenzy remains a weapon. New sockets do not bypass augment compatibility.</p>\n</div></details><h2 id=\"class-armor-candidate\">Ascended class-armor quest rewards</h2><p>Crafted, Lambent, Darkforge, Ivy Etched and Totemic quests now grant existing Ascended versions of their 37 reviewed armor rewards. Substantial class-armor quests qualify even when repeatable; cheap/basic hand-ins stay excluded. Materials and quest requirements remain. Already-owned armor is not automatically converted. <a href=\"unreleased.html#quest-quality\">Scope and live testing</a>.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"chapterhouse-candidate\">The Vigil of the Dawn — live testing</h2><p>The Winged Helm of the Dawn is earned through Camil’s Vigil of the Dawn. Its existing stats and sockets remain unchanged. Chapterhouse also awards three miniboss items, six final Raid variants and a four-quality augment. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> and <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"quest-ingredients\">Quest ingredients and item quality</h2><p>Normal-item quest requirements accept Polished, Exalted and Ascended versions of the same item. Shakrn Meadowgreen in South Karana accepts an Aviak Charm of any ordinary quality plus two Star Rubies for Ascended Crafted Gauntlets, following the current class-armor reward policy. Ingredients are consumed; their quality does not upgrade the configured reward. Exact Normal inputs are used first when both are offered. Explicit quality requirements, reforging recipes and separate epic, hunt and dungeon catalogs retain their own rules. Quest hand-ins and task delivery support the change; in-game acceptance testing remains open.</p>\n<details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"thj-behavior-candidate\"><summary>How ordinary item stats scale</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>The update uses unmodified stock ProjectEQ as an approximation of standard EverQuest, then preserves the exact researched values where available. It changes 143,332 existing tier definitions across 47,809 eligible ordinary families. Normal items, the 209 starter families, custom Hunt/dungeon rewards, augment families and quest-only epics keep their existing treatment. Families that exceed native stat limits are excluded for review.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Ascended field</th><th>Candidate target from stock</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Positive AC, HP, mana, primary stats, resists, weapon damage and HP/mana regeneration</td><td>2×</td></tr><tr><td>Haste</td><td>1.5×, rounded</td></tr><tr><td>Spell Damage when stock has none</td><td>Higher of 2× INT or WIS</td></tr><tr><td>Healing Amount when stock has none</td><td>2× WIS</td></tr><tr><td>Accuracy when stock has none</td><td>Half DEX, rounded upward</td></tr><tr><td>New heroics</td><td>Quarter of the final matching stat, rounded; Ascended only</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Polished and Exalted receive one-third and two-thirds of the increase from Normal to Ascended. These intermediate formulas and extrapolation beyond the screenshots are Nightcap tuning choices. Attack and sparse utility fields use stock values unless an exact observed override applies. Existing effects, sockets, delays, equip rules, loot routes and owned items are preserved.</p>\n\n</div></details><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"loot-finder-preview\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#equipment--loot-finder-preview\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"classic-robes\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#equipment--classic-robes\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><h2 id=\"ashen-compact\">The Ashen Compact — live testing</h2><p><a href=\"ashen-compact.html\">The Ashen Compact</a> is an installed level-50 Shadow Knight helmet campaign in a curated Kael expedition. Its paired server and client release is available for testing; full encounter, rendering and balance acceptance remain open.</p><p>The Warhelm of the Ashen Compact uses the Paladin helm budget with INT replacing WIS. It requires a held Shadow Knight class. Its new enclosed Classic appearance requires the paired client update.</p>\n<h2 id=\"player-bazaar\">Persistent player listings — live testing</h2><p>The Commonlands player market is installed for live testing; native search and buying still need player verification. Its supported permanent items and stacks remain listed while the seller is offline. It has stricter posting requirements than direct player trading, including empty bags and exactly recoverable saved item data. <a href=\"tunnel.html#player-bazaar\">Market instructions and restrictions</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"paladin-weapon-grip\">Paladin weapon grips — live testing</h2><p><strong>Paired October28 update:</strong> fully exit EQ and use launcher Play to install release2026102801. It repairs the stale client definition that could leave SoulFire two-handed after a 1HS message. Shield use and rendered swing checks remain open for player testing.</p><p>The assessed stats are installed for live testing. Ascended SoulFire uses 26/30 in 1HS or 46/45 in 2HS with Accuracy 10; Ascended Avenger uses 30/30 or 66/44 with Accuracy 15; Ascended Defender uses 36/30 or 72/40 with Accuracy 25. Avenger adds 1 point and Defender adds 3 points of shield block with an eligible shield in 1HS. Defender also gains improved healing and heroic wisdom, with its proc available at level 45. Grip changes preserve augments and saved charges. The one-handed grip stays primary-only. Shield abilities and augments can affect which grip deals more damage.</p><p>The SoulFire, Fiery Avenger and Fiery Defender quests award their Ascended versions directly. No extra essence or platinum is required for Defender. Owners of an original Defender can use the free <a href=\"ascension.html\">Epic Forgemaster exchange</a>, preserving its grip and customizations. There is no automatic inventory conversion. Meet each quest's faction and ingredient requirements.</p><p>Change grip out of combat and casting. Remove the shield before returning an equipped weapon to 2HS; augments must support the destination type. SoulFire's heal click is replaced by the grip toggle. Return to 2HS before reforging eligible copies. The grip is saved per item, including Bazaar transfers; generic links and type filters describe the base 2HS definition. Full native gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p><p><a href=\"augment-audit.html\">All top-quality augments, drop zones and secondary specialties</a> — live testing; gameplay acceptance remains open.</p>",
