-  "body": "<p class=\"feature-intro\">Nightcap’s custom adventures and systems, all in one place. Classic is the current chapter; the level cap is 50. Released systems are in live testing; player and balance acceptance remain separate.</p><nav class=\"feature-jumps\" aria-label=\"Feature groups\"><a href=\"#custom-adventures\">Adventures &amp; quests</a><a href=\"#custom-builds\">Character &amp; combat</a><a href=\"#custom-world\">Gear, crafting &amp; world</a><a href=\"#custom-tools\">Tools &amp; previews</a></nav><h2 id=\"custom-adventures\">Custom adventures &amp; quests</h2><div class=\"feature-list\"><section class=\"feature-row\" id=\"adventuring\"><h3>Raid &amp; Grind dungeons</h3><div><p>Choose respawning Grind runs or harder Raid runs with permanent enemy deaths. All 21 Classic dungeons have personal boss checklists, completion rewards and exclusive Raid designs; Chapterhouse and curated Kael add separate level-50 expeditions. New High Keep Raid runs include the Osargen prison break.</p><p><strong>Classic Cazic-Thule:</strong> restored lizardmen, named encounters and patrols are available in the public zone as well as private runs. <a href=\"travel.html#cazic-thule\">Travel and encounter rules</a>.</p><p><a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Choose Raid or Grind →</a></p></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\" id=\"story\"><h3 id=\"hate-layout-preview\">Plane of Hate layout — live testing</h3><p>New Keeper runs place Nightcap’s existing Hate encounters on walking routes, preserving loot and earned rewards. Existing runs keep their original layout. Managed Hate now has 47 additional ordinary enemies, with existing run progress preserved. Pulls and complete-run player acceptance remain open. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#hate-layout-preview\">Entry, landmarks and testing</a>.</p><h3>Custom helmet quests</h3><div><p>Earn the Winged Helm of the Dawn through Camil’s Vigil: a level-50 Paladin story with personal chapters, a three-wave defense and custom Chapterhouse bosses. The Ashen Compact adds a demanding level-50 Shadow Knight campaign in curated Kael, reached through the hidden Everfrost passage. Both quests are in live testing.</p><p><a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Paladin helmet quest →</a> · <a href=\"ashen-compact.html\">Shadow Knight helmet quest →</a></p></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\" id=\"zone-hunt\"><h3>Zone Hunt: custom gear &amp; augments</h3><div><p>Hunt heroic augments across50 Classic zones, with equipment families retained in the original48. Zone rewards have four qualities and balanced secondary specialties, with matching-copy forging and six eligible armor locations for augments.</p><p><a href=\"zone-hunt.html\">How Zone Hunt works →</a> · <a href=\"zones.html\">Browse zone rewards →</a></p></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\" id=\"epics\"><h3>Ascended epic quest</h3><div><p>Bring an earned, supported original class epic to the Epic Forgemaster and reforge it with Essence of Ascension and platinum. Eligibility follows your starting class; the original epic must already be earned.</p><p><a href=\"ascension.html\">Ascend your epic →</a></p></div></section></div><h2 id=\"custom-builds\">Custom character &amp; combat systems</h2><h3 id=\"solo-self-found-preview\">Solo self-found</h3><p>Swear a permanent level-1 oath to find everything yourself: no player trading, Bazaar, parcels, shared bank or player groups, and no passive AA. <a href=\"multiclass.html#solo-self-found\">How to walk alone</a>.</p><div class=\"feature-list\"><section class=\"feature-row\" id=\"character\"><h3>Three classes. One character.</h3><div><p>Keep your starting class and choose two more from level 1. Combine their spells, skills, equipment access and strongest base HP/mana calculations.</p><p><a href=\"multiclass.html\">Build your character →</a></p></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\" id=\"aa\"><h3>AA progression from the beginning</h3><div><p>Earn two AA per level-equivalent while leveling, or allocate up to 100% of eligible XP to AA. The allowed pool opens at level 1, with earned points and prerequisites.</p><p><a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">Plan your AA progression →</a></p></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\" id=\"companions\"><h3>A roster of companions</h3><div><p>Summon multiple pets, command one or all, manage their equipment and develop pet builds through earned gear and abilities.</p><p><a href=\"pets.html\">Manage your pets →</a></p></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\" id=\"combat\"><h3>Combat built around your whole build</h3><div><p>Instant DoT casts, melee while casting, lasting ordinary blessings and earned class synergies support new combinations. Normal death preserves EXP and belongings.</p><p><a href=\"combat.html\">Read the combat rules →</a></p></div></section></div><h2 id=\"custom-world\">Custom gear, crafting &amp; world systems</h2><h3 id=\"keyless-doors-preview\">Keyless doors</h3><p>Ordinary door keys and lock picks are no longer required. <a href=\"travel.html#keyless-doors\">Door access and remaining restrictions</a>.</p><div class=\"feature-list\"><section class=\"feature-row\" id=\"rewards\"><h3>Tiered loot &amp; free trading</h3><div><p>Find Polished, Exalted and Ascended versions of eligible ordinary gear. Trade freely, own duplicates and equip across your held classes while remaining item requirements still apply.</p><p><a href=\"equipment.html\">Understand gear progression →</a> · <a href=\"advanced-loot.html\">Personal loot controls →</a></p></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\" id=\"reforging\"><h3>Reforge duplicate equipment</h3><div><p>Turn matching copies into a higher quality using Artisan Veyra’s reusable Reforging Box or Zone Hunt forging. Recipes differ by reward system; dungeon rewards do not use these upgrades.</p><p><a href=\"item-upgrades.html\">Compare upgrade recipes →</a></p></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\" id=\"class-armor\"><h3>Ascended class-armor quests</h3><div><p>Earn Ascended rewards from the reviewed Crafted, Lambent, Darkforge, Ivy Etched and Totemic quests. Their materials and quest requirements remain; already-owned armor is not converted.</p><p><a href=\"equipment.html#class-armor-candidate\">Find the class-armor rules →</a></p></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\" id=\"crafting\"><h3>Stacked materials &amp; Craft All</h3><div><p>Prepare at the tunnel workshop, combine from material stacks and repeat an eligible selected recipe with Craft All. Skill checks, ingredients and class or station requirements remain.</p><p><a href=\"tradeskills.html\">Use the workshop →</a></p></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\" id=\"exploration\"><h3>Waypoint Explorer</h3><div><p>Discover crystal markers to unlock return destinations with the Waypoint Master. Complete the current discovery catalog to earn the Explorer title; progress is personal.</p><p><a href=\"waypoints.html\">Start exploring →</a></p></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\" id=\"world\"><h3>A custom Commonlands home base</h3><div><p>Gather at class courts, crafting stations, limited-stock traders and level-based blessing services. City routes, rings, spires and Nightcap Recall connect your adventures.</p><p><a href=\"tunnel.html\">Meet the tunnel services →</a> · <a href=\"travel.html\">Explore travel options →</a></p></div></section></div><h2 id=\"custom-tools\">Tools &amp; upcoming content</h2><p>Try builds and rotation priorities in the experimental <a href=\"build-lab.html\">Build Lab</a>, find ordinary equipment with the <a href=\"loot-finder.html\">Loot finder</a>, or update with the <a href=\"launcher.html\">Nightcap launcher</a>. Each tool explains its limits.</p><p><a href=\"unreleased.html#journal\">Adventure Journal &amp; Epic 0.5</a> remains <strong>not released</strong>. Available helmet quests are listed above.</p>\n<h3 id=\"player-bazaar-preview\">Player bazaar — live testing</h3><p>Persistent player-priced listings in East Commonlands, without parking an auctioneer. <a href=\"tunnel.html#player-bazaar\">Posting, buying and current QA</a>.</p><p>Use the <a href=\"tunnel.html#bazaar-seller-panel\">Sell / My Listings tab</a> to post items, cancel listings and collect proceeds with buttons. In live testing.</p><p class=\"overview-links\">Choose a feature above for its guide. Smaller improvements, repairs and release history belong in <a href=\"recent-changes.html\">Change Log</a>.</p><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"hole-entrance\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#features--hole-entrance\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"loot-finder-preview\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#features--loot-finder-preview\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"hate-commonlands-candidate\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#features--hate-commonlands-candidate\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"quest-ingredients-candidate\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#features--quest-ingredients-candidate\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"thj-behavior-candidate\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#features--thj-behavior-candidate\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"tools\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#features--tools\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"updates\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#features--updates\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"october-improvements\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#features--october-improvements\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"thj-scaling\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#features--thj-scaling\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"chapterhouse-candidate\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#features--chapterhouse-candidate\">Change Log →</a></p></aside>\n<h2 id=\"paladin-weapon-grip-preview\">Paladin weapon grips</h2><p><strong>Live testing:</strong> SoulFire, Fiery Avenger and Fiery Defender switch between 1HS and 2HS with a right-click. The paired October28 update repairs stale grip definitions, adds the assessed weapon stats and makes all three quest rewards Ascended. The Paladin epic has no extra payment step; existing normal Defenders have a free exchange. Other classes keep their epic forge and Monk AAs are unchanged. Fully exit EQ and update through the launcher to release2026102801. <a href=\"equipment.html#paladin-weapon-grip\">Stats, behavior and restrictions</a>.</p>\n<p>Hate boss placement is corrected: Maestro and the Hand use their expected platforms, and Innoruuk occupies the southern throne area. Existing run progress and the 47 added ordinary spawns remain. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#hate-layout-preview\">Current landmarks</a>.</p>\n<p><a href=\"augment-audit.html\">All top-quality augments, drop zones and secondary specialties</a> — live testing; gameplay acceptance remains open.</p>\n<h3 id=\"power-source-training\">Power Source item training — Not released</h3><p>An additional combat-XP route from Normal/Base to the existing top quality is in development. The Reforging Box remains. <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#power-source-training\">Power Source training preview</a>.</p>\n\n<h3 id=\"faction-standings-preview\">Faction standings — live testing</h3><p>A white-text faction window with numerical standings, bars, name search and target lookup is available in game. <a href=\"commands.html#faction-standings\">Commands and limits</a>.</p><p>Try builds and rotation priorities in the experimental <a href=\"build-lab.html\">Build Lab</a>, find ordinary equipment with the <a href=\"loot-finder.html\">Loot finder</a>, or update with the <a href=\"launcher.html\">Nightcap launcher</a>. Each tool explains its limits.</p><p><a href=\"unreleased.html#journal\">Adventure Journal &amp; Epic 0.5</a> remains <strong>not released</strong>. Available helmet quests are listed above.</p>\n",
+  "body": "<p class=\"feature-intro\">Nightcap’s custom adventures and systems, all in one place. Classic is the current chapter; the level cap is 50. Released systems are in live testing; player and balance acceptance remain separate.</p><nav class=\"feature-jumps\" aria-label=\"Feature groups\"><a href=\"#custom-adventures\">Adventures &amp; quests</a><a href=\"#custom-builds\">Character &amp; combat</a><a href=\"#custom-world\">Gear, crafting &amp; world</a><a href=\"#custom-tools\">Tools &amp; previews</a></nav><h2 id=\"custom-adventures\">Custom adventures &amp; quests</h2><div class=\"feature-list\"><section class=\"feature-row\" id=\"adventuring\"><h3>Raid &amp; Grind dungeons</h3><div><p>Choose respawning Grind runs or harder Raid runs with permanent enemy deaths. All 21 Classic dungeons have personal boss checklists, completion rewards and exclusive Raid designs; Chapterhouse and curated Kael add separate level-50 expeditions. New High Keep Raid runs include the Osargen prison break.</p><p><strong>Classic Cazic-Thule:</strong> restored lizardmen, named encounters and patrols are available in the public zone as well as private runs. <a href=\"travel.html#cazic-thule\">Travel and encounter rules</a>.</p><p><a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Choose Raid or Grind →</a></p></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\" id=\"story\"><h3 id=\"hate-layout-preview\">Plane of Hate layout — live testing</h3><p>New Keeper runs place Nightcap’s existing Hate encounters on walking routes, preserving loot and earned rewards. Existing runs keep their original layout. Managed Hate now has 47 additional ordinary enemies, with existing run progress preserved. Pulls and complete-run player acceptance remain open. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#hate-layout-preview\">Entry, landmarks and testing</a>.</p><h3>Custom helmet quests</h3><div><p>Earn the Winged Helm of the Dawn through Camil’s Vigil: a level-50 Paladin story with personal chapters, a three-wave defense and custom Chapterhouse bosses. The Ashen Compact adds a demanding level-50 Shadow Knight campaign in curated Kael, reached through the hidden Everfrost passage. Both quests are in live testing.</p><p><a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Paladin helmet quest →</a> · <a href=\"ashen-compact.html\">Shadow Knight helmet quest →</a></p></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\" id=\"zone-hunt\"><h3>Zone Hunt: custom gear &amp; augments</h3><div><p>Hunt heroic augments across50 Classic zones, with equipment families retained in the original48. Zone rewards have four qualities and balanced secondary specialties, with matching-copy forging and six eligible armor locations for augments.</p><p><a href=\"zone-hunt.html\">How Zone Hunt works →</a> · <a href=\"zones.html\">Browse zone rewards →</a></p></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\" id=\"epics\"><h3>Ascended epic quest</h3><div><p>Bring an earned, supported original class epic to the Epic Forgemaster and reforge it with Essence of Ascension and platinum. Eligibility follows your starting class; the original epic must already be earned.</p><p><a href=\"ascension.html\">Ascend your epic →</a></p></div></section></div><h2 id=\"custom-builds\">Custom character &amp; combat systems</h2><h3 id=\"solo-self-found-preview\">Solo self-found</h3><p>Swear a permanent level-1 oath to find everything yourself: no player trading, Bazaar, parcels, shared bank or player groups, and no passive AA. <a href=\"multiclass.html#solo-self-found\">How to walk alone</a>.</p><div class=\"feature-list\"><section class=\"feature-row\" id=\"character\"><h3>Three classes. One character.</h3><div><p>Keep your starting class and choose two more from level 1. Combine their spells, skills, equipment access and strongest base HP/mana calculations.</p><p><a href=\"multiclass.html\">Build your character →</a></p></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\" id=\"aa\"><h3>AA progression from the beginning</h3><div><p>Earn two AA per level-equivalent while leveling, or allocate up to 100% of eligible XP to AA. The allowed pool opens at level 1, with earned points and prerequisites.</p><p><a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">Plan your AA progression →</a></p></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\" id=\"companions\"><h3>A roster of companions</h3><div><p>Summon multiple pets, command one or all, manage their equipment and develop pet builds through earned gear and abilities.</p><p><a href=\"pets.html\">Manage your pets →</a></p></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\" id=\"combat\"><h3>Combat built around your whole build</h3><div><p>Instant DoT casts, melee while casting, lasting ordinary blessings and earned class synergies support new combinations. Normal death preserves EXP and belongings.</p><p><a href=\"combat.html\">Read the combat rules →</a></p></div></section></div><h2 id=\"custom-world\">Custom gear, crafting &amp; world systems</h2><h3 id=\"keyless-doors-preview\">Keyless doors</h3><p>Ordinary door keys and lock picks are no longer required. <a href=\"travel.html#keyless-doors\">Door access and remaining restrictions</a>.</p><div class=\"feature-list\"><section class=\"feature-row\" id=\"rewards\"><h3>Tiered loot &amp; free trading</h3><div><p>Find Polished, Exalted and Ascended versions of eligible ordinary gear. Trade freely, own duplicates and equip across your held classes while remaining item requirements still apply.</p><p><a href=\"equipment.html\">Understand gear progression →</a> · <a href=\"advanced-loot.html\">Personal loot controls →</a></p></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\" id=\"reforging\"><h3>Reforge duplicate equipment</h3><div><p>Turn matching copies into a higher quality using Artisan Veyra’s reusable Reforging Box or Zone Hunt forging. Recipes differ by reward system; dungeon rewards do not use these upgrades.</p><p><a href=\"item-upgrades.html\">Compare upgrade recipes →</a></p></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\" id=\"class-armor\"><h3>Ascended class-armor quests</h3><div><p>Earn Ascended rewards from the reviewed Crafted, Lambent, Darkforge, Ivy Etched and Totemic quests. Their materials and quest requirements remain; already-owned armor is not converted.</p><p><a href=\"equipment.html#class-armor-candidate\">Find the class-armor rules →</a></p></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\" id=\"crafting\"><h3>Stacked materials &amp; Craft All</h3><div><p>Prepare at the tunnel workshop, combine from material stacks and repeat an eligible selected recipe with Craft All. Skill checks, ingredients and class or station requirements remain.</p><p><a href=\"tradeskills.html\">Use the workshop →</a></p></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\" id=\"exploration\"><h3>Waypoint Explorer</h3><div><p>Discover crystal markers to unlock return destinations with the Waypoint Master. Complete the current discovery catalog to earn the Explorer title; progress is personal.</p><p><a href=\"waypoints.html\">Start exploring →</a></p></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\" id=\"world\"><h3>A custom Commonlands home base</h3><div><p>Gather at class courts, crafting stations, limited-stock traders and level-based blessing services. City routes, rings, spires and Nightcap Recall connect your adventures.</p><p><a href=\"tunnel.html\">Meet the tunnel services →</a> · <a href=\"travel.html\">Explore travel options →</a></p></div></section></div><h2 id=\"custom-tools\">Tools &amp; upcoming content</h2><p>Try builds and rotation priorities in the experimental <a href=\"build-lab.html\">Build Lab</a>, find ordinary equipment with the <a href=\"loot-finder.html\">Loot finder</a>, or update with the <a href=\"launcher.html\">Nightcap launcher</a>. Each tool explains its limits.</p><p><a href=\"unreleased.html#journal\">Adventure Journal &amp; Epic 0.5</a> remains <strong>not released</strong>. Available helmet quests are listed above.</p>\n<h3 id=\"player-bazaar-preview\">Player bazaar — live testing</h3><p>Persistent player-priced listings in East Commonlands, without parking an auctioneer. <a href=\"tunnel.html#player-bazaar\">Posting, buying and current QA</a>.</p><p>Use the <a href=\"tunnel.html#bazaar-seller-panel\">Sell / My Listings tab</a> to post items, cancel listings and collect proceeds with buttons. In live testing.</p><p class=\"overview-links\">Choose a feature above for its guide. Smaller improvements, repairs and release history belong in <a href=\"recent-changes.html\">Change Log</a>.</p><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"hole-entrance\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#features--hole-entrance\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"loot-finder-preview\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#features--loot-finder-preview\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"hate-commonlands-candidate\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#features--hate-commonlands-candidate\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"quest-ingredients-candidate\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#features--quest-ingredients-candidate\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"thj-behavior-candidate\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#features--thj-behavior-candidate\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"tools\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#features--tools\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"updates\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#features--updates\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"october-improvements\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#features--october-improvements\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"thj-scaling\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#features--thj-scaling\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"chapterhouse-candidate\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#features--chapterhouse-candidate\">Change Log →</a></p></aside>\n<h2 id=\"paladin-weapon-grip-preview\">Paladin weapon grips</h2><p><strong>Live testing:</strong> SoulFire, Fiery Avenger and Fiery Defender switch between 1HS and 2HS with a right-click. The paired October28 update repairs stale grip definitions, adds the assessed weapon stats and makes all three quest rewards Ascended. The Paladin epic has no extra payment step; existing normal Defenders have a free exchange. Other classes keep their epic forge and Monk AAs are unchanged. Fully exit EQ and update through the launcher to release2026102801. <a href=\"equipment.html#paladin-weapon-grip\">Stats, behavior and restrictions</a>.</p>\n<p>Hate boss placement is corrected: Maestro and the Hand use their expected platforms, and Innoruuk occupies the southern throne area. Existing run progress and the 47 added ordinary spawns remain. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#hate-layout-preview\">Current landmarks</a>.</p>\n<p><a href=\"augment-audit.html\">All top-quality augments, drop zones and secondary specialties</a> — live testing; gameplay acceptance remains open.</p>",
