-  "body": "<h2 id=\"recipes\">Upgrade recipes</h2><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><caption>Guaranteed upgrades with no coin fee</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Input</th><th scope=\"col\">Result</th><th scope=\"col\">Method</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">3 identical eligible Normal/Base copies</th><td>1 Polished</td><td>Reforging Box; #zoneforge for zone rewards</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">4 identical Polished copies</th><td>1 Exalted</td><td>Reforging Box; #zoneforge for zone rewards</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">4 identical Exalted copies</th><td>1 Ascended ordinary item, or 1 Ascension zone reward</td><td>Reforging Box; #zoneforge for zone rewards</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"box\">Get the reusable Reforging Box</h2><ol><li>Hail <strong>Artisan Veyra</strong> in the East Commonlands tunnel for a free Reforging Box.</li><li>Put the box in a main inventory slot. Leave combat and casting, empty your cursor, and close trade, loot, merchant and station interactions.</li><li>Place three identical eligible Normal/Base copies (leave one slot empty), or four identical Polished or Exalted copies in the box. This is a container combine, not an NPC hand-in.</li><li>Press Combine. A valid recipe consumes the required copies and gives one next-quality item; keep the box for later.</li></ol><p>The box has no recipe above the top tier. Bags cannot be nested in the box. The supported-item catalog determines eligibility.</p>\n<h2 id=\"normal-items\">Three Normal items make Polished</h2><p>The Reforging Box accepts exactly <strong>3 identical eligible Normal (Base) items → 1 Polished item</strong>, for ordinary tiered equipment and Classic zone-hunt rewards. Put the three copies in the reusable box, leave its fourth slot empty, and press Combine. A matching Polished version must exist. The higher recipes still cost four copies. Stackable units count individually; nonstackable charged items count once each. Dungeon rewards and bags remain excluded. The recipe is available for live testing; in-game acceptance remains ongoing.</p>\n<h2 id=\"requirements\">Before combining</h2><p>Use unmodified items of one family and quality. An item's built-in color is allowed; a different player-applied dye color is not. Socketed, player-dyed, ornamented, customized and evolving instances are not eligible. Binding is preserved. Charged objects count as physical items, not as one copy per charge. If a result is unclear or items appear missing, stop retrying and contact the owner.</p>\n<h2 id=\"other-upgrades\">Keep other systems separate</h2><p><a href=\"ascension.html\">Epic Ascension</a> uses its own quest and materials. <a href=\"tradeskills.html\">Ordinary tradeskills</a> retain recipe requirements and success chances. The top-tier names do not mean those systems share recipes.</p><p><a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Dungeon rewards</a> use Normal, Polished and Ascended qualities but have no conversion through these recipes. Earn their qualities through Grind or Raid completion and Raid final-boss drops.</p>\n<h2 id=\"chapterhouse-candidate\">The Vigil of the Dawn — live testing</h2><p>Ember of the First Dawn uses #zoneforge: three Base copies or four Polished/Exalted copies make the next quality. Camil’s helmet receives no new socket. The miniboss and final Raid equipment do not use this augment recipe. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> and <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a>.</p>\n<aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"quest-ingredients-candidate\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#item-upgrades--quest-ingredients-candidate\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"thj-behavior-candidate\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#item-upgrades--thj-behavior-candidate\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><h2 id=\"ashen-compact\">The Ashen Compact — live testing</h2><p><a href=\"ashen-compact.html\">The Ashen Compact</a> is an installed level-50 Shadow Knight helmet campaign in a curated Kael expedition. Its paired server and client release is available for testing; full encounter, rendering and balance acceptance remain open.</p><p>Cinder forging uses three identical Base copies, then four Polished or Exalted copies. The helmet and other Kael equipment do not use that augment recipe.</p>\n<h2 id=\"paladin-grip-preview\">Paladin grips — live testing</h2><p>The <a href=\"equipment.html#paladin-weapon-grip\">weapon grip toggle</a> stores 1HS as an item customization. Switch back to 2HS before using the Reforging Box with an otherwise eligible weapon. Existing recipe, quality and augment requirements remain; new upgrade results start in 2HS. The SoulFire, Fiery Avenger and Fiery Defender quests now award Ascended weapons directly. Box recipes remain unchanged. Existing normal Fiery Defenders have a free <a href=\"ascension.html#paladin-grip-preview\">Epic Forgemaster exchange</a>; there is no automatic inventory conversion.</p>\n<h2 id=\"power-source-training\">Power Source training — Not released</h2><p>A candidate adds combat-XP training for supported ordinary equipment and Hunt augments. Place one eligible item in the Power Source slot and earn eligible combat XP; it advances through its existing qualities to Ascended (ordinary) or Ascension (Hunt). The item grants no equipment benefits while training. Existing held-class eligibility, any remaining race/deity restrictions, and required/recommended levels still apply.</p><p>The proposed Normal/Base-to-top target is roughly 4–8 hours, with increasingly longer steps: 80, 160 and 240 comparable-kill equivalents. Timing depends on earned XP, group shares and downtime and still needs in-game measurement. Character and AA XP are not spent, and AA allocation or the character level cap does not stop training.</p><p>The Reforging Box and #zoneforge retain their recipes. In this candidate, otherwise eligible copies with partial training can still be combined; that progress is discarded and the result starts its new tier at zero. Other customization restrictions remain. Progress is intended to follow the instance through transfers; custody and client checks remain pending. <code>#itemxp</code> reports progress when this feature is enabled. This method is not available on the player server yet.</p>",
+  "body": "<h2 id=\"recipes\">Upgrade recipes</h2><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><caption>Guaranteed upgrades with no coin fee</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Input</th><th scope=\"col\">Result</th><th scope=\"col\">Method</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">3 identical eligible Normal/Base copies</th><td>1 Polished</td><td>Reforging Box; #zoneforge for zone rewards</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">4 identical Polished copies</th><td>1 Exalted</td><td>Reforging Box; #zoneforge for zone rewards</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">4 identical Exalted copies</th><td>1 Ascended ordinary item, or 1 Ascension zone reward</td><td>Reforging Box; #zoneforge for zone rewards</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"box\">Get the reusable Reforging Box</h2><ol><li>Hail <strong>Artisan Veyra</strong> in the East Commonlands tunnel for a free Reforging Box.</li><li>Put the box in a main inventory slot. Leave combat and casting, empty your cursor, and close trade, loot, merchant and station interactions.</li><li>Place three identical eligible Normal/Base copies (leave one slot empty), or four identical Polished or Exalted copies in the box. This is a container combine, not an NPC hand-in.</li><li>Press Combine. A valid recipe consumes the required copies and gives one next-quality item; keep the box for later.</li></ol><p>The box has no recipe above the top tier. Bags cannot be nested in the box. The supported-item catalog determines eligibility.</p>\n<h2 id=\"normal-items\">Three Normal items make Polished</h2><p>The Reforging Box accepts exactly <strong>3 identical eligible Normal (Base) items → 1 Polished item</strong>, for ordinary tiered equipment and Classic zone-hunt rewards. Put the three copies in the reusable box, leave its fourth slot empty, and press Combine. A matching Polished version must exist. The higher recipes still cost four copies. Stackable units count individually; nonstackable charged items count once each. Dungeon rewards and bags remain excluded. The recipe is available for live testing; in-game acceptance remains ongoing.</p>\n<h2 id=\"requirements\">Before combining</h2><p>Use unmodified items of one family and quality. An item's built-in color is allowed; a different player-applied dye color is not. Socketed, player-dyed, ornamented, customized and evolving instances are not eligible. Binding is preserved. Charged objects count as physical items, not as one copy per charge. If a result is unclear or items appear missing, stop retrying and contact the owner.</p>\n<h2 id=\"other-upgrades\">Keep other systems separate</h2><p><a href=\"ascension.html\">Epic Ascension</a> uses its own quest and materials. <a href=\"tradeskills.html\">Ordinary tradeskills</a> retain recipe requirements and success chances. The top-tier names do not mean those systems share recipes.</p><p><a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Dungeon rewards</a> use Normal, Polished and Ascended qualities but have no conversion through these recipes. Earn their qualities through Grind or Raid completion and Raid final-boss drops.</p>\n<h2 id=\"chapterhouse-candidate\">The Vigil of the Dawn — live testing</h2><p>Ember of the First Dawn uses #zoneforge: three Base copies or four Polished/Exalted copies make the next quality. Camil’s helmet receives no new socket. The miniboss and final Raid equipment do not use this augment recipe. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> and <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a>.</p>\n<aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"quest-ingredients-candidate\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#item-upgrades--quest-ingredients-candidate\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"thj-behavior-candidate\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#item-upgrades--thj-behavior-candidate\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><h2 id=\"ashen-compact\">The Ashen Compact — live testing</h2><p><a href=\"ashen-compact.html\">The Ashen Compact</a> is an installed level-50 Shadow Knight helmet campaign in a curated Kael expedition. Its paired server and client release is available for testing; full encounter, rendering and balance acceptance remain open.</p><p>Cinder forging uses three identical Base copies, then four Polished or Exalted copies. The helmet and other Kael equipment do not use that augment recipe.</p>\n<h2 id=\"paladin-grip-preview\">Paladin grips — live testing</h2><p>The <a href=\"equipment.html#paladin-weapon-grip\">weapon grip toggle</a> stores 1HS as an item customization. Switch back to 2HS before using the Reforging Box with an otherwise eligible weapon. Existing recipe, quality and augment requirements remain; new upgrade results start in 2HS. The SoulFire, Fiery Avenger and Fiery Defender quests now award Ascended weapons directly. Box recipes remain unchanged. Existing normal Fiery Defenders have a free <a href=\"ascension.html#paladin-grip-preview\">Epic Forgemaster exchange</a>; there is no automatic inventory conversion.</p>",
