-  "body": "<h2 id=\"augment-audit-20261106\">November6: zone augments and exotic icons — live testing</h2><p>Augments can drop from any unowned killable NPC in enabled zones, including guards, named enemies, killable merchants and scripted adds. New secondary specialties and gem/crystal icons cover all qualities. Cazic-Thule/newer Hate augment pools enable; both expeditions now roll1.5%. Artwork is approved; gameplay QA remains open. <a href=\"augment-audit.html\">Full list and limits</a>.</p><h2 id=\"hunt-rates-20261101\">November 1: zone augments drop three times as often - live</h2><p>Zone Hunt augments now drop at <strong>1.5%</strong> per eligible kill (was 0.5%), about one per 67 kills. Zone equipment stays at 0.5%, and qualities stay Base 60%, Polished 30%, Exalted 8%, Ascension 2%. Each zone page lists its rates. Chapterhouse and Ashen Compact augments are unchanged. No client update is required. <a href=\"zone-hunt.html#drops\">How drops work</a>.</p><h2 id=\"ssf-20261101\">November 1: solo self-found mode - live testing</h2><p>New level-1 characters can swear a permanent solo self-found oath at the Ancient Chronicler. Self-found characters cannot trade with players, use either Bazaar, parcels, the shared or guild bank, or group or raid with players, and earn no passive AA. No client update is required. Player acceptance remains open. <a href=\"multiclass.html#solo-self-found\">How it works</a>.</p><h2 id=\"hate-density-20261030\">October 30: Plane of Hate density - live testing</h2><p>Server-side checks verified every Grind spawn point and natural respawns, including both Maestro encounters. The installed density update adds 47 ordinary enemies to managed Raid and Grind, preserving current runs and rewards. No client update or run reset is required. Player acceptance remains open. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#hate-layout-preview\">Hate modes and landmarks</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"public-cazic-20261030\">October 30 — public Classic Cazic-Thule restored</h2><p>Restored 188 Classic encounter points in open-world Cazic-Thule, which previously had no eligible combat population under Classic. Khaleid’s route now leads to the restored public encounters. Existing private Raid and Grind runs retain their own population and rewards. No client update is required; gameplay acceptance remains open.</p><p>Hate’s saved Raid population was also checked: every expected point was accounted for by living mobs, recorded kills or the final-boss gate. No Hate mobs were added. New-layout Grind and client visibility remain separate checks.</p><h2 id=\"recall-labels-20261030\">October 30: Commonlands recall labels corrected</h2><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Recall labels corrected (October 30):</strong> Client release 2026103001 restores Ancient Attunement’s name, Nightcap Recall’s hotbutton label and the recall description. Fully exit EverQuest and press Play in the normal launcher to update. Cast time, reuse and bind behavior are unchanged. In-game verification remains open.</p>\n<details class=\"change-entry\" open><summary>October28: Bazaar posting and readable controls — live testing</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Client update2026102803 accepts valid whole-platinum digits in both native text formats, reports unreadable input, and enlarges seller text with light colors. The earlier startup fixes and weapon changes are preserved. The owner confirmed the reported posting issue is resolved, the preview appears and the larger light text is readable. Broader market QA remains separate.</p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" open><summary>October 26: Bazaar seller panel and Paladin grips — live testing</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"bazaar-panel-candidate\">Sell / My Listings controls</h2><p>Client update 2026102601 adds the native Sell / My Listings tab for posting, cancelling owned listings and collecting offline proceeds. The paired server release also includes Paladin weapon grips. Close EverQuest and use launcher Play to update. Native gameplay acceptance remains open. <a href=\"tunnel.html#bazaar-seller-panel\">Panel instructions</a>.</p></div></details><h2 id=\"commonlands-bazaar-20261026\">October 26: Commonlands player bazaar — live testing</h2><p>Persistent player listings, offline seller proceeds and native search/purchase routing are installed in public East Commonlands. No parked auctioneer is required. Native RoF2 search, buying and full seller/buyer acceptance remain open. <a href=\"tunnel.html#player-bazaar\">Market instructions and restrictions</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"october24-coordinated\">October 24 — High Keep rescue, Ashen Compact and aggro corrections</h2><p>New High Keep Raid runs now rescue Osargen. The level-50 Ashen Compact begins with Drazhul and the Keeper in the hidden Everfrost passage before Permafrost. Close EQ and use launcher Play for its helmet appearance. NPC departure cleanup and stationary return-home restoration are corrected; the original Lower Guk bedroom-train report still needs an observed retest. Existing earned progress is retained. Full route, escort, appearance and balance acceptance remain open.</p>\n<h2 id=\"ashen-compact-everfrost\">October 24 — Ashen Compact entrance preview</h2><p>Before the coordinated release above, the <a href=\"ashen-compact.html\">Shadow Knight campaign</a> entrance was moved to the hidden Everfrost passage before Permafrost. Its frostbound crossing and return connect to curated Kael. At that preview stage it was a test candidate; the release above supersedes that availability.</p><h2 id=\"rogue-tome-learning\">October 24 - Multiclass tome learning repaired</h2><p>Eligible tomes can now be learned through any held class, fixing secondary and third-class Rogue learning. Failed right-clicks preserve the original tome; full lists, duplicate entries and failed saves no longer consume it. Discipline use levels and the level-1 AA policy are unchanged. See <a href=\"multiclass.html#learning-tomes\">learning combat disciplines</a> for requirements. Live gameplay acceptance remains under review.</p><h2 id=\"custom-feature-directory\">October 24 — Custom content on Features</h2><p><a href=\"features.html\">Features</a> now groups Raid &amp; Grind dungeons, helmet quests, Zone Hunt, epic reforging, class armor, crafting, exploration and custom character systems. Each entry links to its guide. The Ashen Compact preview is explicitly not released; gameplay, rewards and balance are unchanged.</p><p>Current instructions live in <a href=\"all-pages.html\">Guides</a>. This is the history of releases, improvements and fixes; older entries describe their date and may be superseded.</p><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"wiki-clarity\" open><summary>October 24, 2026 · A clearer wiki</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Features now highlights the major differences from standard EQ. Guides start with useful instructions; fixes and repeated release announcements are collected here. Navigation and text sizes are consistent, and long reference lists expand when needed. Existing tools, gameplay rules, reward values and links are preserved.</p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"hole-entrance\"><summary>October 24 · The Hole entrance</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing — keyless Hole entrance:</strong> The Hole Key and lock-picking requirement have been removed from the entrance rock in Paineel at <code>/loc 568,-896,-96</code>. Click the rock to open the passage without a key or lock picks. The server update is installed; in-game acceptance is pending. Paineel city-lift keys and the Sacred Key doors inside The Hole remain unchanged.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"aa-level-progression\"><summary>October 23: two AA per level and level-1 AA controls</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The paired update is installed for live testing. Keep AA allocation at 0% to earn full leveling XP plus two AA per level. Use the AA +/− controls from level 1, choose an intermediate percentage, or select 100% to hold your level and grind AA. Full focus earns 20 AA per current-level equivalent of XP. Update through launcher Play for game 2026102301. Saved points, purchases and partial progress are retained; native gameplay acceptance remains open.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"chapterhouse-candidate\"><summary>October 23 · The Vigil of the Dawn — live testing</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>October 23: Camil’s Chapterhouse quest, level-50–53 encounters, custom rewards, Ember augment, waypoint and Keeper are deployed for live testing. Native Tasks track the story. Full encounter balance and player acceptance remain open. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> and <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a>.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"loot-finder-preview\"><summary>October 22: production loot finder</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The <a href=\"loot-finder.html\">class and era loot finder</a> supports any held class by default, optional all-class matching, slot/quality/level/zone filters and item links to source mobs, locations and calculated drop chances. Production content refreshes automatically every fifteen minutes, with the last successful capture retained if a refresh fails. Existing gameplay, rewards and acceptance labels are unchanged.</p><p class=\"notice\" id=\"hate-commonlands-candidate\"><strong>Live testing — Hate Keeper in Commonlands:</strong> Find the Plane of Hate Keeper in East Commonlands at <code>/loc -1570,-346,3</code>, between Mirielle and Khalure in the travel area. Raid, Grind and return entry lead to Hate; private Hate instances retain an entrance Keeper. Public and private Hate entry require level 46; GM status is no longer required. The server update is installed. The owner confirmed the relocation, Commonlands visibility and Hate travel. Broader dungeon balance and full-clear QA remain separate.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"build-lab\"><summary>Build Lab — October 22</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The <a href=\"build-lab.html\">experimental Build Lab</a> compares two saved builds, supported spell benefits, Hunt item stat differences and editable ability priorities. Inspect mana and cast timelines or search the best priority order under your test conditions. It uses dated source controls and explicit assumptions, not a complete native combat simulation or universal best-build ranking.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"interactive-handbook\"><summary>October 22 — Your interactive field guide</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The wiki has a new lantern-lit design with four adventure paths, instant quick search, saved guides, light and dark reading modes, and a reading-progress bar. The equipment catalog keeps its filters and all four reward qualities. On the home page, expand <strong>Release notes &amp; live testing</strong> for the existing gameplay notices. <a href=\"about.html#navigation\">Learn the shortcuts and field notes →</a></p><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> The <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> give every dungeon three exclusive designs. The 14 added dungeons contribute 42 designs in two qualities; all 414 dungeon rewards are MAGIC. Fear, Hate and Sky receive lore-driven relics and equipped utility clicks. Gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"classic-dungeons-candidate\"><summary>October 22 — every Classic dungeon and unique rewards live</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#classic-candidate\">Every Classic dungeon coverage</a> adds the same Raid/Grind choices in 21 combat dungeon zones, including Fear, Hate and Sky. All 21 are installed for live testing; gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p>\n<p>The paired release also repairs stale dungeon item checks behind the reported Keeper error and installs durable Sky key services. Existing runs, earned rewards and the latest quest-tier and client updates are preserved. Native gameplay and balance acceptance remain open.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"quest-ingredients-20261022\"><summary>October 22 - quest ingredient fix live for testing</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Polished, Exalted and Ascended ingredients can satisfy Normal quest requirements, including Aviak Charm for Crafted Gauntlets. Shared hand-ins, task delivery and five older Temple quests are covered. The paired server and quest release is deployed; player QA remains open. <a href=\"equipment.html#quest-ingredients\">Scope and limits</a>.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"class-armor-candidate\"><summary>October 22 — Ascended class-armor quest rewards</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Crafted, Lambent, Darkforge, Ivy Etched and Totemic quests now grant 37 reviewed Ascended armor rewards. Substantial repeatable class-armor quests qualify; cheap/basic hand-ins remain excluded. The dependent Darkforge epic turn-in accepts Normal and Ascended pieces. Existing owned gear is not automatically converted. <strong>Live testing:</strong> native delivery and balance acceptance remain open. <a href=\"unreleased.html#quest-quality\">Scope and testing</a>.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"crystal-markers\"><summary>October 22 · Waypoint crystals — live testing</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Waypoints now have a glowing crystal with the existing <strong>a waypoint</strong> label. Fully close EverQuest, then use the normal launcher’s Play button to install game 2026102202 before testing. The crystal adds a model to the portal effect; appearance in Classic and Modern model modes and with particles low or off still needs in-game checks. Locations, discovery progress and return destinations are unchanged.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"classic-robes-20261022\"><summary>October 22 — robe waist correction in live testing</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Game update <strong>2026102204</strong> repairs the native waist binding after the earlier 2026102203 repair failed, covering all seven added Classic robe races and both genders. Close the game, reopen the normal launcher and press Play. In-game visual, dye and animation acceptance remains open. <a href=\"equipment.html#classic-robes\">Read the scope</a>.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"keeper-visibility-20261022\"><summary>October 22 — Dungeon Keeper placement</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The correction now separates Keepers from overlapping waypoints in Befallen, Unrest, Najena, Permafrost and Nagafen’s Lair. High Keep and Cazic-Thule already had separate positions. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">All seven Keeper locations</a> are listed for live testing; visibility remains unconfirmed. Waypoints, dungeon progress and client files are unchanged.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Level-scaled AA — live testing:</strong> Earn two AA per level while leveling. From level 1, use the AA +/− buttons to choose 0–100%; 100% pauses leveling so you can grind AA where you prefer. Close EverQuest and update through launcher Play for game 2026102301. Existing points, purchases and partial progress stay intact. <a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">AA progression and examples</a>.</p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"aa-million-xp\"><summary>October 21: slower AA earning and XP boost retirement</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The October 21 release used 1,000,000 AA experience per point with 10% passive earning; the October 23 level-scaled update supersedes that earning model. Goldwind’s paid package is retired, Matron’s free buffs remain, and XP boost durations are respected. Existing points and purchases remain intact. Live balance testing continues.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"thj-behavior-candidate\"><summary>October 19 · THJ behavior and stock gear — live testing</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is installed for live testing. Scaling uses 131 researched Legendary items and matching standard EverQuest baselines. Classic level 50 and starter progression are preserved. Reopen the normal launcher for game 2026101902 before testing. See <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open testing limits</a>.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"all-class-aa-20261019\"><summary>October 19: all-class AA update</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live AA testing:</strong> All 16 classes have more earned AA options: 75 newly available lines, 111 expanded lines and Druid access to Healing Boon. No existing line is removed. Classic remains level 50. Reconnect and turn Recommended AA off to browse your held classes. <a href=\"multiclass.html#all-class-aa\">Read the AA update</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Launch repair published:</strong> Game update 2026101901 corrects the client catalog mismatch that blocked Play after the previous update. Close EverQuest and the launcher, reopen your normal Nightcap shortcut, and press Play to receive the repair. Your game settings and the other managed files are preserved. Native login and gameplay confirmation remain open.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"thj-release\"><summary>October 18: item, spell, pet and melee release</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p><strong>Live testing:</strong> Selected Ascended items now use reviewed THJ values. Direct damage adds effective Spell Damage, ordinary DoT ticks add half, and heroic INT/WIS improve direct values. Starter quality steps remain modest below comparable Normal dungeon equipment.</p><p>The same release adds paged permanent-pet equipment, bounded owner-stat inheritance, earned pet/melee AA updates, separate Rabid Bear benefit and illusion effects, and shared 750 base caps with Hunt headroom. Close EverQuest and use the launcher for game update 2026101802. Classic level 50 remains active; gameplay and balance acceptance are still open.</p>\n<h2>October 18 - More ordinary quality loot</h2><p>Polished, Exalted and Ascended now have 20%, 5% and 1% chances per eligible ordinary equipment/bag drop. Hunt, dungeon and quest rewards are unchanged. Already generated loot is not rerolled.</p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"reforge-colors\"><summary>October 18, 2026: built-in item colors</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#requirements\">Reforging Box</a> and <a href=\"zone-hunt.html#forging\">zone forging</a> now accept an item's built-in color. This fixes ordinary items such as Dagger of Marnek being rejected as customized. A different player-applied dye color and the other customization restrictions still prevent combining. Recipes remain three Normal/Base copies or four higher-quality copies. No client update is required for this fix; in-game acceptance remains open.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"october-18-cooldowns\"><summary>October 18, 2026: separate ability cooldowns</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p><a href=\"combat.html#ability-cooldowns\">Activated AA families now have independent cooldowns</a>, including Rampage and Purify Body. Item and discipline timer collisions are also repaired. Existing saved waits keep their original expiry. Reconnect and test your abilities; <a href=\"unreleased.html#cooldown-identities\">generic skill and content-defined groups</a> remain under review.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"october-18\"><summary>October 18, 2026: Classic travel file repair</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Signed game update 2026101801 adds automatic missing/corrupt terrain and object archive repair for 17 Classic travel destinations, including West Commonlands, Misty Thicket and Toxxulia. Close EverQuest and press Play in the usual launcher. Existing gameplay assets and player settings are preserved; native zoning acceptance remains open.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"october-17\"><summary>October 17, 2026: progression, combat and crafting</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><ul><li>The optional <a href=\"multiclass.html#recommended-aa\">Recommended AA filter</a> provides an early survival, sustain and damage shortlist across held classes.</li><li>Passive AA is now 10%, preserving full leveling EXP, earned points and 4,000 AA XP per point.</li><li><a href=\"combat.html#monk-cooldowns\">Six basic Monk attacks</a> have separate reuse. <a href=\"combat.html#cooldown-corrections\">Cooldown duration repairs</a> address excessive and restarted timers; other shared identities remain under investigation.</li><li><a href=\"combat.html#death-exp\">Normal death costs no EXP or levels</a>; prior losses are not refunded.</li><li><a href=\"tradeskills.html#stack-limits\">Stackable items support at least 100</a>, retaining larger limits.</li><li>The <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#normal-items\">Reforging Box accepts three identical eligible Normal/Base copies</a> for Polished. Higher recipes still cost four.</li><li>Idle zones can unload without ending their workers and triggering a whole-game restart.</li><li>Update through launcher Play for the matched client. Gameplay and balance acceptance continue.</li></ul>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"october-16\"><summary>October 16, 2026</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><ul><li>The <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#required-bosses\">dungeon guide now lists every required boss</a> and explains boss-stage notices, full-clear credit and Keeper Status when task objectives are blank.</li><li><a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Raid and Grind dungeons</a> are deployed for live testing with personal boss checklists, shared rewards and exclusive Raid drops. Gameplay and balance acceptance remain open.</li><li><a href=\"features.html\">Features</a> now gathers the major departures from Classic.</li><li><a href=\"multiclass.html#equipment-access\">Equipment eligibility</a> recognizes held classes and permits playable races when the class matches; remaining restrictions still apply.</li><li><a href=\"combat.html#buffs\">Temporary AA buffs</a> retain their timers; ordinary blessings remain lasting.</li><li><a href=\"tunnel.html#banking\">Mira Coinwell</a> provides tunnel banking. Haldra stocks Leather Padding.</li><li>The wiki’s guides, commands and generated reward pages have been reviewed together against current release evidence.</li></ul>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"october-13\"><summary>October 13, 2026</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><ul><li><a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">Passive AA changed from 40% to 20%</a>, preserving full normal XP and 4,000 AA XP per point.</li><li><a href=\"multiclass.html#alternate-abilities\">All allowed AA ranks open at level 1</a>; points, eligibility and prerequisite ranks remain.</li><li><a href=\"tradeskills.html\">Stacked tradeskill ingredients and Craft All</a> are deployed.</li><li>The tunnel workshop layout is more spacious; the <a href=\"waypoints.html\">Unrest waypoint</a> moved beside its entrance Keeper.</li><li>Supported divine summoned-hammer families have <a href=\"equipment.html#summoned-gear\">zero resale value</a>.</li><li>The reported multiclass training/offhand issue and merchant Sell All button issue were confirmed resolved.</li></ul>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"october-12\"><summary>October 11–12, 2026</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><ul><li><a href=\"item-upgrades.html\">Reusable four-copy upgrades</a> are available from Artisan Veyra; higher #zoneforge steps now use four copies.</li><li><a href=\"equipment.html#free-trade\">LORE restrictions are disabled</a>. Food and drink requirements were removed.</li><li><a href=\"multiclass.html#spell-access\">Early scribing</a> allows eligible scrolls into the spellbook before their casting level.</li><li><a href=\"equipment.html#selling\">Sell All protects food, drink, reagents and casting focus items</a>.</li><li>The launcher uses personal access codes and shows <a href=\"launcher.html#patch-notes\">patch summaries</a>.</li><li>Waypoint portals and floating-eye Instance Keepers received visual corrections. The reported pet-summon crash was confirmed resolved.</li></ul>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"october-9\"><summary>October 9, 2026</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><ul><li><a href=\"zones.html\">48 Classic reward zones</a>, <a href=\"items.html\">384 reward variants</a>, type-22 augments and zone forging launched.</li><li>Passive AA increased to 40% at that time; the October 13 reduction above supersedes that rate.</li><li><a href=\"advanced-loot.html#row-controls\">Always Loot / Never Loot controls</a>, effective Spell Damage on <a href=\"combat.html#throw-stone\">Throw Stone</a>, and retained spell gems after normal death were added.</li></ul><p>Release labels describe availability, not completed balance or gameplay acceptance. See <a href=\"unreleased.html\">In development</a> for candidates.</p>\n\n</div></details><h2 id=\"earlier-guide-notices\">Earlier release detail</h2><p>Notices previously repeated across guides are retained below for their original context. Use the current guides for today’s instructions.</p><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Ascension quest: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"ascension--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear — live testing</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is installed for live testing. Scaling uses 131 researched Legendary items and matching standard EverQuest baselines. Classic level 50 and starter progression are preserved. Reopen the normal launcher for game 2026101902 before testing. See <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open testing limits</a>.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Combat, buffs &amp; recovery: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p class=\"notice\"><a href=\"build-lab.html\">Try the experimental Build Lab</a> to compare stat changes and test spell priorities against explicit combat assumptions. Full gear, AA and pet effects are not automatically modeled.</p>\n<h2 id=\"combat--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear — live testing</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is installed for live testing. Scaling uses 131 researched Legendary items and matching standard EverQuest baselines. Classic level 50 and starter progression are preserved. Reopen the normal launcher for game 2026101902 before testing. See <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open testing limits</a>.</p><p>The update makes Improved Damage, Improved Healing, Mana Preservation, Reagent Conservation and Hate Adjustment use their strongest endpoints. Improved Damage is multiplied by 10, with explicit Mage exceptions: Heart of Flame 100% and Fire Core 150%. Damage focuses limited to single-target spells can affect supported area targets while retaining their other restrictions. Bard damage-focus songs keep their random ranges; direct-damage focuses gain 10× while DoT focuses do not. Bard songs receive no spell focus or twincast, and their 3-second base cast becomes 2.5 seconds. These interpretations require playtesting.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live AA testing:</strong> All 16 classes have more earned AA options: 75 newly available lines, 111 expanded lines and Druid access to Healing Boon. No existing line is removed. Classic remains level 50. Reconnect and turn Recommended AA off to browse your held classes. <a href=\"multiclass.html#all-class-aa\">Read the AA update</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> Direct Spell Damage, ordinary DoT ticks, heroic INT/WIS, pet healing and held-class melee effects have changed. Update through the launcher before testing. Spell-rank choice, mana sustain and burst balance still need player checks.</p>\n<h2 id=\"combat--cooldown-corrections\">Cooldown duration repairs</h2><p>Reuse reductions no longer create extremely long lockouts on item clicks, Mend, Bash, Frenzy and linked spells. Fully reduced cooldowns stay ready instead of restarting old timers on affected skills and AA completion paths. Ordinary reuse and effects that intentionally add time remain. Shared spell and discipline content groups, generic basic attacks, and Begging/Pick Pockets remain under investigation. This live update does not clear existing saved timers.</p>\n<h2 id=\"combat--blessing-repair\">Blessing effects that survive reconnects</h2><p>Repairs restore saved buff effects after login and stop permanent blessings expiring on the next tick. You should not need another hail for ordinary blessings. Old nonexpiring XP boosts now receive a minimal countdown on load; positive remaining timers are retained. Player retesting continues.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Raid &amp; Grind dungeons: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"dungeon-modes--hole-entrance\">The Hole entrance</h2><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing — keyless Hole entrance:</strong> The Hole Key and lock-picking requirement have been removed from the entrance rock in Paineel at <code>/loc 568,-896,-96</code>. Click the rock to open the passage without a key or lock picks. The server update is installed; in-game acceptance is pending. Paineel city-lift keys and the Sacred Key doors inside The Hole remain unchanged.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\" id=\"dungeon-modes--hate-commonlands-candidate\"><strong>Live testing — Hate Keeper in Commonlands:</strong> Find the Plane of Hate Keeper in East Commonlands at <code>/loc -1570,-346,3</code>, between Mirielle and Khalure in the travel area. Raid, Grind and return entry lead to Hate; private Hate instances retain an entrance Keeper. Public and private Hate entry require level 46; GM status is no longer required. The server update is installed. The owner confirmed the relocation, Commonlands visibility and Hate travel. Broader dungeon balance and full-clear QA remain separate.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing — every Classic dungeon:</strong> The installed release extends Raid, Grind, Enter, Join, Status, Claim Rewards and Reset to 21 Classic combat dungeons, including Fear, Hate and Sky. All 21 dungeons and their new rewards are installed for testing. In-game and balance acceptance are pending.</p>\n<h2 id=\"dungeon-modes--classic-candidate\">Every Classic dungeon — live testing</h2><p><strong>Live testing.</strong> Added zones: blackburrow, crushbone, runnyeye, soldunga, guktop, gukbottom, mistmoore, kedge, paw, hole, qcat, fearplane, hateplane, airplane. Current native populations are retained; this is not a historical restoration of every zone. Runs keep the existing twelve-hour limit and personal credit requirements.</p><p>Added Raid final bosses receive three dungeon-specific exclusive designs in Polished and Ascended versions. All dungeon rewards are MAGIC; existing item IDs and other stats remain unchanged. Managed Sky adds durable key exchangers on each key island, still requiring the normal tokens. Managed Grind gives the four previously scripted Sky bosses eight-hour timers and preserves the princess’s four-hour timer. Public and legacy Sky retain their original behavior. Plane runs isolate their quest state from public zones and other runs.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Keeper placement — live testing:</strong> The overlapping Keepers in Befallen, Unrest, Najena, Permafrost and Nagafen’s Lair now have positions 15 units from their waypoints. High Keep and Cazic-Thule already had separate positions and remain unchanged. Visibility is not yet confirmed in game. If an eye is still hidden, use <code>/target Instance_Keeper</code> and hail. Waypoints and dungeon progress are unchanged.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Dungeon</th><th>Keeper /loc</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Befallen</td><td><code>-67,35,3.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Unrest</td><td><code>-38,67,3.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Najena</td><td><code>-61,858,4.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Permafrost</td><td><code>-121,46,2.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Nagafen’s Lair</td><td><code>-424,-248,-108</code></td></tr><tr><td>High Keep (unchanged)</td><td><code>-16,88,4</code></td></tr><tr><td>Cazic-Thule (unchanged)</td><td><code>71,-74,4</code></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> Selected dungeon equipment budgets are raised so comparable Normal rewards exceed Ascended starter gear. Modes, objectives, Keepers and eligibility remain unchanged.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Raid and Grind dungeon modes</a> are available from all 21 dungeon Keepers. Existing legacy runs keep their original behavior until expiry or reset. Gameplay and balance acceptance remain open.</p><p>Raid and Grind choices are available in all 21 Classic combat dungeons listed here, including Fear, Hate and Sky. Each run lasts twelve hours and allows up to six characters. Testing and balance acceptance remain open.</p>\n<h2 id=\"dungeon-modes--unique-rewards\">Unique Classic raid rewards — live testing</h2><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> The <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> give every dungeon three exclusive designs. The 14 added dungeons contribute 42 designs in two qualities; all 414 dungeon rewards are MAGIC. Fear, Hate and Sky receive lore-driven relics and equipped utility clicks. Gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p><p>New recommended levels follow each dungeon’s equipment band. Planar items require level 46. All remain permanent, tradeable, non-LORE, zero-resale and outside existing forging recipes. The original seven exclusive families remain, with MAGIC added where needed. Already earned rewards and generated loot keep their identities.</p><p>New numeric power stays within the existing band, slot and quality budgets. Their lore is original Nightcap fiction inspired by each dungeon. Each family has Polished and Ascended versions.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Dungeon / band</th><th>Exclusive designs</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>blackburrow / 20</td><td>Elgnub&#x27;s Burrowfang<br>Blackburrow Packwarden Mantle<br>Brewer&#x27;s Amber Seal</td></tr><tr><td>crushbone / 20</td><td>Crush&#x27;s Broken Scepter<br>Ambassador&#x27;s Ashen Veil<br>Liberator of the Pens</td></tr><tr><td>runnyeye / 30</td><td>Pickclaw Tunnelbreaker<br>Evil Eye Witness<br>Crown of the Pickclaw Court</td></tr><tr><td>soldunga / 40</td><td>Goblin King&#x27;s Cinderstaff<br>Firebloom Forgegrips<br>Embervault Reliquary</td></tr><tr><td>guktop / 30</td><td>Shinlord&#x27;s Oathblade<br>Heart of the Living Guk<br>Reedwoven Watcher Boots</td></tr><tr><td>gukbottom / 50</td><td>Ghoul Lord&#x27;s Last Decree<br>Pall of the Silent Court<br>Seal of Released Souls</td></tr><tr><td>mistmoore / 40</td><td>Xicotl&#x27;s Midnight Talon<br>Mistmoore Bloodless Gorget<br>Echo of the Unfinished Waltz</td></tr><tr><td>kedge / 50</td><td>Phinigel&#x27;s Tidebound Trident<br>Pearl of the Drowned Chorus<br>Kedge Deepcurrent Robe</td></tr><tr><td>paw / 40</td><td>Ishva&#x27;s Splitpaw Knuckles<br>Splitpaw Spiritcord<br>Denfather Stoneguard</td></tr><tr><td>hole / 50</td><td>Wretched Stonecleaver<br>Pael Sealed Memory<br>Earthbound Oathplate</td></tr><tr><td>qcat / 20</td><td>Omorb&#x27;s Sluicefang<br>Catacomb Vigil Lantern<br>Qeynos Underway Satchel</td></tr><tr><td>fearplane / 50</td><td>Spine of the Faceless<br>Visage of Unbroken Will<br>Dreadhusk of the Last Stand</td></tr><tr><td>hateplane / 50</td><td>Innoruuk&#x27;s Severed Covenant<br>Maestro&#x27;s Unfinished Requiem<br>Seal of the First Betrayal</td></tr><tr><td>airplane / 50</td><td>Veeshan&#x27;s Unwritten Horizon<br>Mantle of the First Brood<br>Astrolabe of the Eighth Island</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Planar relics</h3><p><strong>Fear:</strong> Visage of Unbroken Will reveals the unseen with See Invisible, beside Spine of the Faceless and Dreadhusk of the Last Stand. Its reuse is five minutes.</p><p><strong>Hate:</strong> Maestro’s Unfinished Requiem grants Invisibility; Innoruuk’s Severed Covenant and Seal of the First Betrayal recall hatred and broken elven royalty. Its reuse is ten minutes.</p><p><strong>Sky:</strong> Astrolabe of the Eighth Island grants ordinary Levitate, beside Veeshan’s Unwritten Horizon and Mantle of the First Brood. Its reuse is fifteen minutes. Levitate requires one Bat Wing and respects no-levitation zones, including Sky itself; island keys are still required.</p><p>Each click requires equipping the item at level 46 and a ten-second cast. Both qualities and duplicate copies share the same family cooldown; Ascended does not improve the utility. Cast/reuse figures are base values subject to native focus reductions. Native targeting, reagent conservation and spell restrictions remain.</p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Equipment &amp; trading: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"equipment--loot-finder-preview\">Find ordinary equipment</h2><p>Use the <a href=\"loot-finder.html\">loot finder</a> to match your held classes and locate database-dropped equipment within the active era. Each item shows source mobs, zones, spawn locations and calculated drop chances, including ordinary quality upgrades. The <a href=\"items.html\">Hunt catalog</a> and dungeon guides cover their separate reward systems.</p><p class=\"notice\"><a href=\"build-lab.html\">Try the experimental Build Lab</a> to compare stat changes and test spell priorities against explicit combat assumptions. Full gear, AA and pet effects are not automatically modeled.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> The <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> give every dungeon three exclusive designs. The 14 added dungeons contribute 42 designs in two qualities; all 414 dungeon rewards are MAGIC. Fear, Hate and Sky receive lore-driven relics and equipped utility clicks. Gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p>\n<h2 id=\"equipment--quest-ingredients\">Quest ingredient qualities - live testing</h2><p>Normal-item quest requirements accept Polished, Exalted and Ascended versions of the same item. Shakrn Meadowgreen in South Karana accepts an Aviak Charm of any ordinary quality plus two Star Rubies for Ascended Crafted Gauntlets, following the current class-armor reward policy. Ingredients are consumed; their quality does not upgrade the configured reward. Exact Normal inputs are used first when both are offered. Explicit quality requirements, reforging recipes and separate epic, hunt and dungeon catalogs retain their own rules. Quest hand-ins and task delivery support the change; in-game acceptance testing remains open.</p>\n<h2 id=\"equipment--classic-robes\">Classic race robes — live testing</h2><p>Game update 2026102204 repairs the native model binding behind the waist gap reported on Barbarian and Half Elf. The earlier 2026102203 update did not resolve that gap. The correction covers male and female Half Elves, Wood Elves, Barbarians, Dwarves, Trolls, Ogres and Halflings. Close EverQuest completely, reopen the normal launcher and press Play to update. Other players also need the update to see the corrected models. Equipment eligibility and item stats remain unchanged. Native waist, dye and animation acceptance is still pending.</p>\n<h2 id=\"equipment--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear — live testing</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is installed for live testing. Scaling uses 131 researched Legendary items and matching standard EverQuest baselines. Classic level 50 and starter progression are preserved. Reopen the normal launcher for game 2026101902 before testing. See <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open testing limits</a>.</p><p>The update uses unmodified stock ProjectEQ as an approximation of standard EverQuest, then preserves the exact researched values where available. It changes 143,332 existing tier definitions across 47,809 eligible ordinary families. Normal items, the 209 starter families, custom Hunt/dungeon rewards, augment families and quest-only epics keep their existing treatment. Families that exceed native stat limits are excluded for review.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Ascended field</th><th>Candidate target from stock</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Positive AC, HP, mana, primary stats, resists, weapon damage and HP/mana regeneration</td><td>2×</td></tr><tr><td>Haste</td><td>1.5×, rounded</td></tr><tr><td>Spell Damage when stock has none</td><td>Higher of 2× INT or WIS</td></tr><tr><td>Healing Amount when stock has none</td><td>2× WIS</td></tr><tr><td>Accuracy when stock has none</td><td>Half DEX, rounded upward</td></tr><tr><td>New heroics</td><td>Quarter of the final matching stat, rounded; Ascended only</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Polished and Exalted receive one-third and two-thirds of the increase from Normal to Ascended. These intermediate formulas and extrapolation beyond the screenshots are Nightcap tuning choices. Attack and sparse utility fields use stock values unless an exact observed override applies. Existing effects, sockets, delays, equip rules, loot routes and owned items are preserved.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> Selected Ascended items now use reviewed THJ values, including reductions. Starter upgrades remain modest and comparable Normal dungeon gear is stronger. Spell Damage and Healing Amount have 750 base caps, plus earned Hunt headroom.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><a href=\"items.html\"><strong>Browse the equipment catalog →</strong></a> Find a reward by slot, required level or source zone, with all four qualities grouped together.</p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Features: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"features--hole-entrance\">The Hole entrance</h2><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing — keyless Hole entrance:</strong> The Hole Key and lock-picking requirement have been removed from the entrance rock in Paineel at <code>/loc 568,-896,-96</code>. Click the rock to open the passage without a key or lock picks. The server update is installed; in-game acceptance is pending. Paineel city-lift keys and the Sacred Key doors inside The Hole remain unchanged.</p>\n<h2 id=\"features--loot-finder-preview\">Plan equipment for your classes</h2><p>The <a href=\"loot-finder.html\">loot finder</a> matches equipment usable by any held class, with an optional all-selected-classes mode, active-era filtering and source mobs, locations and calculated drop chances. Production content refreshes automatically every fifteen minutes. This tool does not change loot or equipment rules.</p><p class=\"notice\" id=\"features--hate-commonlands-candidate\"><strong>Live testing — Hate Keeper in Commonlands:</strong> Find the Plane of Hate Keeper in East Commonlands at <code>/loc -1570,-346,3</code>, between Mirielle and Khalure in the travel area. Raid, Grind and return entry lead to Hate; private Hate instances retain an entrance Keeper. Public and private Hate entry require level 46; GM status is no longer required. The server update is installed. The owner confirmed the relocation, Commonlands visibility and Hate travel. Broader dungeon balance and full-clear QA remain separate.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><a href=\"build-lab.html\">Try the experimental Build Lab</a> to compare stat changes and test spell priorities against explicit combat assumptions. Full gear, AA and pet effects are not automatically modeled.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> The <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> give every dungeon three exclusive designs. The 14 added dungeons contribute 42 designs in two qualities; all 414 dungeon rewards are MAGIC. Fear, Hate and Sky receive lore-driven relics and equipped utility clicks. Gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#classic-candidate\">Every Classic dungeon coverage</a> adds the same Raid/Grind choices in 21 combat dungeon zones, including Fear, Hate and Sky. All 21 are installed for live testing; gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p>\n<h2 id=\"features--quest-ingredients-candidate\">Quest ingredient qualities - live testing</h2><p>Better ordinary qualities can satisfy Normal quest ingredients, including the Aviak Charm for Crafted Gauntlets. The quest keeps its configured reward. See <a href=\"equipment.html#quest-ingredients\">ingredient rules and limits</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> Five reviewed class-armor families now give <a href=\"unreleased.html#quest-quality\">guaranteed Ascended rewards</a>. Substantial repeatable quests qualify; cheap/basic hand-ins remain excluded.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> Game update 2026102204 repairs the native waist binding in the robe bodies added for seven Classic races. Item power and held-class equipment access are unchanged. Native visual acceptance remains open. <a href=\"equipment.html#classic-robes\">Robe update</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Level-scaled AA — live testing:</strong> Earn two AA per level while leveling. From level 1, use the AA +/− buttons to choose 0–100%; 100% pauses leveling so you can grind AA where you prefer. Close EverQuest and update through launcher Play for game 2026102301. Existing points, purchases and partial progress stay intact. <a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">AA progression and examples</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"features--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear — live testing</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is installed for live testing. Scaling uses 131 researched Legendary items and matching standard EverQuest baselines. Classic level 50 and starter progression are preserved. Reopen the normal launcher for game 2026101902 before testing. See <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open testing limits</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live AA testing:</strong> All 16 classes have more earned AA options: 75 newly available lines, 111 expanded lines and Druid access to Healing Boon. The latest custom behavior update retires Spell Casting Subtlety and obsolete Silent Casting modifiers, with recorded-cost refunds. Classic remains level 50. Reconnect and turn Recommended AA off to browse your held classes. <a href=\"multiclass.html#all-class-aa\">Read the AA update</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> The combined item, spell, pet equipment and melee release is installed for live testing. It preserves Classic level 50 and earned progression. See the updated combat, equipment and pet guides below.</p>\n<p>Ordinary eligible equipment and bags have a 20% Polished, 5% Exalted and 1% Ascended chance per drop. <a href=\"equipment.html#item-tiers\">Read the loot quality rules</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"feature-intro\">The major departures from Classic, with the rules you need before your next adventure. Start with a topic below, then follow its guide for requirements and limits.</p><p class=\"notice\">These systems are deployed for live testing. Balance and some gameplay checks remain ongoing. <a href=\"unreleased.html\">In development</a> lists work that is not yet available.</p><h2 id=\"features--character\">Build one character from three classes</h2><div class=\"feature-list\"><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Three classes from level 1</h3><div><p>Keep your starting class and choose two different extra classes. Your held classes shape spell access, equipment, skills, and base health and mana.</p><a href=\"multiclass.html#three-classes\">Choose your classes →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>AA progression from the beginning</h3><div><p>Allowed AA ranks open at level 1. With AA allocation at 0%, earn full leveling XP plus two AA per level. The AA +/− controls work from level 1; choose 100% to pause leveling and focus on AA. Points and prerequisites still matter.</p><a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">Understand AA progression →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Scribe spells ahead of time</h3><div><p>Eligible scrolls can enter your spellbook early. Memorizing and casting still require the normal level for a class you hold.</p><a href=\"multiclass.html#spell-access\">Learn the spell rules →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>A roster of companions</h3><div><p>Multiple summoned pets, selected-pet or All-pets commands, and stored pet armor support a multiclass roster.</p><a href=\"pets.html\">Manage your pets →</a></div></section></div><h2 id=\"features--rewards\">Earn, trade and upgrade your gear</h2><div class=\"feature-list\"><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Stronger item qualities and zone rewards</h3><div><p>Ordinary tiered gear and the 48-zone reward hunt offer distinct quality families. Hunt augments fit six armor locations and add heroic stats.</p><a href=\"zone-hunt.html\">Explore rewards and sockets →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Turn duplicates into upgrades</h3><div><p>Use three Base zone rewards for Polished, then four matching copies for each higher step. Veyra’s reusable box also upgrades eligible ordinary Polished and Exalted items. The box also accepts <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#normal-items\">three identical eligible Normal/Base copies for Polished</a>.</p><a href=\"item-upgrades.html\">See the upgrade recipes →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Free trading and no LORE limit</h3><div><p>Trade formerly restricted and attuned items and keep duplicate LORE items. Inventory space, temporary lifetime and other item rules still apply.</p><a href=\"equipment.html#free-trade\">Read trading and resale rules →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Equipment for your held classes</h3><div><p>Wear ordinary equipment allowed by any held class, regardless of playable race. Other restrictions, including slot, level and deity, remain.</p><a href=\"multiclass.html#equipment-access\">Check equipment eligibility →</a></div></section></div><h2 id=\"features--adventuring\">Prepare in the tunnel, then explore</h2><div class=\"feature-list\"><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Raid or Grind in all 21 Classic dungeons</h3><div><p>Choose normal respawning enemies or harder enemies with permanent deaths. Earn personal boss-checklist rewards; Raid final bosses add exclusive loot.</p><a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Choose your dungeon mode →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>A shared home base</h3><div><p>New characters start with a kit and 100 platinum in the East Commonlands tunnel. Trainers, spell shops, supplies, banking, buffs and travel services are gathered there.</p><a href=\"tunnel.html\">Meet the tunnel services →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Travel, discovery and private dungeons</h3><div><p>Use tunnel travel services, discover waypoint destinations and enter supported personal dungeon instances. Ancient Attunement recalls you home without changing your bind.</p><a href=\"travel.html\">Plan your journey →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Lasting blessings; temporary combat abilities</h3><div><p>Ordinary beneficial blessings persist on players and owned pets. Temporary AA effects, disciplines and short-duration effects retain their timers.</p><a href=\"combat.html#buffs\">Know which effects last →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Keep fighting while you cast</h3><div><p>Damage-over-time spells cast instantly, and melee autoattacks can continue during casting. Mana costs, reuse, resistance and control effects still matter.</p><a href=\"combat.html#casting\">Read the combat changes →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Less upkeep between adventures</h3><div><p>Food and drink are optional. Normal death retains EXP, level, AA progress, carried equipment, inventory, money and memorized spell gems; beneficial buffs are lost. Preparation, earned gear and encounter execution still matter.</p><a href=\"combat.html\">Read combat and recovery →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Healing without changing your target</h3><div><p>Ordinary heals can heal your own permanent pet. With an enemy selected, eligible heals still redirect to you. Specialized spells retain their target rules.</p><a href=\"combat.html#healing\">Check healing targets →</a></div></section></div><h2 id=\"features--tools\">Spend more time playing</h2><div class=\"feature-list\"><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Stacked materials and Craft All</h3><div><p>Stackable items support at least 100, preserving larger limits. Use stacks without manually splitting every ingredient. Repeat a recipe with Craft All while retaining normal recipe requirements, success chances and skill gains.</p><a href=\"tradeskills.html\">Use the crafting controls →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Advanced loot and bulk selling</h3><div><p>Use personal loot queues, loot preferences and group rolls. Sell All keeps bags and casting supplies; bank valuable gear before selling.</p><a href=\"advanced-loot.html\">Learn the loot interface →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>One launcher, current updates</h3><div><p>The normal Nightcap shortcut delivers managed game/interface updates and dated patch summaries. Keep your existing folder and personal settings.</p><a href=\"launcher.html\">Update before playing →</a></div></section></div><h2 id=\"features--updates\">Keep up with changes</h2><p>Read <a href=\"recent-changes.html\">Recent changes</a> for dated updates. Each release review covers affected guides, commands, item and zone pages, and this Features overview together.</p><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Raid and Grind dungeon modes</a> are available from all 21 dungeon Keepers. Existing legacy runs keep their original behavior until expiry or reset. Gameplay and balance acceptance remain open.</p>\n\n\n<h2 id=\"features--october-improvements\">More guidance and independent attacks</h2><p>The optional <a href=\"multiclass.html#recommended-aa\">Recommended AA filter</a> helps you choose early survival and damage upgrades. <a href=\"combat.html#monk-cooldowns\">Six basic Monk attacks have separate cooldowns</a>, and <a href=\"combat.html#cooldown-corrections\">cooldown duration repairs</a> prevent several excessive lockouts. <a href=\"combat.html#ability-cooldowns\">Activated AA families now keep separate cooldowns</a>, including Rampage and Purify Body. Gameplay and balance checks continue.</p>\n<h2 id=\"features--thj-scaling\">Item and spell progression</h2><p><a href=\"equipment.html#reviewed-ascended\">Reviewed Ascended items</a>, modest starter upgrades and stronger dungeon budgets bring item progression closer to the observed THJ references. <a href=\"combat.html#spell-scaling\">Additive Spell Damage and direct heroic-stat bonuses</a>, <a href=\"pets.html#pet-armor\">paged pet equipment</a> and <a href=\"combat.html#melee-builds\">earned shield/melee synergies</a> are installed together. Player combat and balance checks remain open.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"features--chapterhouse-candidate\">The Vigil of the Dawn — live testing</h2><p>Camil’s level-50 Paladin story in Chapterhouse uses native Tasks, persistent personal chapters and a one-time helmet claim. Custom enemies and encounter mechanics support a demanding capstone, with era-curated rewards. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> and <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a>.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Getting started: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Level-scaled AA — live testing:</strong> Earn two AA per level while leveling. From level 1, use the AA +/− buttons to choose 0–100%; 100% pauses leveling so you can grind AA where you prefer. Close EverQuest and update through launcher Play for game 2026102301. Existing points, purchases and partial progress stay intact. <a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">AA progression and examples</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"getting-started--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear — live testing</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is installed for live testing. Scaling uses 131 researched Legendary items and matching standard EverQuest baselines. Classic level 50 and starter progression are preserved. Reopen the normal launcher for game 2026101902 before testing. See <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open testing limits</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> Starter equipment now has modest quality upgrades. For approved starter weapons, each quality adds one damage while delay stays fixed. Comparable Normal dungeon equipment remains the next meaningful step.</p>\n<h2 id=\"getting-started--travel-files\">Repair missing Classic zone files</h2><p>Use the usual launcher Play flow for the <a href=\"launcher.html#zone-repair\">Classic travel archive repair</a>. Do not extract an older full client update over your settings.</p>\n<p>Nightcap is a solo-preferred progression server: thoughtful preparation, earned gear and encounter execution matter. Friends are welcome. The current chapter is <strong>Classic</strong>, with a <strong>level cap of 50</strong>.</p>\n<p><a href=\"features.html\"><strong>Read Features first</strong></a> for the major ways Nightcap differs from Classic.</p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Welcome to the Nightcap Wiki: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"index--hole-entrance\">The Hole entrance</h2><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing — keyless Hole entrance:</strong> The Hole Key and lock-picking requirement have been removed from the entrance rock in Paineel at <code>/loc 568,-896,-96</code>. Click the rock to open the passage without a key or lock picks. The server update is installed; in-game acceptance is pending. Paineel city-lift keys and the Sacred Key doors inside The Hole remain unchanged.</p>\n<h2 id=\"index--loot-finder-preview\">Find your next upgrade</h2><p>Choose up to three held classes and find current-era equipment, its source mobs, locations and calculated drop chances. <a href=\"loot-finder.html\">Open the loot finder</a>. Production content refreshes automatically every fifteen minutes.</p><p class=\"notice\" id=\"index--hate-commonlands-candidate\"><strong>Live testing — Hate Keeper in Commonlands:</strong> Find the Plane of Hate Keeper in East Commonlands at <code>/loc -1570,-346,3</code>, between Mirielle and Khalure in the travel area. Raid, Grind and return entry lead to Hate; private Hate instances retain an entrance Keeper. Public and private Hate entry require level 46; GM status is no longer required. The server update is installed. The owner confirmed the relocation, Commonlands visibility and Hate travel. Broader dungeon balance and full-clear QA remain separate.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> The <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> give every dungeon three exclusive designs. The 14 added dungeons contribute 42 designs in two qualities; all 414 dungeon rewards are MAGIC. Fear, Hate and Sky receive lore-driven relics and equipped utility clicks. Gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#classic-candidate\">Every Classic dungeon coverage</a> adds the same Raid/Grind choices in 21 combat dungeon zones, including Fear, Hate and Sky. All 21 are installed for live testing; gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p>\n<h2 id=\"index--quest-ingredients-candidate\">Live testing: quest ingredient qualities</h2><p>Quest hand-ins and deliveries now accept Polished, Exalted and Ascended versions of Normal ingredients. <a href=\"equipment.html#quest-ingredients\">Try the Crafted Gauntlets turn-in and review the limits</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> <a href=\"unreleased.html#quest-quality\">Crafted and four other reviewed class-armor families</a> now award Ascended gear. Original quest requirements remain.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> The <a href=\"equipment.html#classic-robes\">Classic robe waist correction</a> is available for seven races in game 2026102204. Close the game and update through the launcher; native visual acceptance remains open.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Level-scaled AA — live testing:</strong> Earn two AA per level while leveling. From level 1, use the AA +/− buttons to choose 0–100%; 100% pauses leveling so you can grind AA where you prefer. Close EverQuest and update through launcher Play for game 2026102301. Existing points, purchases and partial progress stay intact. <a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">AA progression and examples</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"index--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear — live testing</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is installed for live testing. Scaling uses 131 researched Legendary items and matching standard EverQuest baselines. Classic level 50 and starter progression are preserved. Reopen the normal launcher for game 2026101902 before testing. See <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open testing limits</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live AA testing:</strong> All 16 classes have more earned AA options: 75 newly available lines, 111 expanded lines and Druid access to Healing Boon. The latest custom behavior update retires Spell Casting Subtlety and obsolete Silent Casting modifiers, with recorded-cost refunds. Classic remains level 50. Reconnect and turn Recommended AA off to browse your held classes. <a href=\"multiclass.html#all-class-aa\">Read the AA update</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Launch repair published:</strong> Game update 2026101901 corrects the client catalog mismatch that blocked Play after the previous update. Close EverQuest and the launcher, reopen your normal Nightcap shortcut, and press Play to receive the repair. Your game settings and the other managed files are preserved. Native login and gameplay confirmation remain open.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> The item/spell and pet/melee release is available for live testing. Reopen the launcher for the matching client update, then check your gear, spells and pet equipment. Classic level 50 remains active.</p>\n<p>Ordinary loot quality chances are now 20% Polished, 5% Exalted and 1% Ascended per eligible item drop. <a href=\"equipment.html#item-tiers\">Loot quality details</a>.</p><p class=\"notice\"><strong>October 18 update:</strong> <a href=\"combat.html#ability-cooldowns\">Independent AA cooldowns and item/discipline timer repairs</a> are available for live testing. Reconnect before testing; existing waits retain their original expiry.</p><p><strong>October 18:</strong> <a href=\"launcher.html#zone-repair\">Classic travel archive repair</a> is available through normal launcher Play, including West Commonlands. Close EverQuest before updating.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>October 17 update:</strong> <a href=\"multiclass.html#recommended-aa\">Recommended AA</a>, passive AA while leveling, <a href=\"combat.html#death-exp\">no normal-death EXP loss</a>, <a href=\"tradeskills.html#stack-limits\">stacks of at least 100</a>, <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#normal-items\">three-Normal reforging</a> and <a href=\"combat.html#monk-cooldowns\">independent Monk attacks</a> are available for live testing. Close EQ and use launcher Play.</p>\n<div class=\"welcome\"><div class=\"welcome-copy\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">A familiar world. Your own path.</p><h2>Three classes.<br>One more adventure.</h2><p>Find your build, learn the custom systems, and discover what is waiting beyond the tunnel.</p><a class=\"button\" href=\"getting-started.html\">Start your journey →</a></div><img src=\"assets/traders-at-dusk.png\" width=\"1672\" height=\"941\" alt=\"Nightcap traders beneath lanterns in a stone tunnel at dusk.\"></div><div class=\"facts\"><span><strong>Classic</strong> current era</span><span><strong>50</strong> level cap</span><span><strong>3</strong> classes per character</span><span><strong>48</strong> reward zones</span></div><p class=\"feature-entry\"><strong>New to Nightcap?</strong> <a href=\"features.html\">Explore Features — the major changes from Classic →</a></p><div class=\"portal-grid\"><section class=\"portal\"><h2>Character & classes</h2><ul><li><a href=\"multiclass.html\">Multiclass & progression</a><small>Choose your classes, skills and abilities.</small></li><li><a href=\"pets.html\">Pets & pet armor</a><small>Your companions, commands and loadouts.</small></li></ul></section><section class=\"portal\"><h2>Items & equipment</h2><ul><li><a href=\"items.html\">Browse equipment</a><small>Find gear and augments by slot, level and zone.</small></li><li><a href=\"zone-hunt.html\">Zone hunt & forging</a><small>Drop chances, heroic augments and upgrades.</small></li><li><a href=\"equipment.html\">Equipment & trading</a><small>Existing tiers, bags and selling rules.</small></li></ul></section><section class=\"portal\"><h2>Explore the world</h2><ul><li><a href=\"zones.html\">Zones & rewards</a><small>48 Classic destinations and their rewards.</small></li><li><a href=\"tunnel.html\">East Commonlands tunnel</a><small>Trainers, merchants and blessings.</small></li><li><a href=\"travel.html\">Travel & instances</a><small>Find your way out. Find your way home.</small></li></ul></section><section class=\"portal\"><h2>Adventures & quests</h2><ul><li><a href=\"advanced-loot.html\">Advanced loot</a><small>Personal drops, filters and group rolls.</small></li><li><a href=\"ascension.html\">Ascension quest</a><small>Reforge your original class epic.</small></li><li><a href=\"waypoints.html\">Waypoint Explorer</a><small>Discover destinations and earn a title.</small></li></ul></section></div><div class=\"home-columns\"><section><h2>New in Nightcap</h2><p><a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\"><strong>Raid or Grind in all 21 Classic dungeons.</strong></a> Complete personal boss checklists for new rewards, with exclusive Raid drops. Available for live testing.</p><p><strong>Build, craft and upgrade.</strong> Early spell scribing, stacked tradeskills and Craft All, reusable item upgrades, and equipment for your held classes are live. The <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#normal-items\">normal-item box recipe</a> is available for live testing.</p><p>Passive AA is now <strong>10%</strong> alongside normal leveling. <a href=\"recent-changes.html\">Read the latest changes →</a></p></section><section><h2>At the campfire</h2><ul><li><a href=\"commands.html\">Keep the command reference handy</a></li><li><a href=\"launcher.html\">Update your launcher and game</a></li><li><a href=\"combat.html\">Read about combat and recovery</a></li><li><a href=\"unreleased.html\">See what is still in development</a></li></ul><p class=\"notice\">Nightcap is in live testing. Feature labels distinguish installed systems from unreleased work.</p></section></div>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"index--chapterhouse-candidate\">The Vigil of the Dawn — live testing</h2><p>Camil’s Vigil of the Dawn is available for live testing. Begin in East Commonlands with a level-50 character holding Paladin, then visit the Keeper near Befallen in West Commonlands. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> and <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a>.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Item upgrades: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"item-upgrades--quest-ingredients-candidate\">Quest ingredient qualities - live testing</h2><p><a href=\"equipment.html#quest-ingredients\">Ordinary quality variants can satisfy Normal quest requirements</a>. This does not change the number or quality of copies required by the Reforging Box or zone forging.</p>\n<h2 id=\"item-upgrades--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear — live testing</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is installed for live testing. Scaling uses 131 researched Legendary items and matching standard EverQuest baselines. Classic level 50 and starter progression are preserved. Reopen the normal launcher for game 2026101902 before testing. See <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open testing limits</a>.</p><p>The update changes stats on existing ordinary qualities. It does not change forge costs, quality chances, recipes or item ownership. Reforging still uses the existing progression.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> Selected Ascended values and intermediate stats have been retuned while retaining item identities, effects and sockets. Upgrade costs, commands and existing ownership are unchanged.</p>\n<p>Nightcap has two forgeable tier families: ordinary tiered equipment ends at <strong>Ascended</strong>, while the Classic zone-hunt rewards end at <strong>Ascension</strong>. They have separate item definitions. Match the exact item and quality.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Launcher &amp; interface: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"launcher--classic-robes-candidate\">Classic robe waist correction — live testing</h2><p>Game update <strong>2026102204</strong> repairs native model binding on the added Classic robe bodies after the earlier 2026102203 repair failed. Close EverQuest completely, reopen the normal launcher and press Play. The update installs both character archives together; a server reload cannot update local models. Other players also need the update. Native appearance and animation checks remain open. <a href=\"equipment.html#classic-robes\">Affected races and testing status</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Launch repair published:</strong> Game update 2026101901 corrects the client catalog mismatch that blocked Play after the previous update. Close EverQuest and the launcher, reopen your normal Nightcap shortcut, and press Play to receive the repair. Your game settings and the other managed files are preserved. Native login and gameplay confirmation remain open.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> Game update 2026101802 pairs the expanded pet Equipment tab and spell/AA descriptions with the new server release. Close EverQuest and use the normal launcher before testing. The Classic travel repairs remain included.</p>\n<h2 id=\"launcher--zone-repair\">Classic travel file checks</h2><p>Game update 2026101801 adds terrain and object archive checks for 17 Classic travel destinations, including West Commonlands, Misty Thicket and Toxxulia. Fully close EverQuest, reopen your usual launcher, select the game folder you actually use, and press Play. Missing or corrupted managed files are downloaded before the game starts; matching files are reused. Your settings are preserved. This covers the listed managed archives, not every file in a RoF2 installation. Report the exact error if a zone still fails after updating.</p>\n<h2 id=\"launcher--startup-repairs\">Startup and character-selection repairs</h2><p>Updates repair model archives and missing materials behind the recent Play and character-selection failures. Install through the usual launcher; no reinstall is needed.</p>\n<h2 id=\"launcher--animation-repairs\">Creature and pet animation repairs</h2><p>The latest updates repair shared creature animations and Enchanter weapon-pet identity. Beetle walking and death were confirmed fixed; pet motion and wider visual checks continue.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"launcher--october-release\">October 17 gameplay update</h2><p>Close EverQuest and choose Play to receive the Recommended AA window and independent Monk attack timers. Latest update lists these changes with death EXP, stack limits, reforging and reliability improvements. Previous patches retains the dungeon launch notes.</p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Multiclass &amp; progression: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"multiclass--loot-finder-preview\">Search gear for your held classes</h2><p>The <a href=\"loot-finder.html\">loot finder</a> defaults to <em>Any held class</em>, matching Nightcap equipment access. Select up to three classes; use <em>All selected classes</em> when every selected class must appear on the item. Slot, required level, deity and special item rules still apply.</p><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Robe appearance — live testing:</strong> Game update 2026102204 repairs the native robe waist binding for seven Classic races. Close the game and update through the normal launcher. Held-class equipment eligibility stays the same. <a href=\"equipment.html#classic-robes\">Affected races and testing status</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Level-scaled AA — live testing:</strong> Earn two AA per level while leveling. From level 1, use the AA +/− buttons to choose 0–100%; 100% pauses leveling so you can grind AA where you prefer. Close EverQuest and update through launcher Play for game 2026102301. Existing points, purchases and partial progress stay intact. <a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">AA progression and examples</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"multiclass--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear — live testing</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is installed for live testing. Scaling uses 131 researched Legendary items and matching standard EverQuest baselines. Classic level 50 and starter progression are preserved. Reopen the normal launcher for game 2026101902 before testing. See <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open testing limits</a>.</p><p>The AA changes include group Act of Valor, activated 40% Harvest, four percentage-based Mana Burns, universal caster Silent Casting, Warrior attack debuffs, Wizard Pyromancy/Cryomancy and a separate Wizard Dimensional Shielding. Spell Casting Subtlety and obsolete Silent Casting modifiers are retired; recorded purchase costs are refunded once on login. Class ownership, other purchases and starter grants remain intact. Exact uncertain costs and coefficients are listed in the candidate guide.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live AA testing:</strong> All 16 classes have more earned AA options: 75 newly available lines, 111 expanded lines and Druid access to Healing Boon. The latest custom behavior update retires Spell Casting Subtlety and obsolete Silent Casting modifiers, with recorded-cost refunds. Classic remains level 50. Reconnect and turn Recommended AA off to browse your held classes. <a href=\"multiclass.html#all-class-aa\">Read the AA update</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> Reviewed earned pet and melee AA ranks and held-class combat benefits are available for live testing. Normal ownership, costs, prerequisites and skill requirements remain. The active level cap is still 50; the separate Planes of Power profile is not activated.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Pets &amp; pet armor: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"pets--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear — live testing</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is installed for live testing. Scaling uses 131 researched Legendary items and matching standard EverQuest baselines. Classic level 50 and starter progression are preserved. Reopen the normal launcher for game 2026101902 before testing. See <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open testing limits</a>.</p><p>The focus changes apply to players and permanent pets. Temporary pets retain their prior focus behavior. Existing pet/WPM item effects, sockets, equipment rules and access remain intact.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> Permanent pet equipment now has three pages covering 22 locations, with a total budget of 15 items for Mage pets or eight for other permanent class pets. Update through the launcher before opening Equipment.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Travel &amp; instances: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"travel--hole-entrance\">The Hole entrance</h2><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing — keyless Hole entrance:</strong> The Hole Key and lock-picking requirement have been removed from the entrance rock in Paineel at <code>/loc 568,-896,-96</code>. Click the rock to open the passage without a key or lock picks. The server update is installed; in-game acceptance is pending. Paineel city-lift keys and the Sacred Key doors inside The Hole remain unchanged.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\" id=\"travel--hate-commonlands-candidate\"><strong>Live testing — Hate Keeper in Commonlands:</strong> Find the Plane of Hate Keeper in East Commonlands at <code>/loc -1570,-346,3</code>, between Mirielle and Khalure in the travel area. Raid, Grind and return entry lead to Hate; private Hate instances retain an entrance Keeper. Public and private Hate entry require level 46; GM status is no longer required. The server update is installed. The owner confirmed the relocation, Commonlands visibility and Hate travel. Broader dungeon balance and full-clear QA remain separate.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> The <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> give every dungeon three exclusive designs. The 14 added dungeons contribute 42 designs in two qualities; all 414 dungeon rewards are MAGIC. Fear, Hate and Sky receive lore-driven relics and equipped utility clicks. Gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#classic-candidate\">Every Classic dungeon coverage</a> adds the same Raid/Grind choices in 21 combat dungeon zones, including Fear, Hate and Sky. All 21 are installed for live testing; gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Not released:</strong> The separate level-65/Planes of Power profile and its additional merchant stock remain staged. This item/spell release keeps Classic level 50 and the current travel and vendor gates.</p>\n<h2 id=\"travel--missing-zone-files\">If a Classic destination fails to load</h2><p>Close EverQuest and use launcher Play to install game update 2026101801 or newer. The patcher now checks and repairs terrain/object archives for 17 Classic travel destinations, including West Commonlands, Misty Thicket and Toxxulia. Confirm the launcher points to the folder you use. If your character is stuck, contact the owner for a location rescue; retain the exact error if updating does not resolve it. Native travel acceptance is still being checked.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>East Commonlands tunnel: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"tunnel--experience-blessing\">XP blessing retired</h2><p>Magus Goldwind no longer charges platinum or grants the XP package. Speak with Matron Restora for free ordinary buffs. Existing timed XP boosts keep their remaining duration; old nonexpiring copies receive a minimal countdown on login or zoning and fade when buff timers run. Replacement ways to earn boosts are under consideration and are not available yet.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>In development: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p class=\"notice\" id=\"unreleased--hate-commonlands-candidate\"><strong>Live testing — Hate Keeper in Commonlands:</strong> Find the Plane of Hate Keeper in East Commonlands at <code>/loc -1570,-346,3</code>, between Mirielle and Khalure in the travel area. Raid, Grind and return entry lead to Hate; private Hate instances retain an entrance Keeper. Public and private Hate entry require level 46; GM status is no longer required. The server update is installed. The owner confirmed the relocation, Commonlands visibility and Hate travel. Broader dungeon balance and full-clear QA remain separate.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> The <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> give every dungeon three exclusive designs. The 14 added dungeons contribute 42 designs in two qualities; all 414 dungeon rewards are MAGIC. Fear, Hate and Sky receive lore-driven relics and equipped utility clicks. Gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#classic-candidate\">Every Classic dungeon coverage</a> adds the same Raid/Grind choices in 21 combat dungeon zones, including Fear, Hate and Sky. All 21 are installed for live testing; gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--quest-ingredients\">Quest ingredient qualities - live testing</h2><p>The fix for rejection of Aviak Charm (Polished) is deployed. Shared quest hand-ins and task delivery accept ordinary higher-quality variants for Normal requirements. Check completion, missing inputs and returned extras in game; <a href=\"equipment.html#quest-ingredients\">explicit-quality and forging rules remain separate</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--crystal-markers\">Waypoint crystals — live testing</h2><p>Waypoints now have a glowing crystal with the existing <strong>a waypoint</strong> label. Fully close EverQuest, then use the normal launcher’s Play button to install game 2026102202 before testing. The crystal adds a model to the portal effect; appearance in Classic and Modern model modes and with particles low or off still needs in-game checks. Locations, discovery progress and return destinations are unchanged.</p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--classic-robes\">Classic robe waist correction — live testing</h2><p>Game update 2026102204 repairs the native waist binding after the earlier 2026102203 repair failed on Barbarian and Half Elf. It covers the added robe bodies for Half Elf, Wood Elf, Barbarian, Dwarf, Troll, Ogre and Halfling models, both genders. Close the game and update through the normal launcher before testing. Native visual, dye and animation acceptance remains open. Item power, class eligibility and progression remain unchanged. <a href=\"equipment.html#classic-robes\">Update details</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--befallen-keeper\">Dungeon Keeper visibility — live testing</h2><p>The placement correction now covers all five confirmed waypoint overlaps: Befallen, Unrest, Najena, Permafrost and Nagafen’s Lair. High Keep and Cazic-Thule retain their already-separate positions. All seven still need visible-model and direct-selection checks. See the <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Keeper locations</a>; use <code>/target Instance_Keeper</code> and hail if needed. No client update or dungeon reset is required.</p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear — live testing</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is installed for live testing. Scaling uses 131 researched Legendary items and matching standard EverQuest baselines. Classic level 50 and starter progression are preserved. Reopen the normal launcher for game 2026101902 before testing. See <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open testing limits</a>.</p><h3>Custom AA behavior</h3><ul><li>Warlord’s Fury: +100% physical skill damage for up to 12 seconds, 60-second reuse.</li><li>Gut Punch: initial damage and +50% physical damage taken for up to 12 seconds. Press the Attack lowers AC; Grappling Strike lowers evasion. Their unverified opening/debuff values remain explicit tuning choices.</li><li>Act of Valor: spends 50% of maximum mana once and heals nearby group members for 2 HP per mana spent.</li><li>Harvest: activate to restore 40% maximum mana.</li><li>Mana Burn/Blast/Blaze/Volatile Mana Blaze: spend 10/20/30/40% maximum mana; retain 4 damage per mana as a tuning choice. All reach 15-minute reuse with full Hastened Manaburn. Target immunity rejects the cast without mana or cooldown loss.</li><li>Silent Casting: all casting classes, one-hour duration, 60-second reuse, suspendable timer. Subtlety and obsolete haste/duration modifiers refund purchased ranks.</li><li>Dimensional Shielding: separate Wizard AA protecting casting from hits, movement and hostile interrupt effects. Stuns and voluntary cancellation still interrupt. Its 120-second duration and 30-minute reuse are retained-value tuning choices.</li><li>Pyromancy/Cryomancy: 35% proc chance, initial damage plus DoT, opposite-element resistance reduction and compatibility with other buffs. Existing level/mana/trigger restrictions remain.</li></ul><h3>Evidence and testing limits</h3><p>Released THJ notes take precedence over older test notes. “Most” static focuses, endpoint selection, the 10× interpretation and the supported area-target scope require validation. The stock baseline is ProjectEQ, not a recovered THJ or Daybreak database. Five weapon observations support the weapon extrapolation. No level-65 profile, new loot access, automatic AA points or free gear is included. In-game checks must cover mana failures, group healing, refund persistence, song focusing, actual hit damage and gear inspection before gameplay balance is accepted.</p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--all-class-aa\">All-class AAs are now in live testing</h2><p>The rank and access update is installed. See <a href=\"multiclass.html#all-class-aa\">the released AA rules</a>. Additional custom THJ effects are now installed as described above; encounter balance remains open.</p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--thj-parity\">Item and spell scaling is now in live testing</h2><p>The combined release is installed. Read <a href=\"equipment.html\">Equipment</a>, <a href=\"combat.html\">Combat</a> and <a href=\"pets.html\">Pets</a> for its current rules. Historical THJ evidence does not establish every current THJ formula; spell-rank choice, mana sustain, pet contribution and maximum-AA melee burst still need in-game balance checks.</p><h2 id=\"unreleased--wpm-melee\">Shield and melee changes are now in live testing</h2><p>The earned held-class melee and shield changes shipped with the combined release. See <a href=\"combat.html#melee-builds\">the combat guide</a>. Gameplay acceptance remains open.</p><h2 id=\"unreleased--pet-scaling\">Separate level-65 and Planes of Power profile — not released</h2><p>The expanded pet equipment and scaling changes are installed, but the level-65/Planes of Power profile and 389 additional merchant entries are still staged. Classic level 50 remains active. Nothing grants levels, spellbooks, AA points or epics automatically. Manifest Elements keeps its normal Mage level 59 requirement.</p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--quest-quality\">Guaranteed quality for substantial class armor — live testing</h2><p>The installed update grants existing Ascended versions of 37 Crafted, Lambent, Darkforge, Ivy Etched and Totemic quest rewards. Substantial class-armor quests may qualify even when repeatable; cheap/basic hand-ins remain excluded. All original materials, money checks, faction and experience remain. The dependent Shadow Knight epic turn-in accepts Normal or Ascended Darkforge pieces, including mixed sets.</p><p>The 37 reviewed rewards are live. Already-owned items are not automatically converted. Other armor quests require individual review: Armor of Ro finishes through tradeskills, and Temple cleric branches need a separate audit. Materials, returned items, starter gear, spells, epic rewards and unaudited quests are not globally upgraded. Gameplay and progression balance still need in-game testing.</p><h2 id=\"unreleased--cooldown-identities\">Remaining shared skill and spell cooldowns</h2><p>The <a href=\"combat.html#ability-cooldowns\">AA and cross-ability timer correction is deployed for live testing</a>. Content-defined groups, including Harmshield/Cannibalize and Battle Cry/Throw Stone, remain open work. Bash/Slam, Backstab, Frenzy and non-Monk Kick still share a basic attack timer; Begging and Pick Pockets also share reuse. Linked potion/item groups remain. These links are under review; they are not included in the independence correction.</p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--journal\">Adventure Journal &amp; Epic 0.5</h2><p>The eight journal quests and Wayfarer’s Oath charm have been built but are <strong>not installed on the server</strong>. The update uses three shared chapters followed by Guardian, Striker, Arcanist, Warden or Binder paths. These are not available rewards.</p><h2 id=\"unreleased--combat\">Combat and item candidates</h2><p>Broader Monk and Beastlord fist-damage formulas and some existing tiered item corrections have a tested candidate but no recorded deployment. A frozen personal casting bar remains under investigation. The separate <a href=\"multiclass.html#earned-skills\">extra-class skill, trainer and offhand correction</a> is deployed; the reported player issue was confirmed resolved.</p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--testing\">Ongoing checks for deployed features</h2><p>Broader equipment and class combinations, stats, regeneration, ability names and Bard movement/songs still need player checks. Those are acceptance checks for installed systems, not a claim that all of them are unreleased. See <a href=\"features.html\">Features</a> for the available systems.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--chapterhouse-candidate\">The Vigil of the Dawn — live testing</h2><p>The Vigil of the Dawn has moved into live testing. Combat, travel and recovery still require player acceptance; installation is not completed gameplay validation. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> and <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a>.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Waypoint Explorer: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"waypoints--crystal-markers\">Waypoint crystals — live testing</h2><p>Waypoints now have a glowing crystal with the existing <strong>a waypoint</strong> label. Fully close EverQuest, then use the normal launcher’s Play button to install game 2026102202 before testing. The crystal adds a model to the portal effect; appearance in Classic and Modern model modes and with particles low or off still needs in-game checks. Locations, discovery progress and return destinations are unchanged.</p>\n</div></details>\n\n<h2 id=\"paladin-weapon-grip-20261026\">October 26, 2026 — Paladin weapon grips</h2><p><strong>Live testing:</strong> a right-click 1HS/2HS toggle is available for SoulFire, Fiery Avenger and Fiery Defender, including existing quality variants. SoulFire’s Complete Heal click is replaced by the toggle. Native gameplay acceptance remains pending. <a href=\"equipment.html#paladin-weapon-grip\">Grip instructions</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"paladin-grip-repair-20261027\">October27 grip issue and October28 paired repair</h2><p>SoulFire could report 1HS while the client retained a two-handed definition. The paired October28 release supplies the cache repair, assessed weapon stats and direct Ascended rewards for SoulFire, Fiery Avenger and Fiery Defender. The Paladin epic no longer requires essence or platinum, and existing normal Defenders have a free exchange. Other epic recipes and Monk AAs are unchanged. Fully exit EQ and use launcher Play to install release2026102801. Native player acceptance remains open. <a href=\"equipment.html#paladin-weapon-grip\">Stats and grip instructions</a>.</p><h2 id=\"bazaar-ui-repair-20261028\">October28 — missing Bazaar controls</h2><p>The update also corrects a Bazaar XML parsing error that made the entire Nightcap interface fall back to Default. Close EQ completely and update through the launcher. If the character still uses Default afterward, enter <code>/loadskin nightcap 1</code>. Check the Bazaar Sell / My Listings and Advanced Loot controls; visible acceptance remains open.</p>\n<h2 id=\"bazaar-startup-crash-20261028\">October 28: Bazaar startup crash — client hotfix 2026102802</h2><p>Client hotfix 2026102802 corrects missing Bazaar tab borders that caused a crash during world entry. Fully exit EverQuest, reopen the launcher and press Play to update, then retry login and /bazaar. The SoulFire repair remains included. Native login and Bazaar acceptance checks remain open.</p>\n<h2 id=\"hate-layout-20261029\">October 29: Plane of Hate ground-level layout — live testing</h2><p>New Raid and Grind runs from the East Commonlands Keeper now use the newer Hate layout, with Nightcap’s existing encounters, NPC strength, loot, epic items, Hunt drops, experience and completion rewards preserved. Existing unexpired runs remain usable in the original layout. Fully exit EverQuest and update through launcher Play before entering. Player rendering, pathing and balance checks remain open. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#hate-layout-preview\">Entry, landmarks and testing</a>.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"keyless-doors-20261029\">October 29: keyless doors — live testing</h2><p>Keys and lock picks are no longer required for ordinary locked doors throughout existing door content. The update covers 194 doors across 48 zones, including Paineel’s city lift, internal Hole doors, Befallen locks and Plane of Sky transports. Other access rules, items, keyrings and earned progression remain. No client update is required. <a href=\"travel.html#keyless-doors\">Door access and remaining restrictions</a>.</p>\n\n\n<h2 id=\"cast-bar-repair-20261030\">October 30: spell casting bar timing — reported issue resolved</h2><p>Client update <strong>2026103002</strong> corrects casting bars that stayed full until the final instant. Fully exit EverQuest and use launcher Play before testing. Normal server cast times, instant DoTs and Bard timing are unchanged; the Ancient Attunement label repair remains included. The owner confirmed the reported casting-bar issue is fixed. This does not claim completion of every focus or interruption check. <a href=\"launcher.html#cast-bar-repair\">Update instructions</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"hate-boss-placement-20261030\">October 30: Hate boss landmark correction — live testing</h2><p>Corrected the ground-level substitute locations for Maestro, the Hand and Innoruuk to their organ/platform/throne landmarks. Existing saved boss positions move once while preserving health, loot, corpses, kills and respawn timers. The 47 added ordinary spawns and all encounter rewards remain. No client update or run reset is required. Visible gameplay acceptance remains open.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"power-source-training-20261030\">October 30: Power Source item training candidate — Not released</h2><p>A new source candidate adds combat-XP item upgrades while preserving duplicate-item combining. The proposed full path targets 4–8 hours; native verification is underway and gameplay timing remains unaccepted. <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#power-source-training\">Power Source training preview</a>.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"faction-standings-main-20261030\">October30: faction standings — live testing</h2><p><code>#factions</code> now opens your faction standings with white text, numbers and full-range bars. Search by name, page through results or inspect your standing with a targeted NPC faction. No client update is needed; readability and gameplay acceptance remain in testing. <a href=\"commands.html#faction-standings\">Commands and limits</a>.</p>\n",
+  "body": "<h2 id=\"augment-audit-20261106\">November6: zone augments and exotic icons — live testing</h2><p>Augments can drop from any unowned killable NPC in enabled zones, including guards, named enemies, killable merchants and scripted adds. New secondary specialties and gem/crystal icons cover all qualities. Cazic-Thule/newer Hate augment pools enable; both expeditions now roll1.5%. Artwork is approved; gameplay QA remains open. <a href=\"augment-audit.html\">Full list and limits</a>.</p><h2 id=\"hunt-rates-20261101\">November 1: zone augments drop three times as often - live</h2><p>Zone Hunt augments now drop at <strong>1.5%</strong> per eligible kill (was 0.5%), about one per 67 kills. Zone equipment stays at 0.5%, and qualities stay Base 60%, Polished 30%, Exalted 8%, Ascension 2%. Each zone page lists its rates. Chapterhouse and Ashen Compact augments are unchanged. No client update is required. <a href=\"zone-hunt.html#drops\">How drops work</a>.</p><h2 id=\"ssf-20261101\">November 1: solo self-found mode - live testing</h2><p>New level-1 characters can swear a permanent solo self-found oath at the Ancient Chronicler. Self-found characters cannot trade with players, use either Bazaar, parcels, the shared or guild bank, or group or raid with players, and earn no passive AA. No client update is required. Player acceptance remains open. <a href=\"multiclass.html#solo-self-found\">How it works</a>.</p><h2 id=\"hate-density-20261030\">October 30: Plane of Hate density - live testing</h2><p>Server-side checks verified every Grind spawn point and natural respawns, including both Maestro encounters. The installed density update adds 47 ordinary enemies to managed Raid and Grind, preserving current runs and rewards. No client update or run reset is required. Player acceptance remains open. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#hate-layout-preview\">Hate modes and landmarks</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"public-cazic-20261030\">October 30 — public Classic Cazic-Thule restored</h2><p>Restored 188 Classic encounter points in open-world Cazic-Thule, which previously had no eligible combat population under Classic. Khaleid’s route now leads to the restored public encounters. Existing private Raid and Grind runs retain their own population and rewards. No client update is required; gameplay acceptance remains open.</p><p>Hate’s saved Raid population was also checked: every expected point was accounted for by living mobs, recorded kills or the final-boss gate. No Hate mobs were added. New-layout Grind and client visibility remain separate checks.</p><h2 id=\"recall-labels-20261030\">October 30: Commonlands recall labels corrected</h2><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Recall labels corrected (October 30):</strong> Client release 2026103001 restores Ancient Attunement’s name, Nightcap Recall’s hotbutton label and the recall description. Fully exit EverQuest and press Play in the normal launcher to update. Cast time, reuse and bind behavior are unchanged. In-game verification remains open.</p>\n<details class=\"change-entry\" open><summary>October28: Bazaar posting and readable controls — live testing</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Client update2026102803 accepts valid whole-platinum digits in both native text formats, reports unreadable input, and enlarges seller text with light colors. The earlier startup fixes and weapon changes are preserved. The owner confirmed the reported posting issue is resolved, the preview appears and the larger light text is readable. Broader market QA remains separate.</p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" open><summary>October 26: Bazaar seller panel and Paladin grips — live testing</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"bazaar-panel-candidate\">Sell / My Listings controls</h2><p>Client update 2026102601 adds the native Sell / My Listings tab for posting, cancelling owned listings and collecting offline proceeds. The paired server release also includes Paladin weapon grips. Close EverQuest and use launcher Play to update. Native gameplay acceptance remains open. <a href=\"tunnel.html#bazaar-seller-panel\">Panel instructions</a>.</p></div></details><h2 id=\"commonlands-bazaar-20261026\">October 26: Commonlands player bazaar — live testing</h2><p>Persistent player listings, offline seller proceeds and native search/purchase routing are installed in public East Commonlands. No parked auctioneer is required. Native RoF2 search, buying and full seller/buyer acceptance remain open. <a href=\"tunnel.html#player-bazaar\">Market instructions and restrictions</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"october24-coordinated\">October 24 — High Keep rescue, Ashen Compact and aggro corrections</h2><p>New High Keep Raid runs now rescue Osargen. The level-50 Ashen Compact begins with Drazhul and the Keeper in the hidden Everfrost passage before Permafrost. Close EQ and use launcher Play for its helmet appearance. NPC departure cleanup and stationary return-home restoration are corrected; the original Lower Guk bedroom-train report still needs an observed retest. Existing earned progress is retained. Full route, escort, appearance and balance acceptance remain open.</p>\n<h2 id=\"ashen-compact-everfrost\">October 24 — Ashen Compact entrance preview</h2><p>Before the coordinated release above, the <a href=\"ashen-compact.html\">Shadow Knight campaign</a> entrance was moved to the hidden Everfrost passage before Permafrost. Its frostbound crossing and return connect to curated Kael. At that preview stage it was a test candidate; the release above supersedes that availability.</p><h2 id=\"rogue-tome-learning\">October 24 - Multiclass tome learning repaired</h2><p>Eligible tomes can now be learned through any held class, fixing secondary and third-class Rogue learning. Failed right-clicks preserve the original tome; full lists, duplicate entries and failed saves no longer consume it. Discipline use levels and the level-1 AA policy are unchanged. See <a href=\"multiclass.html#learning-tomes\">learning combat disciplines</a> for requirements. Live gameplay acceptance remains under review.</p><h2 id=\"custom-feature-directory\">October 24 — Custom content on Features</h2><p><a href=\"features.html\">Features</a> now groups Raid &amp; Grind dungeons, helmet quests, Zone Hunt, epic reforging, class armor, crafting, exploration and custom character systems. Each entry links to its guide. The Ashen Compact preview is explicitly not released; gameplay, rewards and balance are unchanged.</p><p>Current instructions live in <a href=\"all-pages.html\">Guides</a>. This is the history of releases, improvements and fixes; older entries describe their date and may be superseded.</p><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"wiki-clarity\" open><summary>October 24, 2026 · A clearer wiki</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Features now highlights the major differences from standard EQ. Guides start with useful instructions; fixes and repeated release announcements are collected here. Navigation and text sizes are consistent, and long reference lists expand when needed. Existing tools, gameplay rules, reward values and links are preserved.</p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"hole-entrance\"><summary>October 24 · The Hole entrance</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing — keyless Hole entrance:</strong> The Hole Key and lock-picking requirement have been removed from the entrance rock in Paineel at <code>/loc 568,-896,-96</code>. Click the rock to open the passage without a key or lock picks. The server update is installed; in-game acceptance is pending. Paineel city-lift keys and the Sacred Key doors inside The Hole remain unchanged.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"aa-level-progression\"><summary>October 23: two AA per level and level-1 AA controls</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The paired update is installed for live testing. Keep AA allocation at 0% to earn full leveling XP plus two AA per level. Use the AA +/− controls from level 1, choose an intermediate percentage, or select 100% to hold your level and grind AA. Full focus earns 20 AA per current-level equivalent of XP. Update through launcher Play for game 2026102301. Saved points, purchases and partial progress are retained; native gameplay acceptance remains open.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"chapterhouse-candidate\"><summary>October 23 · The Vigil of the Dawn — live testing</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>October 23: Camil’s Chapterhouse quest, level-50–53 encounters, custom rewards, Ember augment, waypoint and Keeper are deployed for live testing. Native Tasks track the story. Full encounter balance and player acceptance remain open. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> and <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a>.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"loot-finder-preview\"><summary>October 22: production loot finder</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The <a href=\"loot-finder.html\">class and era loot finder</a> supports any held class by default, optional all-class matching, slot/quality/level/zone filters and item links to source mobs, locations and calculated drop chances. Production content refreshes automatically every fifteen minutes, with the last successful capture retained if a refresh fails. Existing gameplay, rewards and acceptance labels are unchanged.</p><p class=\"notice\" id=\"hate-commonlands-candidate\"><strong>Live testing — Hate Keeper in Commonlands:</strong> Find the Plane of Hate Keeper in East Commonlands at <code>/loc -1570,-346,3</code>, between Mirielle and Khalure in the travel area. Raid, Grind and return entry lead to Hate; private Hate instances retain an entrance Keeper. Public and private Hate entry require level 46; GM status is no longer required. The server update is installed. The owner confirmed the relocation, Commonlands visibility and Hate travel. Broader dungeon balance and full-clear QA remain separate.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"build-lab\"><summary>Build Lab — October 22</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The <a href=\"build-lab.html\">experimental Build Lab</a> compares two saved builds, supported spell benefits, Hunt item stat differences and editable ability priorities. Inspect mana and cast timelines or search the best priority order under your test conditions. It uses dated source controls and explicit assumptions, not a complete native combat simulation or universal best-build ranking.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"interactive-handbook\"><summary>October 22 — Your interactive field guide</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The wiki has a new lantern-lit design with four adventure paths, instant quick search, saved guides, light and dark reading modes, and a reading-progress bar. The equipment catalog keeps its filters and all four reward qualities. On the home page, expand <strong>Release notes &amp; live testing</strong> for the existing gameplay notices. <a href=\"about.html#navigation\">Learn the shortcuts and field notes →</a></p><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> The <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> give every dungeon three exclusive designs. The 14 added dungeons contribute 42 designs in two qualities; all 414 dungeon rewards are MAGIC. Fear, Hate and Sky receive lore-driven relics and equipped utility clicks. Gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"classic-dungeons-candidate\"><summary>October 22 — every Classic dungeon and unique rewards live</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#classic-candidate\">Every Classic dungeon coverage</a> adds the same Raid/Grind choices in 21 combat dungeon zones, including Fear, Hate and Sky. All 21 are installed for live testing; gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p>\n<p>The paired release also repairs stale dungeon item checks behind the reported Keeper error and installs durable Sky key services. Existing runs, earned rewards and the latest quest-tier and client updates are preserved. Native gameplay and balance acceptance remain open.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"quest-ingredients-20261022\"><summary>October 22 - quest ingredient fix live for testing</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Polished, Exalted and Ascended ingredients can satisfy Normal quest requirements, including Aviak Charm for Crafted Gauntlets. Shared hand-ins, task delivery and five older Temple quests are covered. The paired server and quest release is deployed; player QA remains open. <a href=\"equipment.html#quest-ingredients\">Scope and limits</a>.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"class-armor-candidate\"><summary>October 22 — Ascended class-armor quest rewards</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Crafted, Lambent, Darkforge, Ivy Etched and Totemic quests now grant 37 reviewed Ascended armor rewards. Substantial repeatable class-armor quests qualify; cheap/basic hand-ins remain excluded. The dependent Darkforge epic turn-in accepts Normal and Ascended pieces. Existing owned gear is not automatically converted. <strong>Live testing:</strong> native delivery and balance acceptance remain open. <a href=\"unreleased.html#quest-quality\">Scope and testing</a>.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"crystal-markers\"><summary>October 22 · Waypoint crystals — live testing</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Waypoints now have a glowing crystal with the existing <strong>a waypoint</strong> label. Fully close EverQuest, then use the normal launcher’s Play button to install game 2026102202 before testing. The crystal adds a model to the portal effect; appearance in Classic and Modern model modes and with particles low or off still needs in-game checks. Locations, discovery progress and return destinations are unchanged.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"classic-robes-20261022\"><summary>October 22 — robe waist correction in live testing</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Game update <strong>2026102204</strong> repairs the native waist binding after the earlier 2026102203 repair failed, covering all seven added Classic robe races and both genders. Close the game, reopen the normal launcher and press Play. In-game visual, dye and animation acceptance remains open. <a href=\"equipment.html#classic-robes\">Read the scope</a>.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"keeper-visibility-20261022\"><summary>October 22 — Dungeon Keeper placement</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The correction now separates Keepers from overlapping waypoints in Befallen, Unrest, Najena, Permafrost and Nagafen’s Lair. High Keep and Cazic-Thule already had separate positions. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">All seven Keeper locations</a> are listed for live testing; visibility remains unconfirmed. Waypoints, dungeon progress and client files are unchanged.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Level-scaled AA — live testing:</strong> Earn two AA per level while leveling. From level 1, use the AA +/− buttons to choose 0–100%; 100% pauses leveling so you can grind AA where you prefer. Close EverQuest and update through launcher Play for game 2026102301. Existing points, purchases and partial progress stay intact. <a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">AA progression and examples</a>.</p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"aa-million-xp\"><summary>October 21: slower AA earning and XP boost retirement</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The October 21 release used 1,000,000 AA experience per point with 10% passive earning; the October 23 level-scaled update supersedes that earning model. Goldwind’s paid package is retired, Matron’s free buffs remain, and XP boost durations are respected. Existing points and purchases remain intact. Live balance testing continues.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"thj-behavior-candidate\"><summary>October 19 · THJ behavior and stock gear — live testing</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is installed for live testing. Scaling uses 131 researched Legendary items and matching standard EverQuest baselines. Classic level 50 and starter progression are preserved. Reopen the normal launcher for game 2026101902 before testing. See <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open testing limits</a>.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"all-class-aa-20261019\"><summary>October 19: all-class AA update</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live AA testing:</strong> All 16 classes have more earned AA options: 75 newly available lines, 111 expanded lines and Druid access to Healing Boon. No existing line is removed. Classic remains level 50. Reconnect and turn Recommended AA off to browse your held classes. <a href=\"multiclass.html#all-class-aa\">Read the AA update</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Launch repair published:</strong> Game update 2026101901 corrects the client catalog mismatch that blocked Play after the previous update. Close EverQuest and the launcher, reopen your normal Nightcap shortcut, and press Play to receive the repair. Your game settings and the other managed files are preserved. Native login and gameplay confirmation remain open.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"thj-release\"><summary>October 18: item, spell, pet and melee release</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p><strong>Live testing:</strong> Selected Ascended items now use reviewed THJ values. Direct damage adds effective Spell Damage, ordinary DoT ticks add half, and heroic INT/WIS improve direct values. Starter quality steps remain modest below comparable Normal dungeon equipment.</p><p>The same release adds paged permanent-pet equipment, bounded owner-stat inheritance, earned pet/melee AA updates, separate Rabid Bear benefit and illusion effects, and shared 750 base caps with Hunt headroom. Close EverQuest and use the launcher for game update 2026101802. Classic level 50 remains active; gameplay and balance acceptance are still open.</p>\n<h2>October 18 - More ordinary quality loot</h2><p>Polished, Exalted and Ascended now have 20%, 5% and 1% chances per eligible ordinary equipment/bag drop. Hunt, dungeon and quest rewards are unchanged. Already generated loot is not rerolled.</p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"reforge-colors\"><summary>October 18, 2026: built-in item colors</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#requirements\">Reforging Box</a> and <a href=\"zone-hunt.html#forging\">zone forging</a> now accept an item's built-in color. This fixes ordinary items such as Dagger of Marnek being rejected as customized. A different player-applied dye color and the other customization restrictions still prevent combining. Recipes remain three Normal/Base copies or four higher-quality copies. No client update is required for this fix; in-game acceptance remains open.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"october-18-cooldowns\"><summary>October 18, 2026: separate ability cooldowns</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p><a href=\"combat.html#ability-cooldowns\">Activated AA families now have independent cooldowns</a>, including Rampage and Purify Body. Item and discipline timer collisions are also repaired. Existing saved waits keep their original expiry. Reconnect and test your abilities; <a href=\"unreleased.html#cooldown-identities\">generic skill and content-defined groups</a> remain under review.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"october-18\"><summary>October 18, 2026: Classic travel file repair</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Signed game update 2026101801 adds automatic missing/corrupt terrain and object archive repair for 17 Classic travel destinations, including West Commonlands, Misty Thicket and Toxxulia. Close EverQuest and press Play in the usual launcher. Existing gameplay assets and player settings are preserved; native zoning acceptance remains open.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"october-17\"><summary>October 17, 2026: progression, combat and crafting</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><ul><li>The optional <a href=\"multiclass.html#recommended-aa\">Recommended AA filter</a> provides an early survival, sustain and damage shortlist across held classes.</li><li>Passive AA is now 10%, preserving full leveling EXP, earned points and 4,000 AA XP per point.</li><li><a href=\"combat.html#monk-cooldowns\">Six basic Monk attacks</a> have separate reuse. <a href=\"combat.html#cooldown-corrections\">Cooldown duration repairs</a> address excessive and restarted timers; other shared identities remain under investigation.</li><li><a href=\"combat.html#death-exp\">Normal death costs no EXP or levels</a>; prior losses are not refunded.</li><li><a href=\"tradeskills.html#stack-limits\">Stackable items support at least 100</a>, retaining larger limits.</li><li>The <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#normal-items\">Reforging Box accepts three identical eligible Normal/Base copies</a> for Polished. Higher recipes still cost four.</li><li>Idle zones can unload without ending their workers and triggering a whole-game restart.</li><li>Update through launcher Play for the matched client. Gameplay and balance acceptance continue.</li></ul>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"october-16\"><summary>October 16, 2026</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><ul><li>The <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#required-bosses\">dungeon guide now lists every required boss</a> and explains boss-stage notices, full-clear credit and Keeper Status when task objectives are blank.</li><li><a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Raid and Grind dungeons</a> are deployed for live testing with personal boss checklists, shared rewards and exclusive Raid drops. Gameplay and balance acceptance remain open.</li><li><a href=\"features.html\">Features</a> now gathers the major departures from Classic.</li><li><a href=\"multiclass.html#equipment-access\">Equipment eligibility</a> recognizes held classes and permits playable races when the class matches; remaining restrictions still apply.</li><li><a href=\"combat.html#buffs\">Temporary AA buffs</a> retain their timers; ordinary blessings remain lasting.</li><li><a href=\"tunnel.html#banking\">Mira Coinwell</a> provides tunnel banking. Haldra stocks Leather Padding.</li><li>The wiki’s guides, commands and generated reward pages have been reviewed together against current release evidence.</li></ul>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"october-13\"><summary>October 13, 2026</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><ul><li><a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">Passive AA changed from 40% to 20%</a>, preserving full normal XP and 4,000 AA XP per point.</li><li><a href=\"multiclass.html#alternate-abilities\">All allowed AA ranks open at level 1</a>; points, eligibility and prerequisite ranks remain.</li><li><a href=\"tradeskills.html\">Stacked tradeskill ingredients and Craft All</a> are deployed.</li><li>The tunnel workshop layout is more spacious; the <a href=\"waypoints.html\">Unrest waypoint</a> moved beside its entrance Keeper.</li><li>Supported divine summoned-hammer families have <a href=\"equipment.html#summoned-gear\">zero resale value</a>.</li><li>The reported multiclass training/offhand issue and merchant Sell All button issue were confirmed resolved.</li></ul>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"october-12\"><summary>October 11–12, 2026</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><ul><li><a href=\"item-upgrades.html\">Reusable four-copy upgrades</a> are available from Artisan Veyra; higher #zoneforge steps now use four copies.</li><li><a href=\"equipment.html#free-trade\">LORE restrictions are disabled</a>. Food and drink requirements were removed.</li><li><a href=\"multiclass.html#spell-access\">Early scribing</a> allows eligible scrolls into the spellbook before their casting level.</li><li><a href=\"equipment.html#selling\">Sell All protects food, drink, reagents and casting focus items</a>.</li><li>The launcher uses personal access codes and shows <a href=\"launcher.html#patch-notes\">patch summaries</a>.</li><li>Waypoint portals and floating-eye Instance Keepers received visual corrections. The reported pet-summon crash was confirmed resolved.</li></ul>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"october-9\"><summary>October 9, 2026</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><ul><li><a href=\"zones.html\">48 Classic reward zones</a>, <a href=\"items.html\">384 reward variants</a>, type-22 augments and zone forging launched.</li><li>Passive AA increased to 40% at that time; the October 13 reduction above supersedes that rate.</li><li><a href=\"advanced-loot.html#row-controls\">Always Loot / Never Loot controls</a>, effective Spell Damage on <a href=\"combat.html#throw-stone\">Throw Stone</a>, and retained spell gems after normal death were added.</li></ul><p>Release labels describe availability, not completed balance or gameplay acceptance. See <a href=\"unreleased.html\">In development</a> for candidates.</p>\n\n</div></details><h2 id=\"earlier-guide-notices\">Earlier release detail</h2><p>Notices previously repeated across guides are retained below for their original context. Use the current guides for today’s instructions.</p><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Ascension quest: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"ascension--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear — live testing</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is installed for live testing. Scaling uses 131 researched Legendary items and matching standard EverQuest baselines. Classic level 50 and starter progression are preserved. Reopen the normal launcher for game 2026101902 before testing. See <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open testing limits</a>.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Combat, buffs &amp; recovery: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p class=\"notice\"><a href=\"build-lab.html\">Try the experimental Build Lab</a> to compare stat changes and test spell priorities against explicit combat assumptions. Full gear, AA and pet effects are not automatically modeled.</p>\n<h2 id=\"combat--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear — live testing</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is installed for live testing. Scaling uses 131 researched Legendary items and matching standard EverQuest baselines. Classic level 50 and starter progression are preserved. Reopen the normal launcher for game 2026101902 before testing. See <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open testing limits</a>.</p><p>The update makes Improved Damage, Improved Healing, Mana Preservation, Reagent Conservation and Hate Adjustment use their strongest endpoints. Improved Damage is multiplied by 10, with explicit Mage exceptions: Heart of Flame 100% and Fire Core 150%. Damage focuses limited to single-target spells can affect supported area targets while retaining their other restrictions. Bard damage-focus songs keep their random ranges; direct-damage focuses gain 10× while DoT focuses do not. Bard songs receive no spell focus or twincast, and their 3-second base cast becomes 2.5 seconds. These interpretations require playtesting.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live AA testing:</strong> All 16 classes have more earned AA options: 75 newly available lines, 111 expanded lines and Druid access to Healing Boon. No existing line is removed. Classic remains level 50. Reconnect and turn Recommended AA off to browse your held classes. <a href=\"multiclass.html#all-class-aa\">Read the AA update</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> Direct Spell Damage, ordinary DoT ticks, heroic INT/WIS, pet healing and held-class melee effects have changed. Update through the launcher before testing. Spell-rank choice, mana sustain and burst balance still need player checks.</p>\n<h2 id=\"combat--cooldown-corrections\">Cooldown duration repairs</h2><p>Reuse reductions no longer create extremely long lockouts on item clicks, Mend, Bash, Frenzy and linked spells. Fully reduced cooldowns stay ready instead of restarting old timers on affected skills and AA completion paths. Ordinary reuse and effects that intentionally add time remain. Shared spell and discipline content groups, generic basic attacks, and Begging/Pick Pockets remain under investigation. This live update does not clear existing saved timers.</p>\n<h2 id=\"combat--blessing-repair\">Blessing effects that survive reconnects</h2><p>Repairs restore saved buff effects after login and stop permanent blessings expiring on the next tick. You should not need another hail for ordinary blessings. Old nonexpiring XP boosts now receive a minimal countdown on load; positive remaining timers are retained. Player retesting continues.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Raid &amp; Grind dungeons: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"dungeon-modes--hole-entrance\">The Hole entrance</h2><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing — keyless Hole entrance:</strong> The Hole Key and lock-picking requirement have been removed from the entrance rock in Paineel at <code>/loc 568,-896,-96</code>. Click the rock to open the passage without a key or lock picks. The server update is installed; in-game acceptance is pending. Paineel city-lift keys and the Sacred Key doors inside The Hole remain unchanged.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\" id=\"dungeon-modes--hate-commonlands-candidate\"><strong>Live testing — Hate Keeper in Commonlands:</strong> Find the Plane of Hate Keeper in East Commonlands at <code>/loc -1570,-346,3</code>, between Mirielle and Khalure in the travel area. Raid, Grind and return entry lead to Hate; private Hate instances retain an entrance Keeper. Public and private Hate entry require level 46; GM status is no longer required. The server update is installed. The owner confirmed the relocation, Commonlands visibility and Hate travel. Broader dungeon balance and full-clear QA remain separate.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing — every Classic dungeon:</strong> The installed release extends Raid, Grind, Enter, Join, Status, Claim Rewards and Reset to 21 Classic combat dungeons, including Fear, Hate and Sky. All 21 dungeons and their new rewards are installed for testing. In-game and balance acceptance are pending.</p>\n<h2 id=\"dungeon-modes--classic-candidate\">Every Classic dungeon — live testing</h2><p><strong>Live testing.</strong> Added zones: blackburrow, crushbone, runnyeye, soldunga, guktop, gukbottom, mistmoore, kedge, paw, hole, qcat, fearplane, hateplane, airplane. Current native populations are retained; this is not a historical restoration of every zone. Runs keep the existing twelve-hour limit and personal credit requirements.</p><p>Added Raid final bosses receive three dungeon-specific exclusive designs in Polished and Ascended versions. All dungeon rewards are MAGIC; existing item IDs and other stats remain unchanged. Managed Sky adds durable key exchangers on each key island, still requiring the normal tokens. Managed Grind gives the four previously scripted Sky bosses eight-hour timers and preserves the princess’s four-hour timer. Public and legacy Sky retain their original behavior. Plane runs isolate their quest state from public zones and other runs.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Keeper placement — live testing:</strong> The overlapping Keepers in Befallen, Unrest, Najena, Permafrost and Nagafen’s Lair now have positions 15 units from their waypoints. High Keep and Cazic-Thule already had separate positions and remain unchanged. Visibility is not yet confirmed in game. If an eye is still hidden, use <code>/target Instance_Keeper</code> and hail. Waypoints and dungeon progress are unchanged.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Dungeon</th><th>Keeper /loc</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Befallen</td><td><code>-67,35,3.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Unrest</td><td><code>-38,67,3.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Najena</td><td><code>-61,858,4.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Permafrost</td><td><code>-121,46,2.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Nagafen’s Lair</td><td><code>-424,-248,-108</code></td></tr><tr><td>High Keep (unchanged)</td><td><code>-16,88,4</code></td></tr><tr><td>Cazic-Thule (unchanged)</td><td><code>71,-74,4</code></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> Selected dungeon equipment budgets are raised so comparable Normal rewards exceed Ascended starter gear. Modes, objectives, Keepers and eligibility remain unchanged.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Raid and Grind dungeon modes</a> are available from all 21 dungeon Keepers. Existing legacy runs keep their original behavior until expiry or reset. Gameplay and balance acceptance remain open.</p><p>Raid and Grind choices are available in all 21 Classic combat dungeons listed here, including Fear, Hate and Sky. Each run lasts twelve hours and allows up to six characters. Testing and balance acceptance remain open.</p>\n<h2 id=\"dungeon-modes--unique-rewards\">Unique Classic raid rewards — live testing</h2><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> The <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> give every dungeon three exclusive designs. The 14 added dungeons contribute 42 designs in two qualities; all 414 dungeon rewards are MAGIC. Fear, Hate and Sky receive lore-driven relics and equipped utility clicks. Gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p><p>New recommended levels follow each dungeon’s equipment band. Planar items require level 46. All remain permanent, tradeable, non-LORE, zero-resale and outside existing forging recipes. The original seven exclusive families remain, with MAGIC added where needed. Already earned rewards and generated loot keep their identities.</p><p>New numeric power stays within the existing band, slot and quality budgets. Their lore is original Nightcap fiction inspired by each dungeon. Each family has Polished and Ascended versions.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Dungeon / band</th><th>Exclusive designs</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>blackburrow / 20</td><td>Elgnub&#x27;s Burrowfang<br>Blackburrow Packwarden Mantle<br>Brewer&#x27;s Amber Seal</td></tr><tr><td>crushbone / 20</td><td>Crush&#x27;s Broken Scepter<br>Ambassador&#x27;s Ashen Veil<br>Liberator of the Pens</td></tr><tr><td>runnyeye / 30</td><td>Pickclaw Tunnelbreaker<br>Evil Eye Witness<br>Crown of the Pickclaw Court</td></tr><tr><td>soldunga / 40</td><td>Goblin King&#x27;s Cinderstaff<br>Firebloom Forgegrips<br>Embervault Reliquary</td></tr><tr><td>guktop / 30</td><td>Shinlord&#x27;s Oathblade<br>Heart of the Living Guk<br>Reedwoven Watcher Boots</td></tr><tr><td>gukbottom / 50</td><td>Ghoul Lord&#x27;s Last Decree<br>Pall of the Silent Court<br>Seal of Released Souls</td></tr><tr><td>mistmoore / 40</td><td>Xicotl&#x27;s Midnight Talon<br>Mistmoore Bloodless Gorget<br>Echo of the Unfinished Waltz</td></tr><tr><td>kedge / 50</td><td>Phinigel&#x27;s Tidebound Trident<br>Pearl of the Drowned Chorus<br>Kedge Deepcurrent Robe</td></tr><tr><td>paw / 40</td><td>Ishva&#x27;s Splitpaw Knuckles<br>Splitpaw Spiritcord<br>Denfather Stoneguard</td></tr><tr><td>hole / 50</td><td>Wretched Stonecleaver<br>Pael Sealed Memory<br>Earthbound Oathplate</td></tr><tr><td>qcat / 20</td><td>Omorb&#x27;s Sluicefang<br>Catacomb Vigil Lantern<br>Qeynos Underway Satchel</td></tr><tr><td>fearplane / 50</td><td>Spine of the Faceless<br>Visage of Unbroken Will<br>Dreadhusk of the Last Stand</td></tr><tr><td>hateplane / 50</td><td>Innoruuk&#x27;s Severed Covenant<br>Maestro&#x27;s Unfinished Requiem<br>Seal of the First Betrayal</td></tr><tr><td>airplane / 50</td><td>Veeshan&#x27;s Unwritten Horizon<br>Mantle of the First Brood<br>Astrolabe of the Eighth Island</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Planar relics</h3><p><strong>Fear:</strong> Visage of Unbroken Will reveals the unseen with See Invisible, beside Spine of the Faceless and Dreadhusk of the Last Stand. Its reuse is five minutes.</p><p><strong>Hate:</strong> Maestro’s Unfinished Requiem grants Invisibility; Innoruuk’s Severed Covenant and Seal of the First Betrayal recall hatred and broken elven royalty. Its reuse is ten minutes.</p><p><strong>Sky:</strong> Astrolabe of the Eighth Island grants ordinary Levitate, beside Veeshan’s Unwritten Horizon and Mantle of the First Brood. Its reuse is fifteen minutes. Levitate requires one Bat Wing and respects no-levitation zones, including Sky itself; island keys are still required.</p><p>Each click requires equipping the item at level 46 and a ten-second cast. Both qualities and duplicate copies share the same family cooldown; Ascended does not improve the utility. Cast/reuse figures are base values subject to native focus reductions. Native targeting, reagent conservation and spell restrictions remain.</p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Equipment &amp; trading: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"equipment--loot-finder-preview\">Find ordinary equipment</h2><p>Use the <a href=\"loot-finder.html\">loot finder</a> to match your held classes and locate database-dropped equipment within the active era. Each item shows source mobs, zones, spawn locations and calculated drop chances, including ordinary quality upgrades. The <a href=\"items.html\">Hunt catalog</a> and dungeon guides cover their separate reward systems.</p><p class=\"notice\"><a href=\"build-lab.html\">Try the experimental Build Lab</a> to compare stat changes and test spell priorities against explicit combat assumptions. Full gear, AA and pet effects are not automatically modeled.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> The <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> give every dungeon three exclusive designs. The 14 added dungeons contribute 42 designs in two qualities; all 414 dungeon rewards are MAGIC. Fear, Hate and Sky receive lore-driven relics and equipped utility clicks. Gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p>\n<h2 id=\"equipment--quest-ingredients\">Quest ingredient qualities - live testing</h2><p>Normal-item quest requirements accept Polished, Exalted and Ascended versions of the same item. Shakrn Meadowgreen in South Karana accepts an Aviak Charm of any ordinary quality plus two Star Rubies for Ascended Crafted Gauntlets, following the current class-armor reward policy. Ingredients are consumed; their quality does not upgrade the configured reward. Exact Normal inputs are used first when both are offered. Explicit quality requirements, reforging recipes and separate epic, hunt and dungeon catalogs retain their own rules. Quest hand-ins and task delivery support the change; in-game acceptance testing remains open.</p>\n<h2 id=\"equipment--classic-robes\">Classic race robes — live testing</h2><p>Game update 2026102204 repairs the native model binding behind the waist gap reported on Barbarian and Half Elf. The earlier 2026102203 update did not resolve that gap. The correction covers male and female Half Elves, Wood Elves, Barbarians, Dwarves, Trolls, Ogres and Halflings. Close EverQuest completely, reopen the normal launcher and press Play to update. Other players also need the update to see the corrected models. Equipment eligibility and item stats remain unchanged. Native waist, dye and animation acceptance is still pending.</p>\n<h2 id=\"equipment--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear — live testing</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is installed for live testing. Scaling uses 131 researched Legendary items and matching standard EverQuest baselines. Classic level 50 and starter progression are preserved. Reopen the normal launcher for game 2026101902 before testing. See <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open testing limits</a>.</p><p>The update uses unmodified stock ProjectEQ as an approximation of standard EverQuest, then preserves the exact researched values where available. It changes 143,332 existing tier definitions across 47,809 eligible ordinary families. Normal items, the 209 starter families, custom Hunt/dungeon rewards, augment families and quest-only epics keep their existing treatment. Families that exceed native stat limits are excluded for review.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Ascended field</th><th>Candidate target from stock</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Positive AC, HP, mana, primary stats, resists, weapon damage and HP/mana regeneration</td><td>2×</td></tr><tr><td>Haste</td><td>1.5×, rounded</td></tr><tr><td>Spell Damage when stock has none</td><td>Higher of 2× INT or WIS</td></tr><tr><td>Healing Amount when stock has none</td><td>2× WIS</td></tr><tr><td>Accuracy when stock has none</td><td>Half DEX, rounded upward</td></tr><tr><td>New heroics</td><td>Quarter of the final matching stat, rounded; Ascended only</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Polished and Exalted receive one-third and two-thirds of the increase from Normal to Ascended. These intermediate formulas and extrapolation beyond the screenshots are Nightcap tuning choices. Attack and sparse utility fields use stock values unless an exact observed override applies. Existing effects, sockets, delays, equip rules, loot routes and owned items are preserved.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> Selected Ascended items now use reviewed THJ values, including reductions. Starter upgrades remain modest and comparable Normal dungeon gear is stronger. Spell Damage and Healing Amount have 750 base caps, plus earned Hunt headroom.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><a href=\"items.html\"><strong>Browse the equipment catalog →</strong></a> Find a reward by slot, required level or source zone, with all four qualities grouped together.</p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Features: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"features--hole-entrance\">The Hole entrance</h2><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing — keyless Hole entrance:</strong> The Hole Key and lock-picking requirement have been removed from the entrance rock in Paineel at <code>/loc 568,-896,-96</code>. Click the rock to open the passage without a key or lock picks. The server update is installed; in-game acceptance is pending. Paineel city-lift keys and the Sacred Key doors inside The Hole remain unchanged.</p>\n<h2 id=\"features--loot-finder-preview\">Plan equipment for your classes</h2><p>The <a href=\"loot-finder.html\">loot finder</a> matches equipment usable by any held class, with an optional all-selected-classes mode, active-era filtering and source mobs, locations and calculated drop chances. Production content refreshes automatically every fifteen minutes. This tool does not change loot or equipment rules.</p><p class=\"notice\" id=\"features--hate-commonlands-candidate\"><strong>Live testing — Hate Keeper in Commonlands:</strong> Find the Plane of Hate Keeper in East Commonlands at <code>/loc -1570,-346,3</code>, between Mirielle and Khalure in the travel area. Raid, Grind and return entry lead to Hate; private Hate instances retain an entrance Keeper. Public and private Hate entry require level 46; GM status is no longer required. The server update is installed. The owner confirmed the relocation, Commonlands visibility and Hate travel. Broader dungeon balance and full-clear QA remain separate.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><a href=\"build-lab.html\">Try the experimental Build Lab</a> to compare stat changes and test spell priorities against explicit combat assumptions. Full gear, AA and pet effects are not automatically modeled.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> The <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> give every dungeon three exclusive designs. The 14 added dungeons contribute 42 designs in two qualities; all 414 dungeon rewards are MAGIC. Fear, Hate and Sky receive lore-driven relics and equipped utility clicks. Gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#classic-candidate\">Every Classic dungeon coverage</a> adds the same Raid/Grind choices in 21 combat dungeon zones, including Fear, Hate and Sky. All 21 are installed for live testing; gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p>\n<h2 id=\"features--quest-ingredients-candidate\">Quest ingredient qualities - live testing</h2><p>Better ordinary qualities can satisfy Normal quest ingredients, including the Aviak Charm for Crafted Gauntlets. The quest keeps its configured reward. See <a href=\"equipment.html#quest-ingredients\">ingredient rules and limits</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> Five reviewed class-armor families now give <a href=\"unreleased.html#quest-quality\">guaranteed Ascended rewards</a>. Substantial repeatable quests qualify; cheap/basic hand-ins remain excluded.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> Game update 2026102204 repairs the native waist binding in the robe bodies added for seven Classic races. Item power and held-class equipment access are unchanged. Native visual acceptance remains open. <a href=\"equipment.html#classic-robes\">Robe update</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Level-scaled AA — live testing:</strong> Earn two AA per level while leveling. From level 1, use the AA +/− buttons to choose 0–100%; 100% pauses leveling so you can grind AA where you prefer. Close EverQuest and update through launcher Play for game 2026102301. Existing points, purchases and partial progress stay intact. <a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">AA progression and examples</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"features--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear — live testing</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is installed for live testing. Scaling uses 131 researched Legendary items and matching standard EverQuest baselines. Classic level 50 and starter progression are preserved. Reopen the normal launcher for game 2026101902 before testing. See <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open testing limits</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live AA testing:</strong> All 16 classes have more earned AA options: 75 newly available lines, 111 expanded lines and Druid access to Healing Boon. The latest custom behavior update retires Spell Casting Subtlety and obsolete Silent Casting modifiers, with recorded-cost refunds. Classic remains level 50. Reconnect and turn Recommended AA off to browse your held classes. <a href=\"multiclass.html#all-class-aa\">Read the AA update</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> The combined item, spell, pet equipment and melee release is installed for live testing. It preserves Classic level 50 and earned progression. See the updated combat, equipment and pet guides below.</p>\n<p>Ordinary eligible equipment and bags have a 20% Polished, 5% Exalted and 1% Ascended chance per drop. <a href=\"equipment.html#item-tiers\">Read the loot quality rules</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"feature-intro\">The major departures from Classic, with the rules you need before your next adventure. Start with a topic below, then follow its guide for requirements and limits.</p><p class=\"notice\">These systems are deployed for live testing. Balance and some gameplay checks remain ongoing. <a href=\"unreleased.html\">In development</a> lists work that is not yet available.</p><h2 id=\"features--character\">Build one character from three classes</h2><div class=\"feature-list\"><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Three classes from level 1</h3><div><p>Keep your starting class and choose two different extra classes. Your held classes shape spell access, equipment, skills, and base health and mana.</p><a href=\"multiclass.html#three-classes\">Choose your classes →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>AA progression from the beginning</h3><div><p>Allowed AA ranks open at level 1. With AA allocation at 0%, earn full leveling XP plus two AA per level. The AA +/− controls work from level 1; choose 100% to pause leveling and focus on AA. Points and prerequisites still matter.</p><a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">Understand AA progression →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Scribe spells ahead of time</h3><div><p>Eligible scrolls can enter your spellbook early. Memorizing and casting still require the normal level for a class you hold.</p><a href=\"multiclass.html#spell-access\">Learn the spell rules →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>A roster of companions</h3><div><p>Multiple summoned pets, selected-pet or All-pets commands, and stored pet armor support a multiclass roster.</p><a href=\"pets.html\">Manage your pets →</a></div></section></div><h2 id=\"features--rewards\">Earn, trade and upgrade your gear</h2><div class=\"feature-list\"><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Stronger item qualities and zone rewards</h3><div><p>Ordinary tiered gear and the 48-zone reward hunt offer distinct quality families. Hunt augments fit six armor locations and add heroic stats.</p><a href=\"zone-hunt.html\">Explore rewards and sockets →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Turn duplicates into upgrades</h3><div><p>Use three Base zone rewards for Polished, then four matching copies for each higher step. Veyra’s reusable box also upgrades eligible ordinary Polished and Exalted items. The box also accepts <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#normal-items\">three identical eligible Normal/Base copies for Polished</a>.</p><a href=\"item-upgrades.html\">See the upgrade recipes →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Free trading and no LORE limit</h3><div><p>Trade formerly restricted and attuned items and keep duplicate LORE items. Inventory space, temporary lifetime and other item rules still apply.</p><a href=\"equipment.html#free-trade\">Read trading and resale rules →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Equipment for your held classes</h3><div><p>Wear ordinary equipment allowed by any held class, regardless of playable race. Other restrictions, including slot, level and deity, remain.</p><a href=\"multiclass.html#equipment-access\">Check equipment eligibility →</a></div></section></div><h2 id=\"features--adventuring\">Prepare in the tunnel, then explore</h2><div class=\"feature-list\"><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Raid or Grind in all 21 Classic dungeons</h3><div><p>Choose normal respawning enemies or harder enemies with permanent deaths. Earn personal boss-checklist rewards; Raid final bosses add exclusive loot.</p><a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Choose your dungeon mode →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>A shared home base</h3><div><p>New characters start with a kit and 100 platinum in the East Commonlands tunnel. Trainers, spell shops, supplies, banking, buffs and travel services are gathered there.</p><a href=\"tunnel.html\">Meet the tunnel services →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Travel, discovery and private dungeons</h3><div><p>Use tunnel travel services, discover waypoint destinations and enter supported personal dungeon instances. Ancient Attunement recalls you home without changing your bind.</p><a href=\"travel.html\">Plan your journey →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Lasting blessings; temporary combat abilities</h3><div><p>Ordinary beneficial blessings persist on players and owned pets. Temporary AA effects, disciplines and short-duration effects retain their timers.</p><a href=\"combat.html#buffs\">Know which effects last →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Keep fighting while you cast</h3><div><p>Damage-over-time spells cast instantly, and melee autoattacks can continue during casting. Mana costs, reuse, resistance and control effects still matter.</p><a href=\"combat.html#casting\">Read the combat changes →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Less upkeep between adventures</h3><div><p>Food and drink are optional. Normal death retains EXP, level, AA progress, carried equipment, inventory, money and memorized spell gems; beneficial buffs are lost. Preparation, earned gear and encounter execution still matter.</p><a href=\"combat.html\">Read combat and recovery →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Healing without changing your target</h3><div><p>Ordinary heals can heal your own permanent pet. With an enemy selected, eligible heals still redirect to you. Specialized spells retain their target rules.</p><a href=\"combat.html#healing\">Check healing targets →</a></div></section></div><h2 id=\"features--tools\">Spend more time playing</h2><div class=\"feature-list\"><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Stacked materials and Craft All</h3><div><p>Stackable items support at least 100, preserving larger limits. Use stacks without manually splitting every ingredient. Repeat a recipe with Craft All while retaining normal recipe requirements, success chances and skill gains.</p><a href=\"tradeskills.html\">Use the crafting controls →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Advanced loot and bulk selling</h3><div><p>Use personal loot queues, loot preferences and group rolls. Sell All keeps bags and casting supplies; bank valuable gear before selling.</p><a href=\"advanced-loot.html\">Learn the loot interface →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>One launcher, current updates</h3><div><p>The normal Nightcap shortcut delivers managed game/interface updates and dated patch summaries. Keep your existing folder and personal settings.</p><a href=\"launcher.html\">Update before playing →</a></div></section></div><h2 id=\"features--updates\">Keep up with changes</h2><p>Read <a href=\"recent-changes.html\">Recent changes</a> for dated updates. Each release review covers affected guides, commands, item and zone pages, and this Features overview together.</p><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Raid and Grind dungeon modes</a> are available from all 21 dungeon Keepers. Existing legacy runs keep their original behavior until expiry or reset. Gameplay and balance acceptance remain open.</p>\n\n\n<h2 id=\"features--october-improvements\">More guidance and independent attacks</h2><p>The optional <a href=\"multiclass.html#recommended-aa\">Recommended AA filter</a> helps you choose early survival and damage upgrades. <a href=\"combat.html#monk-cooldowns\">Six basic Monk attacks have separate cooldowns</a>, and <a href=\"combat.html#cooldown-corrections\">cooldown duration repairs</a> prevent several excessive lockouts. <a href=\"combat.html#ability-cooldowns\">Activated AA families now keep separate cooldowns</a>, including Rampage and Purify Body. Gameplay and balance checks continue.</p>\n<h2 id=\"features--thj-scaling\">Item and spell progression</h2><p><a href=\"equipment.html#reviewed-ascended\">Reviewed Ascended items</a>, modest starter upgrades and stronger dungeon budgets bring item progression closer to the observed THJ references. <a href=\"combat.html#spell-scaling\">Additive Spell Damage and direct heroic-stat bonuses</a>, <a href=\"pets.html#pet-armor\">paged pet equipment</a> and <a href=\"combat.html#melee-builds\">earned shield/melee synergies</a> are installed together. Player combat and balance checks remain open.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"features--chapterhouse-candidate\">The Vigil of the Dawn — live testing</h2><p>Camil’s level-50 Paladin story in Chapterhouse uses native Tasks, persistent personal chapters and a one-time helmet claim. Custom enemies and encounter mechanics support a demanding capstone, with era-curated rewards. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> and <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a>.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Getting started: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Level-scaled AA — live testing:</strong> Earn two AA per level while leveling. From level 1, use the AA +/− buttons to choose 0–100%; 100% pauses leveling so you can grind AA where you prefer. Close EverQuest and update through launcher Play for game 2026102301. Existing points, purchases and partial progress stay intact. <a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">AA progression and examples</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"getting-started--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear — live testing</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is installed for live testing. Scaling uses 131 researched Legendary items and matching standard EverQuest baselines. Classic level 50 and starter progression are preserved. Reopen the normal launcher for game 2026101902 before testing. See <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open testing limits</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> Starter equipment now has modest quality upgrades. For approved starter weapons, each quality adds one damage while delay stays fixed. Comparable Normal dungeon equipment remains the next meaningful step.</p>\n<h2 id=\"getting-started--travel-files\">Repair missing Classic zone files</h2><p>Use the usual launcher Play flow for the <a href=\"launcher.html#zone-repair\">Classic travel archive repair</a>. Do not extract an older full client update over your settings.</p>\n<p>Nightcap is a solo-preferred progression server: thoughtful preparation, earned gear and encounter execution matter. Friends are welcome. The current chapter is <strong>Classic</strong>, with a <strong>level cap of 50</strong>.</p>\n<p><a href=\"features.html\"><strong>Read Features first</strong></a> for the major ways Nightcap differs from Classic.</p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Welcome to the Nightcap Wiki: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"index--hole-entrance\">The Hole entrance</h2><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing — keyless Hole entrance:</strong> The Hole Key and lock-picking requirement have been removed from the entrance rock in Paineel at <code>/loc 568,-896,-96</code>. Click the rock to open the passage without a key or lock picks. The server update is installed; in-game acceptance is pending. Paineel city-lift keys and the Sacred Key doors inside The Hole remain unchanged.</p>\n<h2 id=\"index--loot-finder-preview\">Find your next upgrade</h2><p>Choose up to three held classes and find current-era equipment, its source mobs, locations and calculated drop chances. <a href=\"loot-finder.html\">Open the loot finder</a>. Production content refreshes automatically every fifteen minutes.</p><p class=\"notice\" id=\"index--hate-commonlands-candidate\"><strong>Live testing — Hate Keeper in Commonlands:</strong> Find the Plane of Hate Keeper in East Commonlands at <code>/loc -1570,-346,3</code>, between Mirielle and Khalure in the travel area. Raid, Grind and return entry lead to Hate; private Hate instances retain an entrance Keeper. Public and private Hate entry require level 46; GM status is no longer required. The server update is installed. The owner confirmed the relocation, Commonlands visibility and Hate travel. Broader dungeon balance and full-clear QA remain separate.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> The <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> give every dungeon three exclusive designs. The 14 added dungeons contribute 42 designs in two qualities; all 414 dungeon rewards are MAGIC. Fear, Hate and Sky receive lore-driven relics and equipped utility clicks. Gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#classic-candidate\">Every Classic dungeon coverage</a> adds the same Raid/Grind choices in 21 combat dungeon zones, including Fear, Hate and Sky. All 21 are installed for live testing; gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p>\n<h2 id=\"index--quest-ingredients-candidate\">Live testing: quest ingredient qualities</h2><p>Quest hand-ins and deliveries now accept Polished, Exalted and Ascended versions of Normal ingredients. <a href=\"equipment.html#quest-ingredients\">Try the Crafted Gauntlets turn-in and review the limits</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> <a href=\"unreleased.html#quest-quality\">Crafted and four other reviewed class-armor families</a> now award Ascended gear. Original quest requirements remain.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> The <a href=\"equipment.html#classic-robes\">Classic robe waist correction</a> is available for seven races in game 2026102204. Close the game and update through the launcher; native visual acceptance remains open.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Level-scaled AA — live testing:</strong> Earn two AA per level while leveling. From level 1, use the AA +/− buttons to choose 0–100%; 100% pauses leveling so you can grind AA where you prefer. Close EverQuest and update through launcher Play for game 2026102301. Existing points, purchases and partial progress stay intact. <a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">AA progression and examples</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"index--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear — live testing</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is installed for live testing. Scaling uses 131 researched Legendary items and matching standard EverQuest baselines. Classic level 50 and starter progression are preserved. Reopen the normal launcher for game 2026101902 before testing. See <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open testing limits</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live AA testing:</strong> All 16 classes have more earned AA options: 75 newly available lines, 111 expanded lines and Druid access to Healing Boon. The latest custom behavior update retires Spell Casting Subtlety and obsolete Silent Casting modifiers, with recorded-cost refunds. Classic remains level 50. Reconnect and turn Recommended AA off to browse your held classes. <a href=\"multiclass.html#all-class-aa\">Read the AA update</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Launch repair published:</strong> Game update 2026101901 corrects the client catalog mismatch that blocked Play after the previous update. Close EverQuest and the launcher, reopen your normal Nightcap shortcut, and press Play to receive the repair. Your game settings and the other managed files are preserved. Native login and gameplay confirmation remain open.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> The item/spell and pet/melee release is available for live testing. Reopen the launcher for the matching client update, then check your gear, spells and pet equipment. Classic level 50 remains active.</p>\n<p>Ordinary loot quality chances are now 20% Polished, 5% Exalted and 1% Ascended per eligible item drop. <a href=\"equipment.html#item-tiers\">Loot quality details</a>.</p><p class=\"notice\"><strong>October 18 update:</strong> <a href=\"combat.html#ability-cooldowns\">Independent AA cooldowns and item/discipline timer repairs</a> are available for live testing. Reconnect before testing; existing waits retain their original expiry.</p><p><strong>October 18:</strong> <a href=\"launcher.html#zone-repair\">Classic travel archive repair</a> is available through normal launcher Play, including West Commonlands. Close EverQuest before updating.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>October 17 update:</strong> <a href=\"multiclass.html#recommended-aa\">Recommended AA</a>, passive AA while leveling, <a href=\"combat.html#death-exp\">no normal-death EXP loss</a>, <a href=\"tradeskills.html#stack-limits\">stacks of at least 100</a>, <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#normal-items\">three-Normal reforging</a> and <a href=\"combat.html#monk-cooldowns\">independent Monk attacks</a> are available for live testing. Close EQ and use launcher Play.</p>\n<div class=\"welcome\"><div class=\"welcome-copy\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">A familiar world. Your own path.</p><h2>Three classes.<br>One more adventure.</h2><p>Find your build, learn the custom systems, and discover what is waiting beyond the tunnel.</p><a class=\"button\" href=\"getting-started.html\">Start your journey →</a></div><img src=\"assets/traders-at-dusk.png\" width=\"1672\" height=\"941\" alt=\"Nightcap traders beneath lanterns in a stone tunnel at dusk.\"></div><div class=\"facts\"><span><strong>Classic</strong> current era</span><span><strong>50</strong> level cap</span><span><strong>3</strong> classes per character</span><span><strong>48</strong> reward zones</span></div><p class=\"feature-entry\"><strong>New to Nightcap?</strong> <a href=\"features.html\">Explore Features — the major changes from Classic →</a></p><div class=\"portal-grid\"><section class=\"portal\"><h2>Character & classes</h2><ul><li><a href=\"multiclass.html\">Multiclass & progression</a><small>Choose your classes, skills and abilities.</small></li><li><a href=\"pets.html\">Pets & pet armor</a><small>Your companions, commands and loadouts.</small></li></ul></section><section class=\"portal\"><h2>Items & equipment</h2><ul><li><a href=\"items.html\">Browse equipment</a><small>Find gear and augments by slot, level and zone.</small></li><li><a href=\"zone-hunt.html\">Zone hunt & forging</a><small>Drop chances, heroic augments and upgrades.</small></li><li><a href=\"equipment.html\">Equipment & trading</a><small>Existing tiers, bags and selling rules.</small></li></ul></section><section class=\"portal\"><h2>Explore the world</h2><ul><li><a href=\"zones.html\">Zones & rewards</a><small>48 Classic destinations and their rewards.</small></li><li><a href=\"tunnel.html\">East Commonlands tunnel</a><small>Trainers, merchants and blessings.</small></li><li><a href=\"travel.html\">Travel & instances</a><small>Find your way out. Find your way home.</small></li></ul></section><section class=\"portal\"><h2>Adventures & quests</h2><ul><li><a href=\"advanced-loot.html\">Advanced loot</a><small>Personal drops, filters and group rolls.</small></li><li><a href=\"ascension.html\">Ascension quest</a><small>Reforge your original class epic.</small></li><li><a href=\"waypoints.html\">Waypoint Explorer</a><small>Discover destinations and earn a title.</small></li></ul></section></div><div class=\"home-columns\"><section><h2>New in Nightcap</h2><p><a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\"><strong>Raid or Grind in all 21 Classic dungeons.</strong></a> Complete personal boss checklists for new rewards, with exclusive Raid drops. Available for live testing.</p><p><strong>Build, craft and upgrade.</strong> Early spell scribing, stacked tradeskills and Craft All, reusable item upgrades, and equipment for your held classes are live. The <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#normal-items\">normal-item box recipe</a> is available for live testing.</p><p>Passive AA is now <strong>10%</strong> alongside normal leveling. <a href=\"recent-changes.html\">Read the latest changes →</a></p></section><section><h2>At the campfire</h2><ul><li><a href=\"commands.html\">Keep the command reference handy</a></li><li><a href=\"launcher.html\">Update your launcher and game</a></li><li><a href=\"combat.html\">Read about combat and recovery</a></li><li><a href=\"unreleased.html\">See what is still in development</a></li></ul><p class=\"notice\">Nightcap is in live testing. Feature labels distinguish installed systems from unreleased work.</p></section></div>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"index--chapterhouse-candidate\">The Vigil of the Dawn — live testing</h2><p>Camil’s Vigil of the Dawn is available for live testing. Begin in East Commonlands with a level-50 character holding Paladin, then visit the Keeper near Befallen in West Commonlands. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> and <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a>.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Item upgrades: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"item-upgrades--quest-ingredients-candidate\">Quest ingredient qualities - live testing</h2><p><a href=\"equipment.html#quest-ingredients\">Ordinary quality variants can satisfy Normal quest requirements</a>. This does not change the number or quality of copies required by the Reforging Box or zone forging.</p>\n<h2 id=\"item-upgrades--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear — live testing</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is installed for live testing. Scaling uses 131 researched Legendary items and matching standard EverQuest baselines. Classic level 50 and starter progression are preserved. Reopen the normal launcher for game 2026101902 before testing. See <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open testing limits</a>.</p><p>The update changes stats on existing ordinary qualities. It does not change forge costs, quality chances, recipes or item ownership. Reforging still uses the existing progression.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> Selected Ascended values and intermediate stats have been retuned while retaining item identities, effects and sockets. Upgrade costs, commands and existing ownership are unchanged.</p>\n<p>Nightcap has two forgeable tier families: ordinary tiered equipment ends at <strong>Ascended</strong>, while the Classic zone-hunt rewards end at <strong>Ascension</strong>. They have separate item definitions. Match the exact item and quality.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Launcher &amp; interface: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"launcher--classic-robes-candidate\">Classic robe waist correction — live testing</h2><p>Game update <strong>2026102204</strong> repairs native model binding on the added Classic robe bodies after the earlier 2026102203 repair failed. Close EverQuest completely, reopen the normal launcher and press Play. The update installs both character archives together; a server reload cannot update local models. Other players also need the update. Native appearance and animation checks remain open. <a href=\"equipment.html#classic-robes\">Affected races and testing status</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Launch repair published:</strong> Game update 2026101901 corrects the client catalog mismatch that blocked Play after the previous update. Close EverQuest and the launcher, reopen your normal Nightcap shortcut, and press Play to receive the repair. Your game settings and the other managed files are preserved. Native login and gameplay confirmation remain open.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> Game update 2026101802 pairs the expanded pet Equipment tab and spell/AA descriptions with the new server release. Close EverQuest and use the normal launcher before testing. The Classic travel repairs remain included.</p>\n<h2 id=\"launcher--zone-repair\">Classic travel file checks</h2><p>Game update 2026101801 adds terrain and object archive checks for 17 Classic travel destinations, including West Commonlands, Misty Thicket and Toxxulia. Fully close EverQuest, reopen your usual launcher, select the game folder you actually use, and press Play. Missing or corrupted managed files are downloaded before the game starts; matching files are reused. Your settings are preserved. This covers the listed managed archives, not every file in a RoF2 installation. Report the exact error if a zone still fails after updating.</p>\n<h2 id=\"launcher--startup-repairs\">Startup and character-selection repairs</h2><p>Updates repair model archives and missing materials behind the recent Play and character-selection failures. Install through the usual launcher; no reinstall is needed.</p>\n<h2 id=\"launcher--animation-repairs\">Creature and pet animation repairs</h2><p>The latest updates repair shared creature animations and Enchanter weapon-pet identity. Beetle walking and death were confirmed fixed; pet motion and wider visual checks continue.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"launcher--october-release\">October 17 gameplay update</h2><p>Close EverQuest and choose Play to receive the Recommended AA window and independent Monk attack timers. Latest update lists these changes with death EXP, stack limits, reforging and reliability improvements. Previous patches retains the dungeon launch notes.</p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Multiclass &amp; progression: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"multiclass--loot-finder-preview\">Search gear for your held classes</h2><p>The <a href=\"loot-finder.html\">loot finder</a> defaults to <em>Any held class</em>, matching Nightcap equipment access. Select up to three classes; use <em>All selected classes</em> when every selected class must appear on the item. Slot, required level, deity and special item rules still apply.</p><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Robe appearance — live testing:</strong> Game update 2026102204 repairs the native robe waist binding for seven Classic races. Close the game and update through the normal launcher. Held-class equipment eligibility stays the same. <a href=\"equipment.html#classic-robes\">Affected races and testing status</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Level-scaled AA — live testing:</strong> Earn two AA per level while leveling. From level 1, use the AA +/− buttons to choose 0–100%; 100% pauses leveling so you can grind AA where you prefer. Close EverQuest and update through launcher Play for game 2026102301. Existing points, purchases and partial progress stay intact. <a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">AA progression and examples</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"multiclass--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear — live testing</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is installed for live testing. Scaling uses 131 researched Legendary items and matching standard EverQuest baselines. Classic level 50 and starter progression are preserved. Reopen the normal launcher for game 2026101902 before testing. See <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open testing limits</a>.</p><p>The AA changes include group Act of Valor, activated 40% Harvest, four percentage-based Mana Burns, universal caster Silent Casting, Warrior attack debuffs, Wizard Pyromancy/Cryomancy and a separate Wizard Dimensional Shielding. Spell Casting Subtlety and obsolete Silent Casting modifiers are retired; recorded purchase costs are refunded once on login. Class ownership, other purchases and starter grants remain intact. Exact uncertain costs and coefficients are listed in the candidate guide.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live AA testing:</strong> All 16 classes have more earned AA options: 75 newly available lines, 111 expanded lines and Druid access to Healing Boon. The latest custom behavior update retires Spell Casting Subtlety and obsolete Silent Casting modifiers, with recorded-cost refunds. Classic remains level 50. Reconnect and turn Recommended AA off to browse your held classes. <a href=\"multiclass.html#all-class-aa\">Read the AA update</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> Reviewed earned pet and melee AA ranks and held-class combat benefits are available for live testing. Normal ownership, costs, prerequisites and skill requirements remain. The active level cap is still 50; the separate Planes of Power profile is not activated.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Pets &amp; pet armor: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"pets--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear — live testing</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is installed for live testing. Scaling uses 131 researched Legendary items and matching standard EverQuest baselines. Classic level 50 and starter progression are preserved. Reopen the normal launcher for game 2026101902 before testing. See <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open testing limits</a>.</p><p>The focus changes apply to players and permanent pets. Temporary pets retain their prior focus behavior. Existing pet/WPM item effects, sockets, equipment rules and access remain intact.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> Permanent pet equipment now has three pages covering 22 locations, with a total budget of 15 items for Mage pets or eight for other permanent class pets. Update through the launcher before opening Equipment.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Travel &amp; instances: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"travel--hole-entrance\">The Hole entrance</h2><p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing — keyless Hole entrance:</strong> The Hole Key and lock-picking requirement have been removed from the entrance rock in Paineel at <code>/loc 568,-896,-96</code>. Click the rock to open the passage without a key or lock picks. The server update is installed; in-game acceptance is pending. Paineel city-lift keys and the Sacred Key doors inside The Hole remain unchanged.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\" id=\"travel--hate-commonlands-candidate\"><strong>Live testing — Hate Keeper in Commonlands:</strong> Find the Plane of Hate Keeper in East Commonlands at <code>/loc -1570,-346,3</code>, between Mirielle and Khalure in the travel area. Raid, Grind and return entry lead to Hate; private Hate instances retain an entrance Keeper. Public and private Hate entry require level 46; GM status is no longer required. The server update is installed. The owner confirmed the relocation, Commonlands visibility and Hate travel. Broader dungeon balance and full-clear QA remain separate.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> The <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> give every dungeon three exclusive designs. The 14 added dungeons contribute 42 designs in two qualities; all 414 dungeon rewards are MAGIC. Fear, Hate and Sky receive lore-driven relics and equipped utility clicks. Gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#classic-candidate\">Every Classic dungeon coverage</a> adds the same Raid/Grind choices in 21 combat dungeon zones, including Fear, Hate and Sky. All 21 are installed for live testing; gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Not released:</strong> The separate level-65/Planes of Power profile and its additional merchant stock remain staged. This item/spell release keeps Classic level 50 and the current travel and vendor gates.</p>\n<h2 id=\"travel--missing-zone-files\">If a Classic destination fails to load</h2><p>Close EverQuest and use launcher Play to install game update 2026101801 or newer. The patcher now checks and repairs terrain/object archives for 17 Classic travel destinations, including West Commonlands, Misty Thicket and Toxxulia. Confirm the launcher points to the folder you use. If your character is stuck, contact the owner for a location rescue; retain the exact error if updating does not resolve it. Native travel acceptance is still being checked.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>East Commonlands tunnel: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"tunnel--experience-blessing\">XP blessing retired</h2><p>Magus Goldwind no longer charges platinum or grants the XP package. Speak with Matron Restora for free ordinary buffs. Existing timed XP boosts keep their remaining duration; old nonexpiring copies receive a minimal countdown on login or zoning and fade when buff timers run. Replacement ways to earn boosts are under consideration and are not available yet.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>In development: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p class=\"notice\" id=\"unreleased--hate-commonlands-candidate\"><strong>Live testing — Hate Keeper in Commonlands:</strong> Find the Plane of Hate Keeper in East Commonlands at <code>/loc -1570,-346,3</code>, between Mirielle and Khalure in the travel area. Raid, Grind and return entry lead to Hate; private Hate instances retain an entrance Keeper. Public and private Hate entry require level 46; GM status is no longer required. The server update is installed. The owner confirmed the relocation, Commonlands visibility and Hate travel. Broader dungeon balance and full-clear QA remain separate.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> The <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> give every dungeon three exclusive designs. The 14 added dungeons contribute 42 designs in two qualities; all 414 dungeon rewards are MAGIC. Fear, Hate and Sky receive lore-driven relics and equipped utility clicks. Gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#classic-candidate\">Every Classic dungeon coverage</a> adds the same Raid/Grind choices in 21 combat dungeon zones, including Fear, Hate and Sky. All 21 are installed for live testing; gameplay and balance acceptance remain pending.</p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--quest-ingredients\">Quest ingredient qualities - live testing</h2><p>The fix for rejection of Aviak Charm (Polished) is deployed. Shared quest hand-ins and task delivery accept ordinary higher-quality variants for Normal requirements. Check completion, missing inputs and returned extras in game; <a href=\"equipment.html#quest-ingredients\">explicit-quality and forging rules remain separate</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--crystal-markers\">Waypoint crystals — live testing</h2><p>Waypoints now have a glowing crystal with the existing <strong>a waypoint</strong> label. Fully close EverQuest, then use the normal launcher’s Play button to install game 2026102202 before testing. The crystal adds a model to the portal effect; appearance in Classic and Modern model modes and with particles low or off still needs in-game checks. Locations, discovery progress and return destinations are unchanged.</p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--classic-robes\">Classic robe waist correction — live testing</h2><p>Game update 2026102204 repairs the native waist binding after the earlier 2026102203 repair failed on Barbarian and Half Elf. It covers the added robe bodies for Half Elf, Wood Elf, Barbarian, Dwarf, Troll, Ogre and Halfling models, both genders. Close the game and update through the normal launcher before testing. Native visual, dye and animation acceptance remains open. Item power, class eligibility and progression remain unchanged. <a href=\"equipment.html#classic-robes\">Update details</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--befallen-keeper\">Dungeon Keeper visibility — live testing</h2><p>The placement correction now covers all five confirmed waypoint overlaps: Befallen, Unrest, Najena, Permafrost and Nagafen’s Lair. High Keep and Cazic-Thule retain their already-separate positions. All seven still need visible-model and direct-selection checks. See the <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Keeper locations</a>; use <code>/target Instance_Keeper</code> and hail if needed. No client update or dungeon reset is required.</p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear — live testing</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is installed for live testing. Scaling uses 131 researched Legendary items and matching standard EverQuest baselines. Classic level 50 and starter progression are preserved. Reopen the normal launcher for game 2026101902 before testing. See <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open testing limits</a>.</p><h3>Custom AA behavior</h3><ul><li>Warlord’s Fury: +100% physical skill damage for up to 12 seconds, 60-second reuse.</li><li>Gut Punch: initial damage and +50% physical damage taken for up to 12 seconds. Press the Attack lowers AC; Grappling Strike lowers evasion. Their unverified opening/debuff values remain explicit tuning choices.</li><li>Act of Valor: spends 50% of maximum mana once and heals nearby group members for 2 HP per mana spent.</li><li>Harvest: activate to restore 40% maximum mana.</li><li>Mana Burn/Blast/Blaze/Volatile Mana Blaze: spend 10/20/30/40% maximum mana; retain 4 damage per mana as a tuning choice. All reach 15-minute reuse with full Hastened Manaburn. Target immunity rejects the cast without mana or cooldown loss.</li><li>Silent Casting: all casting classes, one-hour duration, 60-second reuse, suspendable timer. Subtlety and obsolete haste/duration modifiers refund purchased ranks.</li><li>Dimensional Shielding: separate Wizard AA protecting casting from hits, movement and hostile interrupt effects. Stuns and voluntary cancellation still interrupt. Its 120-second duration and 30-minute reuse are retained-value tuning choices.</li><li>Pyromancy/Cryomancy: 35% proc chance, initial damage plus DoT, opposite-element resistance reduction and compatibility with other buffs. Existing level/mana/trigger restrictions remain.</li></ul><h3>Evidence and testing limits</h3><p>Released THJ notes take precedence over older test notes. “Most” static focuses, endpoint selection, the 10× interpretation and the supported area-target scope require validation. The stock baseline is ProjectEQ, not a recovered THJ or Daybreak database. Five weapon observations support the weapon extrapolation. No level-65 profile, new loot access, automatic AA points or free gear is included. In-game checks must cover mana failures, group healing, refund persistence, song focusing, actual hit damage and gear inspection before gameplay balance is accepted.</p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--all-class-aa\">All-class AAs are now in live testing</h2><p>The rank and access update is installed. See <a href=\"multiclass.html#all-class-aa\">the released AA rules</a>. Additional custom THJ effects are now installed as described above; encounter balance remains open.</p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--thj-parity\">Item and spell scaling is now in live testing</h2><p>The combined release is installed. Read <a href=\"equipment.html\">Equipment</a>, <a href=\"combat.html\">Combat</a> and <a href=\"pets.html\">Pets</a> for its current rules. Historical THJ evidence does not establish every current THJ formula; spell-rank choice, mana sustain, pet contribution and maximum-AA melee burst still need in-game balance checks.</p><h2 id=\"unreleased--wpm-melee\">Shield and melee changes are now in live testing</h2><p>The earned held-class melee and shield changes shipped with the combined release. See <a href=\"combat.html#melee-builds\">the combat guide</a>. Gameplay acceptance remains open.</p><h2 id=\"unreleased--pet-scaling\">Separate level-65 and Planes of Power profile — not released</h2><p>The expanded pet equipment and scaling changes are installed, but the level-65/Planes of Power profile and 389 additional merchant entries are still staged. Classic level 50 remains active. Nothing grants levels, spellbooks, AA points or epics automatically. Manifest Elements keeps its normal Mage level 59 requirement.</p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--quest-quality\">Guaranteed quality for substantial class armor — live testing</h2><p>The installed update grants existing Ascended versions of 37 Crafted, Lambent, Darkforge, Ivy Etched and Totemic quest rewards. Substantial class-armor quests may qualify even when repeatable; cheap/basic hand-ins remain excluded. All original materials, money checks, faction and experience remain. The dependent Shadow Knight epic turn-in accepts Normal or Ascended Darkforge pieces, including mixed sets.</p><p>The 37 reviewed rewards are live. Already-owned items are not automatically converted. Other armor quests require individual review: Armor of Ro finishes through tradeskills, and Temple cleric branches need a separate audit. Materials, returned items, starter gear, spells, epic rewards and unaudited quests are not globally upgraded. Gameplay and progression balance still need in-game testing.</p><h2 id=\"unreleased--cooldown-identities\">Remaining shared skill and spell cooldowns</h2><p>The <a href=\"combat.html#ability-cooldowns\">AA and cross-ability timer correction is deployed for live testing</a>. Content-defined groups, including Harmshield/Cannibalize and Battle Cry/Throw Stone, remain open work. Bash/Slam, Backstab, Frenzy and non-Monk Kick still share a basic attack timer; Begging and Pick Pockets also share reuse. Linked potion/item groups remain. These links are under review; they are not included in the independence correction.</p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--journal\">Adventure Journal &amp; Epic 0.5</h2><p>The eight journal quests and Wayfarer’s Oath charm have been built but are <strong>not installed on the server</strong>. The update uses three shared chapters followed by Guardian, Striker, Arcanist, Warden or Binder paths. These are not available rewards.</p><h2 id=\"unreleased--combat\">Combat and item candidates</h2><p>Broader Monk and Beastlord fist-damage formulas and some existing tiered item corrections have a tested candidate but no recorded deployment. A frozen personal casting bar remains under investigation. The separate <a href=\"multiclass.html#earned-skills\">extra-class skill, trainer and offhand correction</a> is deployed; the reported player issue was confirmed resolved.</p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--testing\">Ongoing checks for deployed features</h2><p>Broader equipment and class combinations, stats, regeneration, ability names and Bard movement/songs still need player checks. Those are acceptance checks for installed systems, not a claim that all of them are unreleased. See <a href=\"features.html\">Features</a> for the available systems.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--chapterhouse-candidate\">The Vigil of the Dawn — live testing</h2><p>The Vigil of the Dawn has moved into live testing. Combat, travel and recovery still require player acceptance; installation is not completed gameplay validation. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> and <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a>.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Waypoint Explorer: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"waypoints--crystal-markers\">Waypoint crystals — live testing</h2><p>Waypoints now have a glowing crystal with the existing <strong>a waypoint</strong> label. Fully close EverQuest, then use the normal launcher’s Play button to install game 2026102202 before testing. The crystal adds a model to the portal effect; appearance in Classic and Modern model modes and with particles low or off still needs in-game checks. Locations, discovery progress and return destinations are unchanged.</p>\n</div></details>\n\n<h2 id=\"paladin-weapon-grip-20261026\">October 26, 2026 — Paladin weapon grips</h2><p><strong>Live testing:</strong> a right-click 1HS/2HS toggle is available for SoulFire, Fiery Avenger and Fiery Defender, including existing quality variants. SoulFire’s Complete Heal click is replaced by the toggle. Native gameplay acceptance remains pending. <a href=\"equipment.html#paladin-weapon-grip\">Grip instructions</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"paladin-grip-repair-20261027\">October27 grip issue and October28 paired repair</h2><p>SoulFire could report 1HS while the client retained a two-handed definition. The paired October28 release supplies the cache repair, assessed weapon stats and direct Ascended rewards for SoulFire, Fiery Avenger and Fiery Defender. The Paladin epic no longer requires essence or platinum, and existing normal Defenders have a free exchange. Other epic recipes and Monk AAs are unchanged. Fully exit EQ and use launcher Play to install release2026102801. Native player acceptance remains open. <a href=\"equipment.html#paladin-weapon-grip\">Stats and grip instructions</a>.</p><h2 id=\"bazaar-ui-repair-20261028\">October28 — missing Bazaar controls</h2><p>The update also corrects a Bazaar XML parsing error that made the entire Nightcap interface fall back to Default. Close EQ completely and update through the launcher. If the character still uses Default afterward, enter <code>/loadskin nightcap 1</code>. Check the Bazaar Sell / My Listings and Advanced Loot controls; visible acceptance remains open.</p>\n<h2 id=\"bazaar-startup-crash-20261028\">October 28: Bazaar startup crash — client hotfix 2026102802</h2><p>Client hotfix 2026102802 corrects missing Bazaar tab borders that caused a crash during world entry. Fully exit EverQuest, reopen the launcher and press Play to update, then retry login and /bazaar. The SoulFire repair remains included. Native login and Bazaar acceptance checks remain open.</p>\n<h2 id=\"hate-layout-20261029\">October 29: Plane of Hate ground-level layout — live testing</h2><p>New Raid and Grind runs from the East Commonlands Keeper now use the newer Hate layout, with Nightcap’s existing encounters, NPC strength, loot, epic items, Hunt drops, experience and completion rewards preserved. Existing unexpired runs remain usable in the original layout. Fully exit EverQuest and update through launcher Play before entering. Player rendering, pathing and balance checks remain open. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#hate-layout-preview\">Entry, landmarks and testing</a>.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"keyless-doors-20261029\">October 29: keyless doors — live testing</h2><p>Keys and lock picks are no longer required for ordinary locked doors throughout existing door content. The update covers 194 doors across 48 zones, including Paineel’s city lift, internal Hole doors, Befallen locks and Plane of Sky transports. Other access rules, items, keyrings and earned progression remain. No client update is required. <a href=\"travel.html#keyless-doors\">Door access and remaining restrictions</a>.</p>\n\n\n<h2 id=\"cast-bar-repair-20261030\">October 30: spell casting bar timing — reported issue resolved</h2><p>Client update <strong>2026103002</strong> corrects casting bars that stayed full until the final instant. Fully exit EverQuest and use launcher Play before testing. Normal server cast times, instant DoTs and Bard timing are unchanged; the Ancient Attunement label repair remains included. The owner confirmed the reported casting-bar issue is fixed. This does not claim completion of every focus or interruption check. <a href=\"launcher.html#cast-bar-repair\">Update instructions</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"hate-boss-placement-20261030\">October 30: Hate boss landmark correction — live testing</h2><p>Corrected the ground-level substitute locations for Maestro, the Hand and Innoruuk to their organ/platform/throne landmarks. Existing saved boss positions move once while preserving health, loot, corpses, kills and respawn timers. The 47 added ordinary spawns and all encounter rewards remain. No client update or run reset is required. Visible gameplay acceptance remains open.</p>\n",
