-  "body": "<p>These projects are not yet available, or have a specific unresolved boundary. Installed systems and their instructions are in <a href=\"features.html\">Features</a> and <a href=\"all-pages.html\">Guides</a>; deployment history is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html\">Change Log</a>.</p><h2 id=\"ashen-compact\">The Ashen Compact — live testing</h2><p><a href=\"ashen-compact.html\">The Ashen Compact</a> is an installed level-50 Shadow Knight helmet campaign in a curated Kael expedition. Its paired server and client release is available for testing; full encounter, rendering and balance acceptance remain open.</p><h2 id=\"pet-scaling\">Separate level-65 and Planes of Power profile — not released</h2><p>The expanded pet equipment and scaling changes are installed, but the level-65/Planes of Power profile and 389 additional merchant entries are still staged. Classic level 50 remains active. Nothing grants levels, spellbooks, AA points or epics automatically. Manifest Elements keeps its normal Mage level 59 requirement.</p>\n<h2 id=\"cooldown-identities\">Remaining shared skill and spell cooldowns</h2><p>The <a href=\"combat.html#ability-cooldowns\">AA and cross-ability timer correction is deployed for live testing</a>. Content-defined groups, including Harmshield/Cannibalize and Battle Cry/Throw Stone, remain open work. Bash/Slam, Backstab, Frenzy and non-Monk Kick still share a basic attack timer; Begging and Pick Pockets also share reuse. Linked potion/item groups remain. These links are under review; they are not included in the independence correction.</p>\n<h2 id=\"journal\">Adventure Journal &amp; Epic 0.5</h2><p>The eight journal quests and Wayfarer’s Oath charm have been built but are <strong>not installed on the server</strong>. The update uses three shared chapters followed by Guardian, Striker, Arcanist, Warden or Binder paths. These are not available rewards.</p><h2 id=\"combat\">Combat and item candidates</h2><p>Broader Monk and Beastlord fist-damage formulas and some existing tiered item corrections have a tested candidate but no recorded deployment. A frozen personal casting bar remains under investigation. The separate <a href=\"multiclass.html#earned-skills\">extra-class skill, trainer and offhand correction</a> is deployed; the reported player issue was confirmed resolved.</p>\n<h2 id=\"testing\">Ongoing checks for deployed features</h2><p>Broader equipment and class combinations, stats, regeneration, ability names and Bard movement/songs still need player checks. Those are acceptance checks for installed systems, not a claim that all of them are unreleased. See <a href=\"features.html\">Features</a> for the available systems.</p>\n\n<aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"hate-commonlands-candidate\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#unreleased--hate-commonlands-candidate\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"quest-ingredients\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#unreleased--quest-ingredients\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"crystal-markers\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#unreleased--crystal-markers\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"classic-robes\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#unreleased--classic-robes\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"befallen-keeper\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#unreleased--befallen-keeper\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"thj-behavior-candidate\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#unreleased--thj-behavior-candidate\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"all-class-aa\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#unreleased--all-class-aa\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"thj-parity\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#unreleased--thj-parity\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"wpm-melee\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#unreleased--wpm-melee\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"quest-quality\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#unreleased--quest-quality\">Change Log →</a></p></aside><aside class=\"archived-update\" id=\"chapterhouse-candidate\"><p>This update is in <a href=\"recent-changes.html#unreleased--chapterhouse-candidate\">Change Log →</a></p></aside>\n<h2 id=\"player-bazaar\">Commonlands player bazaar — live testing</h2><p>Native search, fixed-price listings, offline seller proceeds and cancellation are installed. Actual RoF2 search, inspection, direct delivery and complete seller/buyer checks remain open. No auctioneer character needs to remain online. <a href=\"tunnel.html#player-bazaar\">Market guide and restrictions</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"paladin-weapon-grip\">Paladin weapon repair — live testing</h2><p>The paired October28 release installs the grip-definition repair, assessed stats and direct Ascended rewards for all three sword quests. Fiery Defender no longer needs the extra payment step; existing normal Defenders have a free exchange. Monk AAs are unchanged. Player checks for shield use, visible swings, quest exchange and persistence remain open. <a href=\"equipment.html#paladin-weapon-grip\">Current grip behavior and restrictions</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"hate-layout-preview\">Plane of Hate layout — live testing</h2><p>The paired Hate server and client update is installed for testing. New Keeper runs use ground-level routes while existing runs remain in the original layout. Nightcap encounters, loot and earned rewards are preserved. Rendering, routes, pulls and full-run acceptance remain open. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#hate-layout-preview\">Current entry and testing guide</a>.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"keyless-doors\">Keyless doors — live testing</h2><p>The removal of ordinary door key and lock-picking requirements is installed. Guild, scripted and zone/instance access rules remain. <a href=\"travel.html#keyless-doors\">Scope and instructions</a>; native player checks remain open.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"public-cazic-thule\">Public Cazic-Thule — live testing</h2><p>The Classic population is restored for ordinary travel through Khaleid. Player checks for rendering, patrols, loot and unchanged private runs remain open. <a href=\"travel.html#cazic-thule\">Entry and encounter rules</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"faction-standings\">Faction standings — live testing</h2><p>The deployed <code>#factions</code> command adds white-text standings, bars, search and paging. Native readability and in-game acceptance remain open. <a href=\"commands.html#faction-standings\">Command instructions</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"power-source-training\">Power Source training — Not released</h2><p>A candidate adds item advancement through combat XP, alongside the Reforging Box. The proposed 4–8-hour full path needs timed gameplay and client verification before release. <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#power-source-training\">Power Source training preview</a>.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\" id=\"augment-audit-preview\"><strong>Not released:</strong> the <a href=\"augment-audit.html\">November 6 augment audit preview</a> lists all top-quality augments and proposed guard-wide drops, specialty bonuses and exotic icons. Current live behavior remains until a verified release.</p>",
