   "title": "Zone hunt & forging",
   "summary": "Find new rewards, socket heroic augments and forge the next quality.",
-  "body": "<p class=\"notice\"><strong>Live testing:</strong> The base Spell Damage and Healing Amount caps are now 750. Earned Hunt headroom remains additive. Hunt rewards, drop chances, tasks and forging costs are unchanged.</p>\n<p>Fifty Classic zones offer an augment family; the original48 also retain their equipment families. Cazic-Thule and the newer Hate layout add augment-only pools. Live testing. Browse the <a href=\"zones.html\">zone directory</a> or <a href=\"items.html\">item index</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"drops\">How drops work</h2><p>Each eligible native enemy has two independent rolls: <strong>1.5% for its zone augment</strong> and <strong>0.5% for its zone equipment</strong> by default; each zone page lists its exact rates. Both may drop together. Ordinary loot remains. At the defaults an augment averages one per about 67 eligible kills and equipment one per 200, with no guarantee or pity counter.</p><table><caption>Quality after a successful family roll</caption><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Quality</th><th scope=\"col\">Chance</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Base</td><td>60%</td></tr><tr><td>Polished</td><td>30%</td></tr><tr><td>Exalted</td><td>8%</td></tr><tr><td>Ascension</td><td>2%</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Any unowned, killable NPC in an enabled augment zone can roll its augment, including guards, named and quest NPCs, killable merchants and scripted combat adds. Player-owned/charmed pets, mercenaries, swarm pets, protected noncombat actors and restored corpses do not reroll. Native corpse ownership and encounter access still apply. Augments roll at 1.5%; approved native equipment sources keep their separate 0.5% chance and level/night restrictions.</p>\n<h2 id=\"sockets\">Sockets &amp; heroic stats</h2><p>Eligible head, arms, hands, chest, legs and feet armor has a type-22 socket for these augments. Existing sockets remain. Required levels and compatibility still apply.</p><p>At level 50, every two effective heroic INT from these socketed augments adds one point to the item Spell Damage cap, up to +30. Heroic WIS does the same for Healing Amount. With the current base cap of 750, either can reach 780. Increasing a cap does not grant the underlying bonus; you still need enough actual Spell Damage or Healing Amount equipped.</p>\n<h2 id=\"forging\">Forge matching rewards into the next quality</h2><ol><li>Carry three identical Base rewards, or four identical Polished or Exalted rewards, unequipped and unmodified.</li><li>Leave combat, empty your cursor, and close loot, trade and merchant windows.</li><li>Type <code>#zoneforge</code> and choose the named upgrade.</li></ol><p><strong>3 Base → 1 Polished; 4 Polished → 1 Exalted; 4 Exalted → 1 Ascension.</strong> There is no fee or random failure. Different zones and qualities cannot mix. An item's built-in color is allowed; a different player-applied dye color is not. Socketed, player-dyed, ornamented, customized or evolving items cannot be inputs. Ascension is the final quality.</p><p>For Polished and Exalted rewards, Artisan Veyra’s <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#box\">Reforging Box</a> offers the same four-copy upgrades. The box also supports eligible ordinary tiered gear. The box also accepts <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#normal-items\">three identical Base copies for Polished</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"trade\">Trading &amp; resale</h2><p>These rewards can be traded between players but have <strong>no merchant resale value</strong>. If an upgrade result is unclear or items appear missing, stop retrying and tell the owner what happened.</p>\n<h2 id=\"chapterhouse-candidate\">The Vigil of the Dawn — live testing</h2><p>Chapterhouse adds Ember of the First Dawn, a level-50 type-22 armor augment with four qualities and a healing specialty. Any unowned killable enemy, including scripted combat adds, has a 1.5% family roll. Existing Hunt headroom/forging and static-only35% miniboss relic rolls remain. <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">Published rewards</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"ashen-compact\">The Ashen Compact — live testing</h2><p><a href=\"ashen-compact.html\">The Ashen Compact</a> is an installed level-50 Shadow Knight helmet campaign in a curated Kael expedition. Its paired server and client release is available for testing; full encounter, rendering and balance acceptance remain open.</p><p>Cinder of the Ashen Compact is a separate type-22 STA/INT family with mana-preservation focus at higher qualities. Its managed expedition uses a1.5% family roll from any unowned killable enemy, including scripted adds, with60/30/8/2quality weights.</p>\n<h2 id=\"hate-layout\">Hate rewards across both layouts</h2><p>The new private Hate layout uses the original Plane of Hate Hunt family, approved enemy list and drop chances. The catalog’s <a href=\"zone-hateplane.html\">hateplane rewards</a> apply to both layouts; this update does not add a second Hunt family or change forging. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#hate-layout-preview\">Dungeon entry and testing</a>.</p><p><a href=\"augment-audit.html\">All top-quality augments, drop zones and secondary specialties</a> — live testing; gameplay acceptance remains open.</p>\n<h2 id=\"power-source-training\">Power Source training — Not released</h2><p>The candidate lets a supported Hunt reward earn combat XP from Base through Ascension in the Power Source slot. Drop rates, augment compatibility and forging recipes remain. <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#power-source-training\">Power Source training preview</a>.</p>\n",
